      "cml:conclusionText": "Ensure conference agreements meet minimum standards."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-108",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 01A  Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-108"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThis Part sets up a system for regulating international liner\ncargo shipping services.\n•\nThe main components of that system are as follows:\n\n(a)\nregistration of conference agreements;\n\n(b)\nregulation of non-conference ocean carriers with\nsubstantial market power;\n\n(c)\nregulation of unfair pricing practices;\n\n(d)\nregistration of agents of ocean carriers.\n•\nThe parties to a conference agreement relating to international\nliner cargo shipping services may apply for the registration of\nthe agreement.\n•\nIf the conference agreement is registered, the parties will be\ngiven partial and conditional exemptions from:\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 10.02\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a)\nsections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK (cartel conduct);\nand\n\n(b)\nsection 45 (contracts etc. that restrict dealings or affect\ncompetition); and\n\n(c)\nsection 47 (exclusive dealing).\n•\nThe parties to a registered conference agreement are required\nto negotiate with, and provide information to, representative\nshipper bodies.\n•\nThe Commission may investigate whether grounds exist for\nthe Minister to deregister a conference agreement.\n•\nThe main ground for deregistration is a breach by the parties\nto the agreement of requirements imposed on them by this\nPart.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThis Part sets up a system for regulating international liner\ncargo shipping services.\n•\nThe main components of that system are as follows:\n\n(a)\nregistration of conference agreements;\n\n(b)\nregulation of non-conference ocean carriers with\nsubstantial market power;\n\n(c)\nregulation of unfair pricing practices;\n\n(d)\nregistration of agents of ocean carriers.\n•\nThe parties to a conference agreement relating to international\nliner cargo shipping services may apply for the registration of\nthe agreement.\n•\nIf the conference agreement is registered, the parties will be\ngiven partial and conditional exemptions from:\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 10.02\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a)\nsections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK (cartel conduct);\nand\n\n(b)\nsection 45 (contracts etc. that restrict dealings or affect\ncompetition); and\n\n(c)\nsection 47 (exclusive dealing).\n•\nThe parties to a registered conference agreement are required\nto negotiate with, and provide information to, representative\nshipper bodies.\n•\nThe Commission may investigate whether grounds exist for\nthe Minister to deregister a conference agreement.\n•\nThe main ground for deregistration is a breach by the parties\nto the agreement of requirements imposed on them by this\nPart.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-108-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-108-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-108-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-108-logic-linearlogic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab12de95612ad428eed12afb86c91f7cfd0603e36e5ccc88bdb89d99e93df19e",
      "skos:note": "Registration of conference agreements and exemptions from other provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-108",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 01A  Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThis Part sets up a system for regulating international liner\ncargo shipping services.\n•\nThe main components of that system are as follows:\n\n(a)\nregistration of conference agreements;\n\n(b)\nregulation of non-conference ocean carriers with\nsubstantial market power;\n\n(c)\nregulation of unfair pricing practices;\n\n(d)\nregistration of agents of ocean carriers.\n•\nThe parties to a conference agreement relating to international\nliner cargo shipping services may apply for the registration of\nthe agreement.\n•\nIf the conference agreement is registered, the parties will be\ngiven partial and conditional exemptions from:\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 10.02\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a)\nsections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ and 45AK (cartel conduct);\nand\n\n(b)\nsection 45 (contracts etc. that restrict dealings or affect\ncompetition); and\n\n(c)\nsection 47 (exclusive dealing).\n•\nThe parties to a registered conference agreement are required\nto negotiate with, and provide information to, representative\nshipper bodies.\n•\nThe Commission may investigate whether grounds exist for\nthe Minister to deregister a conference agreement.\n•\nThe main ground for deregistration is a breach by the parties\nto the agreement of requirements imposed on them by this\nPart."
    },
