    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-112",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 04  Application of section 46 in relation to conference agreements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-112"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of section 46, if the parties to a conference\nagreement together have a substantial degree of power in a market\nin which any party to the agreement provides international liner\ncargo shipping services under the agreement, each party to the\nconference agreement shall be taken to have a substantial degree of\npower in the market.\n\n(2) In subsection (1):\nconference agreement means an agreement between members of a\nconference in relation to international liner cargo shipping services\nprovided, or proposed to be provided, by them, and includes an\nagreement that varies such an agreement.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nMinimum standards for conference agreements  Division 3\n\nSection 10.06\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of section 46, if the parties to a conference\nagreement together have a substantial degree of power in a market\nin which any party to the agreement provides international liner\ncargo shipping services under the agreement, each party to the\nconference agreement shall be taken to have a substantial degree of\npower in the market.\n\n(2) In subsection (1):\nconference agreement means an agreement between members of a\nconference in relation to international liner cargo shipping services\nprovided, or proposed to be provided, by them, and includes an\nagreement that varies such an agreement.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nMinimum standards for conference agreements  Division 3\n\nSection 10.06\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-112-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-112-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0fc5e894449c7fba505f16785a21f0524d433d8e11ddc5516d6b47f445aeeea4"
    },
