    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 06  Application of Australian law to outwards conference",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-113"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "agreements and withdrawal from agreements\n\n(1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a\nquestion arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards\nliner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance\nwith Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in\nwriting, to the particular question being otherwise determined.\n\n(2) An outwards conference agreement must expressly permit any\nparty to the agreement to withdraw from the agreement on\nreasonable notice without penalty.",
      "skos:definition": "agreements and withdrawal from agreements\n\n(1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a\nquestion arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards\nliner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance\nwith Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in\nwriting, to the particular question being otherwise determined.\n\n(2) An outwards conference agreement must expressly permit any\nparty to the agreement to withdraw from the agreement on\nreasonable notice without penalty.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b4093b9e2abff35f0885dd658b83aad51b17d692dcad48dec5052703ec39916f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-113",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 06  Application of Australian law to outwards conference",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "agreements and withdrawal from agreements\n\n(1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a\nquestion arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards\nliner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance\nwith Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in\nwriting, to the particular question being otherwise determined.\n\n(2) An outwards conference agreement must expressly permit any\nparty to the agreement to withdraw from the agreement on\nreasonable notice without penalty."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10(1) 06  Application of Australian law to outwards conference",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-113-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a\nquestion arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards\nliner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance\nwith Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in\nwriting, to the particular question being otherwise determined.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a\nquestion arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards\nliner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance\nwith Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in\nwriting, to the particular question being otherwise determined.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "345563173088b3005e63ef56ce4382c0a7baadb01cf3adc56b29b642df947f5a",
      "skos:note": "Parties must agree in writing to deviate from Australian law for outwards conference agreements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-113-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10(1) 06  Application of Australian law to outwards conference",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a\nquestion arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards\nliner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance\nwith Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in\nwriting, to the particular question being otherwise determined."
    },
