    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-119",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 12  What conference agreement files are to be kept by the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-119"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "Registrar?\n\n(1) The Registrar shall keep a file, to be known as the conference\nagreement file, for each conference agreement (other than a\nvarying conference agreement).\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nRegisters and files and public inspection of them  Division 4\n\nSection 10.13\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) The conference agreement file for a conference agreement must\ninclude:\n\n(a) documents filed with the Registrar under Division 6 in\nrelation to the agreement or any relevant varying conference\nagreement (other than any part of a document that is not open\nto public inspection);\n\n(b) abstracts accepted by the Registrar under section 10.36 in\nrelation to such documents (being abstracts of those parts of\nthe documents that are not open to public inspection); and\n\n(c) notifications given to the Registrar under subsection 10.40(1)\nor 10.43(1) in relation to the agreement or any relevant\nvarying conference agreement.",
      "skos:definition": "Registrar?\n\n(1) The Registrar shall keep a file, to be known as the conference\nagreement file, for each conference agreement (other than a\nvarying conference agreement).\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nRegisters and files and public inspection of them  Division 4\n\nSection 10.13\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) The conference agreement file for a conference agreement must\ninclude:\n\n(a) documents filed with the Registrar under Division 6 in\nrelation to the agreement or any relevant varying conference\nagreement (other than any part of a document that is not open\nto public inspection);\n\n(b) abstracts accepted by the Registrar under section 10.36 in\nrelation to such documents (being abstracts of those parts of\nthe documents that are not open to public inspection); and\n\n(c) notifications given to the Registrar under subsection 10.40(1)\nor 10.43(1) in relation to the agreement or any relevant\nvarying conference agreement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-119-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-119-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2b805130249500cac20c42351da000c6f4b41b05e3f0a7b2cf0f71cf76cb9305"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-119",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 12  What conference agreement files are to be kept by the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "Registrar?\n\n(1) The Registrar shall keep a file, to be known as the conference\nagreement file, for each conference agreement (other than a\nvarying conference agreement).\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nRegisters and files and public inspection of them  Division 4\n\nSection 10.13\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) The conference agreement file for a conference agreement must\ninclude:\n\n(a) documents filed with the Registrar under Division 6 in\nrelation to the agreement or any relevant varying conference\nagreement (other than any part of a document that is not open\nto public inspection);\n\n(b) abstracts accepted by the Registrar under section 10.36 in\nrelation to such documents (being abstracts of those parts of\nthe documents that are not open to public inspection); and\n\n(c) notifications given to the Registrar under subsection 10.40(1)\nor 10.43(1) in relation to the agreement or any relevant\nvarying conference agreement."
    },
