    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 14  Exemptions apply only to certain activities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-121"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the exemptions provided by this\nSubdivision apply only in relation to the following parts of an\noutwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo\nshipping service:\n\n(a) the parts of the service that consist of the transport of the\ncargo by sea;\n\n(b) stevedoring services;\n\n(c) activities that take place outside Australia.\n\n(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the fixing\nof charges for an inter-terminal transport service where the service\nis part of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards\nliner cargo shipping service.\n\n(3) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the\ndetermination of common terms and conditions for bills of lading\nfor use in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an\ninwards liner cargo shipping service.\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision do\nnot extend to any dealings between the parties to a conference\nagreement and a person who provides ancillary services on behalf\nof the provider of a scheduled cargo shipping service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this section, the exemptions provided by this\nSubdivision apply only in relation to the following parts of an\noutwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo\nshipping service:\n\n(a) the parts of the service that consist of the transport of the\ncargo by sea;\n\n(b) stevedoring services;\n\n(c) activities that take place outside Australia.\n\n(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the fixing\nof charges for an inter-terminal transport service where the service\nis part of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards\nliner cargo shipping service.\n\n(3) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the\ndetermination of common terms and conditions for bills of lading\nfor use in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an\ninwards liner cargo shipping service.\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision do\nnot extend to any dealings between the parties to a conference\nagreement and a person who provides ancillary services on behalf\nof the provider of a scheduled cargo shipping service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a20071a7df2b00bf222e0e73c9db51ea769a1042c7e09987c8c1f9bdc5702fc4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-121",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 14  Exemptions apply only to certain activities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, the exemptions provided by this\nSubdivision apply only in relation to the following parts of an\noutwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo\nshipping service:\n\n(a) the parts of the service that consist of the transport of the\ncargo by sea;\n\n(b) stevedoring services;\n\n(c) activities that take place outside Australia.\n\n(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the fixing\nof charges for an inter-terminal transport service where the service\nis part of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards\nliner cargo shipping service.\n\n(3) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the\ndetermination of common terms and conditions for bills of lading\nfor use in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an\ninwards liner cargo shipping service.\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision do\nnot extend to any dealings between the parties to a conference\nagreement and a person who provides ancillary services on behalf\nof the provider of a scheduled cargo shipping service."
    },
