    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 15  When do exemptions commence to apply in relation to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-122"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "registered conference agreements?\n\n(1) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nExemptions from certain restrictive trade practice prohibitions  Division 5\n\nSection 10.16\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nregistered outwards conference agreement only after the end of\n30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered.\n\n(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\nregistered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is\nthe later of the following times:\n\n(a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally\nregistered;\n\n(b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping)\nAct 2000.",
      "skos:definition": "registered conference agreements?\n\n(1) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nExemptions from certain restrictive trade practice prohibitions  Division 5\n\nSection 10.16\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nregistered outwards conference agreement only after the end of\n30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered.\n\n(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\nregistered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is\nthe later of the following times:\n\n(a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally\nregistered;\n\n(b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping)\nAct 2000.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb0aee32def195f483ad4f68a1007c359bbfc2d1195305e2a50d2517b34c511e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-122",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 15  When do exemptions commence to apply in relation to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "registered conference agreements?\n\n(1) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nExemptions from certain restrictive trade practice prohibitions  Division 5\n\nSection 10.16\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nregistered outwards conference agreement only after the end of\n30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered.\n\n(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\nregistered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is\nthe later of the following times:\n\n(a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally\nregistered;\n\n(b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping)\nAct 2000."
    },
    {
