    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10(2) 15  When do exemptions commence to apply in relation to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-122-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\nregistered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is\nthe later of the following times:\n\n(a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally\nregistered;\n\n(b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping)\nAct 2000.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\nregistered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is\nthe later of the following times:\n\n(a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally\nregistered;\n\n(b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping)\nAct 2000.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1372f05468b91f4706a6b0a6bc0fc41f9257296c58b52c53c961a925544b9dec",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions commence after later of two times"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-122-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10(2) 15  When do exemptions commence to apply in relation to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than\nsections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a\nregistered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is\nthe later of the following times:\n\n(a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally\nregistered;\n\n(b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping)\nAct 2000."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
