    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-125-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10(4) 17A  Exemptions from sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ, 45AK and 45",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-125-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Sections 45AG, 45AK and 45 do not apply to conduct engaged in\nby a party to a freight rate agreement, so far as the conduct gives\neffect to freight rate charges in the freight rate agreement, if:\n\n(a) the freight rates (including base freight rates, surcharges,\nrebates and allowances) specified in the freight rate\nagreement are for inwards liner cargo shipping services\nprovided under a single registered inwards conference\nagreement after whichever is the later of the following times:\n\n(i) the end of 30 days after the last-mentioned agreement is\nfinally registered;\n\n(ii) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo\nShipping) Act 2000; and\n\n(b) the parties to the freight rate agreement are the same as the\nparties to the registered inwards conference agreement.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Sections 45AG, 45AK and 45 do not apply to conduct engaged in\nby a party to a freight rate agreement, so far as the conduct gives\neffect to freight rate charges in the freight rate agreement, if:\n\n(a) the freight rates (including base freight rates, surcharges,\nrebates and allowances) specified in the freight rate\nagreement are for inwards liner cargo shipping services\nprovided under a single registered inwards conference\nagreement after whichever is the later of the following times:\n\n(i) the end of 30 days after the last-mentioned agreement is\nfinally registered;\n\n(ii) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade\nPractices Amendment (International Liner Cargo\nShipping) Act 2000; and\n\n(b) the parties to the freight rate agreement are the same as the\nparties to the registered inwards conference agreement.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-125"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
