        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4fe2fb634afdca1e69c84e55a38ae3c0c3c3a1937ade9ea315573957398bf8b3",
      "skos:note": "Determine whether to accept an abstract of a part of a document not open to public inspection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-145",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 36  Examination of abstract",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a request is properly made under section 10.34 that a part of a\ndocument not be open to public inspection under this Part;\nand\n\n(b) the request is accompanied by an abstract of the part of the\ndocument;\nthe Registrar shall first determine whether to accept the abstract.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
