      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where the parties to a conference agreement give a notice under\nsubsection (1), the Registrar may make such variations (if any) to\nthe particulars entered in the register of conference agreements in\nrelation to the agreement as the Registrar considers necessary or\ndesirable to take account of the notice.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where the parties to a conference agreement give a notice under\nsubsection (1), the Registrar may make such variations (if any) to\nthe particulars entered in the register of conference agreements in\nrelation to the agreement as the Registrar considers necessary or\ndesirable to take account of the notice.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-149"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
