      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where the parties to a registered conference agreement give a\nnotice under subsection (1), the Registrar may make such\nvariations (if any) to the particulars entered in the register of\nconference agreements in relation to the agreement as the Registrar\nconsiders necessary or desirable to take account of the notice.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where the parties to a registered conference agreement give a\nnotice under subsection (1), the Registrar may make such\nvariations (if any) to the particulars entered in the register of\nconference agreements in relation to the agreement as the Registrar\nconsiders necessary or desirable to take account of the notice.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-152"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
