    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-154",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 45  Circumstances in which Minister may exercise powers in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-154"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "relation to registered conference agreements\n\n(1) The Minister shall not give a direction under subsection 10.44(1) in\nrelation to a registered conference agreement unless:\n\n(a) the Minister is satisfied of one or more of the following\nmatters:\n\n(i) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—that\nthe agreement does not comply with section 10.06\n(application of Australian law to outwards conference\nagreements and withdrawal from agreements);\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "relation to registered conference agreements\n\n(1) The Minister shall not give a direction under subsection 10.44(1) in\nrelation to a registered conference agreement unless:\n\n(a) the Minister is satisfied of one or more of the following\nmatters:\n\n(i) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—that\nthe agreement does not comply with section 10.06\n(application of Australian law to outwards conference\nagreements and withdrawal from agreements);\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-154-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-154-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-154-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "966ae1f3546016b8dde03bcf2b33699b603bb576c7f7abb0bbad610d74d519cd",
      "skos:note": "Minister cannot give direction under subsection 10.44(1) in relation to a registered conference agreement unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-154",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 45  Circumstances in which Minister may exercise powers in",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "relation to registered conference agreements\n\n(1) The Minister shall not give a direction under subsection 10.44(1) in\nrelation to a registered conference agreement unless:\n\n(a) the Minister is satisfied of one or more of the following\nmatters:\n\n(i) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—that\nthe agreement does not comply with section 10.06\n(application of Australian law to outwards conference\nagreements and withdrawal from agreements);\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-154-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-154"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
