    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-157-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10(5) 48  Investigation and report by Commission on own initiative or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-157-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Without limiting subsection (1), each of the following persons shall\nbe taken to be a person affected by the operation of a registered\nconference agreement:\n\n(a) a party to the agreement;\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\n\n(c) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—an\nAustralian flag shipping operator;\n\n(d) a shipper who uses, or may reasonably be expected to need to\nuse, outwards liner cargo shipping services or inwards liner\ncargo shipping services provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement;\n\n(e) an association representing shippers who use, or may\nreasonably be expected to need to use, such services.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Without limiting subsection (1), each of the following persons shall\nbe taken to be a person affected by the operation of a registered\nconference agreement:\n\n(a) a party to the agreement;\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\n\n(c) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—an\nAustralian flag shipping operator;\n\n(d) a shipper who uses, or may reasonably be expected to need to\nuse, outwards liner cargo shipping services or inwards liner\ncargo shipping services provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement;\n\n(e) an association representing shippers who use, or may\nreasonably be expected to need to use, such services.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-157"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-157-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ba8b74cfa95aaf36cc0631977bbe74ebf6600e1be6a78a005de8ed211bec0ce3",
      "skos:note": "List of persons affected by the operation of a registered conference agreement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-157-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10(5) 48  Investigation and report by Commission on own initiative or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Without limiting subsection (1), each of the following persons shall\nbe taken to be a person affected by the operation of a registered\nconference agreement:\n\n(a) a party to the agreement;\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\n\n(c) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—an\nAustralian flag shipping operator;\n\n(d) a shipper who uses, or may reasonably be expected to need to\nuse, outwards liner cargo shipping services or inwards liner\ncargo shipping services provided, or proposed to be provided,\nunder the agreement;\n\n(e) an association representing shippers who use, or may\nreasonably be expected to need to use, such services.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-157-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-157-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 49  Undertakings by parties to registered conference agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-158"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The parties to a registered conference agreement may, at any time,\noffer to give an undertaking to do, or not to do, a specified act or\nthing.\n\n(2) The offer must be:\n\n(a) in the appropriate prescribed form; and\n\n(b) made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations.\n\n(3) If the Minister accepts the offer, the Minister may do one or more\nof the following:\n\n(a) revoke any reference made to the Commission under\nsection 10.47 in relation to the agreement;\n\n(b) direct the Commission, in writing, to cease holding any\ninvestigation being held by it under section 10.48 in relation\nto the agreement;\n\n(c) revoke any direction given under subsection 10.44(1) in\nrelation to the agreement.\n\n(4) If the Minister accepts the offer, the parties shall be taken to have\ngiven the undertaking, and the Registrar shall immediately register\nthe undertaking by entering particulars of it in the register of\nconference agreements.\n\n(5) If the Minister revokes a direction given under subsection 10.44(1),\nthe Registrar shall immediately include in the register a notation to\nthe effect that the direction has been revoked.\n\n(6) On the inclusion of the notation, Subdivision A of Division 5\napplies in relation to the agreement to the extent to which it would\nhave applied but for the entry of the particulars of the direction.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The parties to a registered conference agreement may, at any time,\noffer to give an undertaking to do, or not to do, a specified act or\nthing.\n\n(2) The offer must be:\n\n(a) in the appropriate prescribed form; and\n\n(b) made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations.\n\n(3) If the Minister accepts the offer, the Minister may do one or more\nof the following:\n\n(a) revoke any reference made to the Commission under\nsection 10.47 in relation to the agreement;\n\n(b) direct the Commission, in writing, to cease holding any\ninvestigation being held by it under section 10.48 in relation\nto the agreement;\n\n(c) revoke any direction given under subsection 10.44(1) in\nrelation to the agreement.\n\n(4) If the Minister accepts the offer, the parties shall be taken to have\ngiven the undertaking, and the Registrar shall immediately register\nthe undertaking by entering particulars of it in the register of\nconference agreements.\n\n(5) If the Minister revokes a direction given under subsection 10.44(1),\nthe Registrar shall immediately include in the register a notation to\nthe effect that the direction has been revoked.\n\n(6) On the inclusion of the notation, Subdivision A of Division 5\napplies in relation to the agreement to the extent to which it would\nhave applied but for the entry of the particulars of the direction.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-158-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aafda59e45c5c2febe1320070627427874367e836728d35ded323b6e21ffcfa6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-158",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 49  Undertakings by parties to registered conference agreement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The parties to a registered conference agreement may, at any time,\noffer to give an undertaking to do, or not to do, a specified act or\nthing.\n\n(2) The offer must be:\n\n(a) in the appropriate prescribed form; and\n\n(b) made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations.\n\n(3) If the Minister accepts the offer, the Minister may do one or more\nof the following:\n\n(a) revoke any reference made to the Commission under\nsection 10.47 in relation to the agreement;\n\n(b) direct the Commission, in writing, to cease holding any\ninvestigation being held by it under section 10.48 in relation\nto the agreement;\n\n(c) revoke any direction given under subsection 10.44(1) in\nrelation to the agreement.\n\n(4) If the Minister accepts the offer, the parties shall be taken to have\ngiven the undertaking, and the Registrar shall immediately register\nthe undertaking by entering particulars of it in the register of\nconference agreements.\n\n(5) If the Minister revokes a direction given under subsection 10.44(1),\nthe Registrar shall immediately include in the register a notation to\nthe effect that the direction has been revoked.\n\n(6) On the inclusion of the notation, Subdivision A of Division 5\napplies in relation to the agreement to the extent to which it would\nhave applied but for the entry of the particulars of the direction."
    },
