    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-160",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 50  Investigations by Commission into market power of ocean",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-160"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "carriers\n\n(1) The Minister may refer to the Commission for investigation and\nreport the question whether an ocean carrier has a substantial\ndegree of market power in the provision of outwards liner cargo\nshipping services or inwards liner cargo shipping services on a\ntrade route otherwise than because the ocean carrier is a party to a\nconference agreement.\n\n(2) The Commission shall hold an investigation into the question and\nreport to the Minister.\n\n(3) In its investigation, the Commission shall give special\nconsideration to any matters specified in the reference as matters to\nbe given special consideration by the Commission.",
      "skos:definition": "carriers\n\n(1) The Minister may refer to the Commission for investigation and\nreport the question whether an ocean carrier has a substantial\ndegree of market power in the provision of outwards liner cargo\nshipping services or inwards liner cargo shipping services on a\ntrade route otherwise than because the ocean carrier is a party to a\nconference agreement.\n\n(2) The Commission shall hold an investigation into the question and\nreport to the Minister.\n\n(3) In its investigation, the Commission shall give special\nconsideration to any matters specified in the reference as matters to\nbe given special consideration by the Commission.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-160-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-160-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-160-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "825dcdaf565462e3dd51c9954d879b83729a9af43024bb58f8fa6b2a9d2f9a19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-160",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 50  Investigations by Commission into market power of ocean",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "carriers\n\n(1) The Minister may refer to the Commission for investigation and\nreport the question whether an ocean carrier has a substantial\ndegree of market power in the provision of outwards liner cargo\nshipping services or inwards liner cargo shipping services on a\ntrade route otherwise than because the ocean carrier is a party to a\nconference agreement.\n\n(2) The Commission shall hold an investigation into the question and\nreport to the Minister.\n\n(3) In its investigation, the Commission shall give special\nconsideration to any matters specified in the reference as matters to\nbe given special consideration by the Commission."
    },
