    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-163",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 53  Non-conference ocean carrier with substantial market power",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-163"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "not to hinder Australian flag shipping operators etc.\n\n(1) A registered non-conference ocean carrier with substantial market\npower shall not prevent or hinder an Australian flag shipping\noperator from engaging efficiently in the provision of outwards\nliner cargo shipping services to an extent that is reasonable.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining what is\nreasonable, have regard to:\n\n(a) the national interest; and\n\n(b) the interests of the following:\n\n(i) Australian shippers generally;\n\n(ii) Australian shippers in a particular trade;\n\n(iii) Australian shippers of particular kinds of goods;\n\n(iv) shippers in a particular part of Australia; and\n\n(c) any other relevant matters.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "not to hinder Australian flag shipping operators etc.\n\n(1) A registered non-conference ocean carrier with substantial market\npower shall not prevent or hinder an Australian flag shipping\noperator from engaging efficiently in the provision of outwards\nliner cargo shipping services to an extent that is reasonable.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining what is\nreasonable, have regard to:\n\n(a) the national interest; and\n\n(b) the interests of the following:\n\n(i) Australian shippers generally;\n\n(ii) Australian shippers in a particular trade;\n\n(iii) Australian shippers of particular kinds of goods;\n\n(iv) shippers in a particular part of Australia; and\n\n(c) any other relevant matters.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-163-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-163-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "29091bc4250edc54e69b575c36d46dc8f6d130e189c6a915f5d61cb58a9ecdac"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-163",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 53  Non-conference ocean carrier with substantial market power",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "not to hinder Australian flag shipping operators etc.\n\n(1) A registered non-conference ocean carrier with substantial market\npower shall not prevent or hinder an Australian flag shipping\noperator from engaging efficiently in the provision of outwards\nliner cargo shipping services to an extent that is reasonable.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining what is\nreasonable, have regard to:\n\n(a) the national interest; and\n\n(b) the interests of the following:\n\n(i) Australian shippers generally;\n\n(ii) Australian shippers in a particular trade;\n\n(iii) Australian shippers of particular kinds of goods;\n\n(iv) shippers in a particular part of Australia; and\n\n(c) any other relevant matters.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
