    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-174",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 64  Undertakings not to engage in pricing practices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-174"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An ocean carrier may, at any time, offer to give an undertaking:\n\n(a) not to engage in a pricing practice; and\n\n(b) to give the Registrar such information as the Registrar from\ntime to time requires (verified as the Registrar requires) for\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nUnfair pricing practices  Division 11\n\nSection 10.65\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe purpose of ascertaining whether the ocean carrier is\nengaging in, or has engaged in, the pricing practice.\n\n(2) The offer must be:\n\n(a) in the appropriate prescribed form; and\n\n(b) made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations.\n\n(3) If the Minister accepts the offer, the Minister may do either or both\nof the following:\n\n(a) revoke any reference made to the Commission under\nsubsection 10.63(1) in relation to the ocean carrier;\n\n(b) revoke any order made under subsection 10.61(1) in relation\nto the ocean carrier.\n\n(4) If the Minister accepts the offer, the ocean carrier shall be taken to\nhave given the undertaking, and the Registrar shall immediately\nregister the undertaking by entering particulars of it in the register\nof obligations concerning unfair pricing practices.\n\n(5) If the Minister revokes an order made under subsection 10.61(1),\nthe Registrar shall immediately include in the register a notation to\nthe effect that the order has been revoked.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An ocean carrier may, at any time, offer to give an undertaking:\n\n(a) not to engage in a pricing practice; and\n\n(b) to give the Registrar such information as the Registrar from\ntime to time requires (verified as the Registrar requires) for\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nUnfair pricing practices  Division 11\n\nSection 10.65\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe purpose of ascertaining whether the ocean carrier is\nengaging in, or has engaged in, the pricing practice.\n\n(2) The offer must be:\n\n(a) in the appropriate prescribed form; and\n\n(b) made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations.\n\n(3) If the Minister accepts the offer, the Minister may do either or both\nof the following:\n\n(a) revoke any reference made to the Commission under\nsubsection 10.63(1) in relation to the ocean carrier;\n\n(b) revoke any order made under subsection 10.61(1) in relation\nto the ocean carrier.\n\n(4) If the Minister accepts the offer, the ocean carrier shall be taken to\nhave given the undertaking, and the Registrar shall immediately\nregister the undertaking by entering particulars of it in the register\nof obligations concerning unfair pricing practices.\n\n(5) If the Minister revokes an order made under subsection 10.61(1),\nthe Registrar shall immediately include in the register a notation to\nthe effect that the order has been revoked.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-174-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-174-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-174-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-174-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-174-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6bbfd972705c630dd7f32c2992281275bf546d5ab3c660cfed9cf7ad01a7fc75"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-174",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 64  Undertakings not to engage in pricing practices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An ocean carrier may, at any time, offer to give an undertaking:\n\n(a) not to engage in a pricing practice; and\n\n(b) to give the Registrar such information as the Registrar from\ntime to time requires (verified as the Registrar requires) for\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nUnfair pricing practices  Division 11\n\nSection 10.65\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe purpose of ascertaining whether the ocean carrier is\nengaging in, or has engaged in, the pricing practice.\n\n(2) The offer must be:\n\n(a) in the appropriate prescribed form; and\n\n(b) made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations.\n\n(3) If the Minister accepts the offer, the Minister may do either or both\nof the following:\n\n(a) revoke any reference made to the Commission under\nsubsection 10.63(1) in relation to the ocean carrier;\n\n(b) revoke any order made under subsection 10.61(1) in relation\nto the ocean carrier.\n\n(4) If the Minister accepts the offer, the ocean carrier shall be taken to\nhave given the undertaking, and the Registrar shall immediately\nregister the undertaking by entering particulars of it in the register\nof obligations concerning unfair pricing practices.\n\n(5) If the Minister revokes an order made under subsection 10.61(1),\nthe Registrar shall immediately include in the register a notation to\nthe effect that the order has been revoked."
    },
