    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-179",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 69  Representation of ocean carrier by registered agent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-179"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Everything done by or in relation to an ocean carrier’s registered\nagent in that capacity shall, for the purposes of this Act, be taken to\nbe done by or in relation to the ocean carrier.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a document required or permitted\nto be served on, or given to, an ocean carrier under or for the\npurposes of this Act (including the process of any court) may be\nserved on, or given to, the ocean carrier by serving it on, or giving\nit to, the ocean carrier’s registered agent.\n\n(3) A document that is, under subsection (2), permitted to be served\non, or given to, an ocean carrier’s registered agent may be served\non, or given to, the agent by:\n\n(a) delivering it to the agent personally; or\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nRegistration of ocean carrier agents  Division 12\n\nSection 10.70\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) leaving it at, or sending it by pre-paid post to, the address for\nservice specified in relation to the agent in the register of\nocean carrier agents.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not affect:\n\n(a) the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth, or any\nlaw of a State or Territory, that authorises the service of a\ndocument otherwise than as provided in that subsection; or\n\n(b) the power of a court to authorise service of a document\notherwise than as provided in that subsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Everything done by or in relation to an ocean carrier’s registered\nagent in that capacity shall, for the purposes of this Act, be taken to\nbe done by or in relation to the ocean carrier.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a document required or permitted\nto be served on, or given to, an ocean carrier under or for the\npurposes of this Act (including the process of any court) may be\nserved on, or given to, the ocean carrier by serving it on, or giving\nit to, the ocean carrier’s registered agent.\n\n(3) A document that is, under subsection (2), permitted to be served\non, or given to, an ocean carrier’s registered agent may be served\non, or given to, the agent by:\n\n(a) delivering it to the agent personally; or\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nRegistration of ocean carrier agents  Division 12\n\nSection 10.70\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) leaving it at, or sending it by pre-paid post to, the address for\nservice specified in relation to the agent in the register of\nocean carrier agents.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not affect:\n\n(a) the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth, or any\nlaw of a State or Territory, that authorises the service of a\ndocument otherwise than as provided in that subsection; or\n\n(b) the power of a court to authorise service of a document\notherwise than as provided in that subsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-179-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-179-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-179-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-179-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e2126400b1422a4a6e19154ebfa7455aaacd608ed979f34255d01d5d3d137b7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-179",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 69  Representation of ocean carrier by registered agent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Everything done by or in relation to an ocean carrier’s registered\nagent in that capacity shall, for the purposes of this Act, be taken to\nbe done by or in relation to the ocean carrier.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a document required or permitted\nto be served on, or given to, an ocean carrier under or for the\npurposes of this Act (including the process of any court) may be\nserved on, or given to, the ocean carrier by serving it on, or giving\nit to, the ocean carrier’s registered agent.\n\n(3) A document that is, under subsection (2), permitted to be served\non, or given to, an ocean carrier’s registered agent may be served\non, or given to, the agent by:\n\n(a) delivering it to the agent personally; or\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nRegistration of ocean carrier agents  Division 12\n\nSection 10.70\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) leaving it at, or sending it by pre-paid post to, the address for\nservice specified in relation to the agent in the register of\nocean carrier agents.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not affect:\n\n(a) the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth, or any\nlaw of a State or Territory, that authorises the service of a\ndocument otherwise than as provided in that subsection; or\n\n(b) the power of a court to authorise service of a document\notherwise than as provided in that subsection."
    },
