    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-184",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 72B  Criteria for making exemption order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-184"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister must not make an exemption order unless the\nMinister is of the opinion that it is in the national interest to make\nthe order.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining what is in the\nnational interest, the Minister must have regard to each of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) Australia’s international relations;\n\n(b) Australia’s international obligations;\n\n(c) any relevant principle of international law or practice;\n\n(d) the interests of Australian exporters;\n\n(e) the interests of Australian importers;\n\n(f) any other relevant matters.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister must not make an exemption order unless the\nMinister is of the opinion that it is in the national interest to make\nthe order.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining what is in the\nnational interest, the Minister must have regard to each of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) Australia’s international relations;\n\n(b) Australia’s international obligations;\n\n(c) any relevant principle of international law or practice;\n\n(d) the interests of Australian exporters;\n\n(e) the interests of Australian importers;\n\n(f) any other relevant matters.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-184-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-184-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ce0d8ecf4273a261728c924e4195d40bf8be392fabf5cc62ab5abadede7048a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-184",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 72B  Criteria for making exemption order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister must not make an exemption order unless the\nMinister is of the opinion that it is in the national interest to make\nthe order.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining what is in the\nnational interest, the Minister must have regard to each of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) Australia’s international relations;\n\n(b) Australia’s international obligations;\n\n(c) any relevant principle of international law or practice;\n\n(d) the interests of Australian exporters;\n\n(e) the interests of Australian importers;\n\n(f) any other relevant matters."
    },
