      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-197",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 82A  Review by Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-197"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following decisions of\nthe Commission is a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a decision to refuse to hold an investigation under\nsubsection 10.48(2) or 10.58(2);\n\n(b) a decision under section 10.88 to:\n\n(i) exclude a document, or the particulars of a submission,\nfrom the register of Commission investigations; or\n\n(ii) refuse to exclude a document, or the particulars of a\nsubmission, from the register of Commission\ninvestigations.\n\n(2) If the Commission makes a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a person whose interests are affected by the decision; or\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\nmay apply in writing to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) An application under this section for a review of a decision must be\nmade within 21 days after the Commission made the decision.\n\n(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following decisions of\nthe Commission is a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a decision to refuse to hold an investigation under\nsubsection 10.48(2) or 10.58(2);\n\n(b) a decision under section 10.88 to:\n\n(i) exclude a document, or the particulars of a submission,\nfrom the register of Commission investigations; or\n\n(ii) refuse to exclude a document, or the particulars of a\nsubmission, from the register of Commission\ninvestigations.\n\n(2) If the Commission makes a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a person whose interests are affected by the decision; or\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\nmay apply in writing to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) An application under this section for a review of a decision must be\nmade within 21 days after the Commission made the decision.\n\n(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-197-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-197-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-197-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-197-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0d70edf33ce6607c2daba6be01cb933f19ae43543e6e135ecdf1e05bf2a6336"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-197",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 82A  Review by Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following decisions of\nthe Commission is a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a decision to refuse to hold an investigation under\nsubsection 10.48(2) or 10.58(2);\n\n(b) a decision under section 10.88 to:\n\n(i) exclude a document, or the particulars of a submission,\nfrom the register of Commission investigations; or\n\n(ii) refuse to exclude a document, or the particulars of a\nsubmission, from the register of Commission\ninvestigations.\n\n(2) If the Commission makes a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a person whose interests are affected by the decision; or\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\nmay apply in writing to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) An application under this section for a review of a decision must be\nmade within 21 days after the Commission made the decision.\n\n(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision."
    },
    {
