    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-198",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 82B  Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-198"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a decision of the Commission of a kind mentioned\nin section 10.82A, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming,\nsetting aside or varying the decision of the Commission and, for\nthe purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and\nexercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a\ndecision of the Commission is taken for the purposes of this Act\n(other than this Division) to be a decision of the Commission.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nReview of decisions of Commission  Division 14A\n\nSection 10.82C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to\ngive such information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nCommission in connection with the making of the decision to\nwhich the review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On a review of a decision of the Commission of a kind mentioned\nin section 10.82A, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming,\nsetting aside or varying the decision of the Commission and, for\nthe purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and\nexercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a\ndecision of the Commission is taken for the purposes of this Act\n(other than this Division) to be a decision of the Commission.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nReview of decisions of Commission  Division 14A\n\nSection 10.82C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to\ngive such information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nCommission in connection with the making of the decision to\nwhich the review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-198-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-198-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-198-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-198-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "969e9060d83e2e1fbef22ca31ae89a10f679b19bc0f33b9d0db2310fac2aa682"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-198",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 82B  Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a decision of the Commission of a kind mentioned\nin section 10.82A, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming,\nsetting aside or varying the decision of the Commission and, for\nthe purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and\nexercise all the powers of the Commission.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a\ndecision of the Commission is taken for the purposes of this Act\n(other than this Division) to be a decision of the Commission.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nReview of decisions of Commission  Division 14A\n\nSection 10.82C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to\ngive such information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nCommission in connection with the making of the decision to\nwhich the review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal."
    },
    {
