      "cml:conclusionText": "reviewable decisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-201",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 64(3)(a) to:",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-201"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(i) revoke a reference; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke a reference;\n\n(d) a decision under paragraph 10.49(3)(c) to:\n\n(i) revoke a direction; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke a direction;\n\n(e) a decision to:\n\n(i) make; or\n\n(ii) refuse to make;\n\nan order under subsection 10.54(1) or 10.61(1);\n\n(f) a decision under paragraph 10.59(3)(c) or 10.64(3)(b) to:\n\n(i) revoke an order; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke an order.\n\n(2) If the Minister makes a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a person whose interests are affected by the decision; or\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\nmay apply in writing to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nReview of decisions of Minister  Division 14B\n\nSection 10.82E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) An application under this section for a review of a decision must be\nmade within 21 days after the Minister made the decision.\n\n(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(i) revoke a reference; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke a reference;\n\n(d) a decision under paragraph 10.49(3)(c) to:\n\n(i) revoke a direction; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke a direction;\n\n(e) a decision to:\n\n(i) make; or\n\n(ii) refuse to make;\n\nan order under subsection 10.54(1) or 10.61(1);\n\n(f) a decision under paragraph 10.59(3)(c) or 10.64(3)(b) to:\n\n(i) revoke an order; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke an order.\n\n(2) If the Minister makes a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a person whose interests are affected by the decision; or\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\nmay apply in writing to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nReview of decisions of Minister  Division 14B\n\nSection 10.82E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) An application under this section for a review of a decision must be\nmade within 21 days after the Minister made the decision.\n\n(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-201-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-201-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-201-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b9fd65f04cfbc432d9b57dab64e6ef20dc588e0e517b9684ac4c29b08103973"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-201",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 64(3)(a) to:",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(i) revoke a reference; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke a reference;\n\n(d) a decision under paragraph 10.49(3)(c) to:\n\n(i) revoke a direction; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke a direction;\n\n(e) a decision to:\n\n(i) make; or\n\n(ii) refuse to make;\n\nan order under subsection 10.54(1) or 10.61(1);\n\n(f) a decision under paragraph 10.59(3)(c) or 10.64(3)(b) to:\n\n(i) revoke an order; or\n\n(ii) refuse to revoke an order.\n\n(2) If the Minister makes a reviewable decision:\n\n(a) a person whose interests are affected by the decision; or\n\n(b) a designated shipper body;\nmay apply in writing to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nInternational liner cargo shipping  Part X\nReview of decisions of Minister  Division 14B\n\nSection 10.82E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(3) An application under this section for a review of a decision must be\nmade within 21 days after the Minister made the decision.\n\n(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision."
    },
