      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a review of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The review obligation is a subclass of the general obligation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-202",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 82E  Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-202"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.111",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a decision of the Minister of a kind mentioned in\nsection 10.82D, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming,\nsetting aside or varying the decision of the Minister and, for the\npurposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise\nall the powers of the Minister.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a\ndecision of the Minister is taken for the purposes of this Act (other\nthan this Division) to be a decision of the Minister.\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may request the Minister to give\nsuch information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies. The Minister\nmust comply with such a request.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nMinister in connection with the making of the decision to which\nthe review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On a review of a decision of the Minister of a kind mentioned in\nsection 10.82D, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming,\nsetting aside or varying the decision of the Minister and, for the\npurposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise\nall the powers of the Minister.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a\ndecision of the Minister is taken for the purposes of this Act (other\nthan this Division) to be a decision of the Minister.\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may request the Minister to give\nsuch information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies. The Minister\nmust comply with such a request.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nMinister in connection with the making of the decision to which\nthe review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-202-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-202-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-202-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-202-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3e6c24fd716bfcc220ceb5904b15fd34b38ec2a2bbb9852c9ef97a1fed4183b0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-202",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 82E  Functions and powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 111,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a decision of the Minister of a kind mentioned in\nsection 10.82D, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming,\nsetting aside or varying the decision of the Minister and, for the\npurposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise\nall the powers of the Minister.\n\n(2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a\ndecision of the Minister is taken for the purposes of this Act (other\nthan this Division) to be a decision of the Minister.\n\n(3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the\nTribunal presiding at the review may request the Minister to give\nsuch information, make such reports and provide such other\nassistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies. The Minister\nmust comply with such a request.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any\ninformation given, documents produced or evidence given to the\nMinister in connection with the making of the decision to which\nthe review relates.\nNote:\nDivision 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal."
    },
