      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Certain decisions are not reviewable.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Decision as to the form of a register is exempt.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Review of such decision is not allowed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-207",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 85  Statement to accompany notices of Registrar",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-207"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the Registrar makes a reviewable decision (within the\nmeaning of section 10.84) and gives to a person whose interests are\naffected by the decision written notice of the making of the\ndecision, the notice must include:\n\n(a) a statement to the effect that application may be made to the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal under the Administrative\nReview Tribunal Act 2024 for review of a decision of the\nRegistrar under this Part; and\n\n(b) a statement to the effect that a person who is entitled to apply\nto the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of a\ndecision may, under section 268 of that Act, request a\nstatement of reasons (within the meaning of that Act).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where the Registrar makes a reviewable decision (within the\nmeaning of section 10.84) and gives to a person whose interests are\naffected by the decision written notice of the making of the\ndecision, the notice must include:\n\n(a) a statement to the effect that application may be made to the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal under the Administrative\nReview Tribunal Act 2024 for review of a decision of the\nRegistrar under this Part; and\n\n(b) a statement to the effect that a person who is entitled to apply\nto the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of a\ndecision may, under section 268 of that Act, request a\nstatement of reasons (within the meaning of that Act).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-207-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-207-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "94aac477ceadf378bdca81a266ddeca2e0c729bd3a86c5d3ffc49f71b5473cd2",
      "skos:note": "Notice must include application for review and request for statement of reasons.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-207",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 85  Statement to accompany notices of Registrar",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the Registrar makes a reviewable decision (within the\nmeaning of section 10.84) and gives to a person whose interests are\naffected by the decision written notice of the making of the\ndecision, the notice must include:\n\n(a) a statement to the effect that application may be made to the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal under the Administrative\nReview Tribunal Act 2024 for review of a decision of the\nRegistrar under this Part; and\n\n(b) a statement to the effect that a person who is entitled to apply\nto the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of a\ndecision may, under section 268 of that Act, request a\nstatement of reasons (within the meaning of that Act).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
