    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-215",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 91  Application of Part XID and section 155 to investigations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-10-215"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "under Part\n\n(1) Part XID and section 155 apply in relation to an investigation by\nthe Commission under this Part as if the investigation were an\ninvestigation by the Commission relating to a matter that\nconstitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of this Act.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) shall not be taken to limit by implication any\npowers that the Commission has apart from that subsection.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 130\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "under Part\n\n(1) Part XID and section 155 apply in relation to an investigation by\nthe Commission under this Part as if the investigation were an\ninvestigation by the Commission relating to a matter that\nconstitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of this Act.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) shall not be taken to limit by implication any\npowers that the Commission has apart from that subsection.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 130\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
