    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "131(2) Application of the Australian Consumer Law in relation to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1):\n\n(a) section 21 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth in relation to:\n\n(i) a supply or possible supply of goods or services by any\nperson to a corporation; or\n\n(ii) an acquisition or possible acquisition of goods or\nservices from any person by a corporation; and\n\n(b) section 147 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth to, and in relation to, a corporation as a\nsupplier referred to in that section; and\n\n(c) Division 2 of Part 5-1 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of\nthe Commonwealth to and in relation to a person if the other\nperson referred to in section 219 of Schedule 2 is a\ncorporation; and\n\n(d) section 33 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth to, and in relation to, the conduct of any\nperson.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1):\n\n(a) section 21 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth in relation to:\n\n(i) a supply or possible supply of goods or services by any\nperson to a corporation; or\n\n(ii) an acquisition or possible acquisition of goods or\nservices from any person by a corporation; and\n\n(b) section 147 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth to, and in relation to, a corporation as a\nsupplier referred to in that section; and\n\n(c) Division 2 of Part 5-1 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of\nthe Commonwealth to and in relation to a person if the other\nperson referred to in section 219 of Schedule 2 is a\ncorporation; and\n\n(d) section 33 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth to, and in relation to, the conduct of any\nperson.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a4ff3006f687c64aee06ab64fe4a16eb5980d0af777a18388b932cfb08724eaa",
      "skos:note": "Application of the Australian Consumer Law in relation to corporations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "131(2) Application of the Australian Consumer Law in relation to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1):\n\n(a) section 21 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth in relation to:\n\n(i) a supply or possible supply of goods or services by any\nperson to a corporation; or\n\n(ii) an acquisition or possible acquisition of goods or\nservices from any person by a corporation; and\n\n(b) section 147 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth to, and in relation to, a corporation as a\nsupplier referred to in that section; and\n\n(c) Division 2 of Part 5-1 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of\nthe Commonwealth to and in relation to a person if the other\nperson referred to in section 219 of Schedule 2 is a\ncorporation; and\n\n(d) section 33 of Schedule 2 also applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth to, and in relation to, the conduct of any\nperson."
    },
