      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "131A Division does not apply to financial services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.123",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite section 131, this Division does not apply, other than in\nrelation to the following provisions of Schedule 2 as they apply as\na law of the Commonwealth, to the supply, or possible supply, of\nservices that are financial services, or of financial products:\n\n(a) Division 3A of Part 3-2;\n\n(b) Division 3A of Part 4-2;\n\n(c) Part 5-5.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1):\n\n(a) Part 2-1 of Schedule 2 and sections 34 and 156 of Schedule 2\ndo not apply to conduct engaged in in relation to financial\nservices; and\n\n(b) Part 2-3 of Schedule 2 does not apply to, or in relation to:\n\n(i) contracts that are financial products; or\n\n(ii) contracts for the supply, or possible supply, of services\nthat are financial services; and\n\n(c) if a financial product consists of or includes an interest in\nland—the following provisions of Schedule 2 do not apply to\nthat interest:\n\n(i) section 30;\n\n(ii) paragraphs 32(1)(c) and (d) and (2)(c) and (d);\n\n(iii) paragraphs 50(1)(c) and (d);\n\n(iv) section 152;\n\n(v) subparagraphs 154(1)(b)(iii) and (iv) and (2)(b)(iii) and\n(iv);\n\n(vi) subparagraphs 168(1)(b)(iii) and (iv); and\n\n(d) sections 39 and 161 of Schedule 2 do not apply to:\n\n(i) a credit card that is part of, or that provides access to, a\ncredit facility that is a financial product; or\n\n(ii) a debit card that allows access to an account that is a\nfinancial product.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite section 131, this Division does not apply, other than in\nrelation to the following provisions of Schedule 2 as they apply as\na law of the Commonwealth, to the supply, or possible supply, of\nservices that are financial services, or of financial products:\n\n(a) Division 3A of Part 3-2;\n\n(b) Division 3A of Part 4-2;\n\n(c) Part 5-5.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1):\n\n(a) Part 2-1 of Schedule 2 and sections 34 and 156 of Schedule 2\ndo not apply to conduct engaged in in relation to financial\nservices; and\n\n(b) Part 2-3 of Schedule 2 does not apply to, or in relation to:\n\n(i) contracts that are financial products; or\n\n(ii) contracts for the supply, or possible supply, of services\nthat are financial services; and\n\n(c) if a financial product consists of or includes an interest in\nland—the following provisions of Schedule 2 do not apply to\nthat interest:\n\n(i) section 30;\n\n(ii) paragraphs 32(1)(c) and (d) and (2)(c) and (d);\n\n(iii) paragraphs 50(1)(c) and (d);\n\n(iv) section 152;\n\n(v) subparagraphs 154(1)(b)(iii) and (iv) and (2)(b)(iii) and\n(iv);\n\n(vi) subparagraphs 168(1)(b)(iii) and (iv); and\n\n(d) sections 39 and 161 of Schedule 2 do not apply to:\n\n(i) a credit card that is part of, or that provides access to, a\ncredit facility that is a financial product; or\n\n(ii) a debit card that allows access to an account that is a\nfinancial product.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "487f859d520820b6feaa59f9a03ffa1c7f329cc982a7c09123a9ec41ecffc1b0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "131A Division does not apply to financial services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 123,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite section 131, this Division does not apply, other than in\nrelation to the following provisions of Schedule 2 as they apply as\na law of the Commonwealth, to the supply, or possible supply, of\nservices that are financial services, or of financial products:\n\n(a) Division 3A of Part 3-2;\n\n(b) Division 3A of Part 4-2;\n\n(c) Part 5-5.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1):\n\n(a) Part 2-1 of Schedule 2 and sections 34 and 156 of Schedule 2\ndo not apply to conduct engaged in in relation to financial\nservices; and\n\n(b) Part 2-3 of Schedule 2 does not apply to, or in relation to:\n\n(i) contracts that are financial products; or\n\n(ii) contracts for the supply, or possible supply, of services\nthat are financial services; and\n\n(c) if a financial product consists of or includes an interest in\nland—the following provisions of Schedule 2 do not apply to\nthat interest:\n\n(i) section 30;\n\n(ii) paragraphs 32(1)(c) and (d) and (2)(c) and (d);\n\n(iii) paragraphs 50(1)(c) and (d);\n\n(iv) section 152;\n\n(v) subparagraphs 154(1)(b)(iii) and (iv) and (2)(b)(iii) and\n(iv);\n\n(vi) subparagraphs 168(1)(b)(iii) and (iv); and\n\n(d) sections 39 and 161 of Schedule 2 do not apply to:\n\n(i) a credit card that is part of, or that provides access to, a\ncredit facility that is a financial product; or\n\n(ii) a debit card that allows access to an account that is a\nfinancial product.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
