      "cml:integrityHash": "531309b1ca33f21e735debee65830ffafc620ba8a0ae8340b0c8db6fb3bee243",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from concurrent prosecution for offenses against multiple laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "131C(3) Saving of other laws and remedies",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Despite subsection (1):\n\n(a) if an act or omission of a person is both:\n\n(i) an offence against this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw; and\n\n(ii) an offence against a law of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(b) the person is convicted of either of those offences;\nhe or she is not liable to be convicted of the other of those\noffences."
    },
