    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "131C(4) Saving of other laws and remedies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131c-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Except as expressly provided by this Part or the Australian\nConsumer Law, nothing in this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw is taken to limit, restrict or otherwise affect any right or\nremedy a person would have had if this Part and the Australian\nConsumer Law had not been enacted.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Division\n\nSection 131D\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Effect of other Commonwealth laws on the\nAustralian Consumer Law",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Except as expressly provided by this Part or the Australian\nConsumer Law, nothing in this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw is taken to limit, restrict or otherwise affect any right or\nremedy a person would have had if this Part and the Australian\nConsumer Law had not been enacted.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Division\n\nSection 131D\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Effect of other Commonwealth laws on the\nAustralian Consumer Law",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131c-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131c-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ace5ea2546e360140e00e3b45f9b93f05c0b07f235f02150a608891d80488964",
      "skos:note": "Preserves rights and remedies under other laws"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "131C(4) Saving of other laws and remedies",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Except as expressly provided by this Part or the Australian\nConsumer Law, nothing in this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw is taken to limit, restrict or otherwise affect any right or\nremedy a person would have had if this Part and the Australian\nConsumer Law had not been enacted.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Division\n\nSection 131D\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Effect of other Commonwealth laws on the\nAustralian Consumer Law"
    },
