    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "131E Application of the Legislation Act 2003",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following instruments made under the Australian Consumer\nLaw by the Commonwealth Minister are to be made by legislative\ninstrument:\n\n(a) a determination under subsection 66(1) (display notices);\n\n(b) a notice under subsection 104(1) (safety standards);\n\n(c) a notice under subsection 109(1) or (2) (interim bans);\n\n(d) a notice under section 111 (extensions of interim bans);\n\n(e) a notice under section 113 (revocation of interim bans);\n\n(f) a notice under subsection 114(1) or (2) (permanent bans);\n\n(g) a notice under section 117 (revocation of permanent bans);\n\n(h) a notice under subsection 122(1) (recall notices);\n\n(i) a notice under subsection 134(1) (information standards).\n\n(2) The following instruments made under the Australian Consumer\nLaw are not legislative instruments:\n\n(a) an approval given under paragraph 106(5)(b) (approval to\nexport);\n\n(b) an approval given under paragraph 118(5)(b) (approval to\nexport);\n\n(c) a notice under subsection 128(3) (voluntary recalls);\n\n(d) a notice under subsection 129(1) or (2) (safety warning\nnotices);\n\n(e) a notice under subsection 130(1) (announcement of results of\nan investigation);\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following instruments made under the Australian Consumer\nLaw by the Commonwealth Minister are to be made by legislative\ninstrument:\n\n(a) a determination under subsection 66(1) (display notices);\n\n(b) a notice under subsection 104(1) (safety standards);\n\n(c) a notice under subsection 109(1) or (2) (interim bans);\n\n(d) a notice under section 111 (extensions of interim bans);\n\n(e) a notice under section 113 (revocation of interim bans);\n\n(f) a notice under subsection 114(1) or (2) (permanent bans);\n\n(g) a notice under section 117 (revocation of permanent bans);\n\n(h) a notice under subsection 122(1) (recall notices);\n\n(i) a notice under subsection 134(1) (information standards).\n\n(2) The following instruments made under the Australian Consumer\nLaw are not legislative instruments:\n\n(a) an approval given under paragraph 106(5)(b) (approval to\nexport);\n\n(b) an approval given under paragraph 118(5)(b) (approval to\nexport);\n\n(c) a notice under subsection 128(3) (voluntary recalls);\n\n(d) a notice under subsection 129(1) or (2) (safety warning\nnotices);\n\n(e) a notice under subsection 130(1) (announcement of results of\nan investigation);\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "73f6e5ba52ffad9f97cacfb95cec765fed6f0613fddfe7bbd730244c54059656"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-131e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "131E Application of the Legislation Act 2003",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following instruments made under the Australian Consumer\nLaw by the Commonwealth Minister are to be made by legislative\ninstrument:\n\n(a) a determination under subsection 66(1) (display notices);\n\n(b) a notice under subsection 104(1) (safety standards);\n\n(c) a notice under subsection 109(1) or (2) (interim bans);\n\n(d) a notice under section 111 (extensions of interim bans);\n\n(e) a notice under section 113 (revocation of interim bans);\n\n(f) a notice under subsection 114(1) or (2) (permanent bans);\n\n(g) a notice under section 117 (revocation of permanent bans);\n\n(h) a notice under subsection 122(1) (recall notices);\n\n(i) a notice under subsection 134(1) (information standards).\n\n(2) The following instruments made under the Australian Consumer\nLaw are not legislative instruments:\n\n(a) an approval given under paragraph 106(5)(b) (approval to\nexport);\n\n(b) an approval given under paragraph 118(5)(b) (approval to\nexport);\n\n(c) a notice under subsection 128(3) (voluntary recalls);\n\n(d) a notice under subsection 129(1) or (2) (safety warning\nnotices);\n\n(e) a notice under subsection 130(1) (announcement of results of\nan investigation);\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
