    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "132C Notification of conference",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-132c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If one or more persons notify the Commission in accordance with a\nproposed ban notice, or a proposed recall notice, that they wish the\nCommission to hold a conference, the Commission must:\n\n(a) appoint a day, time and place for the holding of the\nconference; and\n\n(b) give written notice to the Commonwealth Minister, and to\neach person who so notified the Commission, of that day,\ntime and place.\n\n(2) The day appointed must be at least 5 days, but not more than 14\ndays, after the end of the period:\n\n(a) for a proposed ban notice—specified under\nparagraph 132(3)(e); or\n\n(b) for a proposed recall notice—specified under\nparagraph 132A(3)(e).\n\n(3) A notice under paragraph (1)(b) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If one or more persons notify the Commission in accordance with a\nproposed ban notice, or a proposed recall notice, that they wish the\nCommission to hold a conference, the Commission must:\n\n(a) appoint a day, time and place for the holding of the\nconference; and\n\n(b) give written notice to the Commonwealth Minister, and to\neach person who so notified the Commission, of that day,\ntime and place.\n\n(2) The day appointed must be at least 5 days, but not more than 14\ndays, after the end of the period:\n\n(a) for a proposed ban notice—specified under\nparagraph 132(3)(e); or\n\n(b) for a proposed recall notice—specified under\nparagraph 132A(3)(e).\n\n(3) A notice under paragraph (1)(b) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ef547cd10ee54ed674ca7467b85f6e40e7b408b3154313f78faae7b922bcf55"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-132c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "132C Notification of conference",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If one or more persons notify the Commission in accordance with a\nproposed ban notice, or a proposed recall notice, that they wish the\nCommission to hold a conference, the Commission must:\n\n(a) appoint a day, time and place for the holding of the\nconference; and\n\n(b) give written notice to the Commonwealth Minister, and to\neach person who so notified the Commission, of that day,\ntime and place.\n\n(2) The day appointed must be at least 5 days, but not more than 14\ndays, after the end of the period:\n\n(a) for a proposed ban notice—specified under\nparagraph 132(3)(e); or\n\n(b) for a proposed recall notice—specified under\nparagraph 132A(3)(e).\n\n(3) A notice under paragraph (1)(b) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
