    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "132E Opportunity for a conference after an interim ban has been",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-132e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.131",
      "values:originalText": "imposed by the Commonwealth Minister\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind, or on\nproduct related services of a particular kind, is in force; and\n\n(b) the interim ban was imposed by the Commonwealth\nMinister; and\n\n(c) before the ban was imposed, the Commonwealth Minister\npublished a notice under section 132J certifying that the\ninterim ban should be imposed without delay.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth Minister must, by written notice published on\nthe internet, invite any person who supplied, or proposes to supply:\n\n(a) consumer goods of that kind; or\n\n(b) product related services of that kind;\nto notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified\nin the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a\nconference in relation to the interim ban.\n\n(3) The period specified in the notice under subsection (2):\n\n(a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as\nthe Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and\n\n(b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is\npublished.\n\n(4) A notice under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "imposed by the Commonwealth Minister\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind, or on\nproduct related services of a particular kind, is in force; and\n\n(b) the interim ban was imposed by the Commonwealth\nMinister; and\n\n(c) before the ban was imposed, the Commonwealth Minister\npublished a notice under section 132J certifying that the\ninterim ban should be imposed without delay.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth Minister must, by written notice published on\nthe internet, invite any person who supplied, or proposes to supply:\n\n(a) consumer goods of that kind; or\n\n(b) product related services of that kind;\nto notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified\nin the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a\nconference in relation to the interim ban.\n\n(3) The period specified in the notice under subsection (2):\n\n(a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as\nthe Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and\n\n(b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is\npublished.\n\n(4) A notice under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132e-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132e-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "29c2694087cc134a5f8a08e70c2572a63ad8aeee96b0846ad4e87789cb7f4705"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-132e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "132E Opportunity for a conference after an interim ban has been",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 131,
      "values:originalText": "imposed by the Commonwealth Minister\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an interim ban on consumer goods of a particular kind, or on\nproduct related services of a particular kind, is in force; and\n\n(b) the interim ban was imposed by the Commonwealth\nMinister; and\n\n(c) before the ban was imposed, the Commonwealth Minister\npublished a notice under section 132J certifying that the\ninterim ban should be imposed without delay.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth Minister must, by written notice published on\nthe internet, invite any person who supplied, or proposes to supply:\n\n(a) consumer goods of that kind; or\n\n(b) product related services of that kind;\nto notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified\nin the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a\nconference in relation to the interim ban.\n\n(3) The period specified in the notice under subsection (2):\n\n(a) must be a period of at least 10 days, or such longer period as\nthe Commonwealth Minister specifies in the notice; and\n\n(b) must not commence before the day on which the notice is\npublished.\n\n(4) A notice under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
