    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "132G Recommendation after conclusion of conference",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-132g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(1) As soon as is practicable after the conclusion of a conference held\nunder this Subdivision in relation to an interim ban, the\nCommission must:\n\n(a) by written notice given to the Commonwealth Minister,\nrecommend that the interim ban remain in force, be varied or\nbe revoked; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the notice to be given to each person who\nwas present or represented at the conference.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth Minister must:\n\n(a) have regard to a recommendation made under\nparagraph (1)(a); and\n\n(b) if he or she decides to act otherwise than in accordance with\nthe recommendation—the Commonwealth Minister must, by\nwritten notice published on the internet, set out the reasons\nfor his or her decision.\nSubdivision C—Conduct of conferences",
      "skos:definition": "(1) As soon as is practicable after the conclusion of a conference held\nunder this Subdivision in relation to an interim ban, the\nCommission must:\n\n(a) by written notice given to the Commonwealth Minister,\nrecommend that the interim ban remain in force, be varied or\nbe revoked; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the notice to be given to each person who\nwas present or represented at the conference.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth Minister must:\n\n(a) have regard to a recommendation made under\nparagraph (1)(a); and\n\n(b) if he or she decides to act otherwise than in accordance with\nthe recommendation—the Commonwealth Minister must, by\nwritten notice published on the internet, set out the reasons\nfor his or her decision.\nSubdivision C—Conduct of conferences",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc624b3edbd2a4c83b1231bf6d4e60b32d5c6b051a9f0fedffd1af2d281d6e94"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-132g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "132G Recommendation after conclusion of conference",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(1) As soon as is practicable after the conclusion of a conference held\nunder this Subdivision in relation to an interim ban, the\nCommission must:\n\n(a) by written notice given to the Commonwealth Minister,\nrecommend that the interim ban remain in force, be varied or\nbe revoked; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the notice to be given to each person who\nwas present or represented at the conference.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth Minister must:\n\n(a) have regard to a recommendation made under\nparagraph (1)(a); and\n\n(b) if he or she decides to act otherwise than in accordance with\nthe recommendation—the Commonwealth Minister must, by\nwritten notice published on the internet, set out the reasons\nfor his or her decision.\nSubdivision C—Conduct of conferences"
    },
