    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133A Identity cards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to a person appointed\nas an inspector.\nForm of identity card\n\n(2) The identity card must:\n\n(a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(b) contain a recent photograph of the person.\nOffence\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been issued with an identity card under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing,\nreturn the identity card to the Chairperson.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.\n\n(4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\nDefence: card lost or destroyed\n\n(5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or\ndestroyed.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nInspector must carry card\n\n(6) An inspector issued with an identity card under subsection (1) must\ncarry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers as\nan inspector.\nSubdivision B—Premises to which the public is given access",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to a person appointed\nas an inspector.\nForm of identity card\n\n(2) The identity card must:\n\n(a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(b) contain a recent photograph of the person.\nOffence\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been issued with an identity card under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing,\nreturn the identity card to the Chairperson.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.\n\n(4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\nDefence: card lost or destroyed\n\n(5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or\ndestroyed.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nInspector must carry card\n\n(6) An inspector issued with an identity card under subsection (1) must\ncarry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers as\nan inspector.\nSubdivision B—Premises to which the public is given access",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cdbc39c21ca982950c9881338cbea2069cf9582129b581ee98065af6a4a5af16"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133A Identity cards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to a person appointed\nas an inspector.\nForm of identity card\n\n(2) The identity card must:\n\n(a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(b) contain a recent photograph of the person.\nOffence\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been issued with an identity card under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing,\nreturn the identity card to the Chairperson.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.\n\n(4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\nDefence: card lost or destroyed\n\n(5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or\ndestroyed.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nInspector must carry card\n\n(6) An inspector issued with an identity card under subsection (1) must\ncarry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers as\nan inspector.\nSubdivision B—Premises to which the public is given access"
    },
