      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been issued with an identity card under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing,\nreturn the identity card to the Chairperson.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been issued with an identity card under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing,\nreturn the identity card to the Chairperson.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e32a2fd0cc5cb4c6a94be191560e129874e2649368fa0553e575dae907162067",
      "skos:note": "Return identity card to Chairperson after ceasing to be an inspector."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133A(3) Identity cards",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been issued with an identity card under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing,\nreturn the identity card to the Chairperson.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit."
    },
