    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133E Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from:\n\n(a) giving information or evidence; or\n\n(b) producing a document;\nas required by a disclosure notice given to the person on the ground\nthat the information or evidence, or production of the document,\nmight tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a\npenalty.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n\n(a) the information or evidence given, or the document\nproduced; and\n\n(b) giving the information or evidence, or producing the\ndocument;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n\n(c) in any proceedings instituted by the individual; or\n\n(d) in any criminal proceedings, other than proceedings against\nthe individual for an offence against section 133F or 133G.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is not excused from:\n\n(a) giving information or evidence; or\n\n(b) producing a document;\nas required by a disclosure notice given to the person on the ground\nthat the information or evidence, or production of the document,\nmight tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a\npenalty.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n\n(a) the information or evidence given, or the document\nproduced; and\n\n(b) giving the information or evidence, or producing the\ndocument;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n\n(c) in any proceedings instituted by the individual; or\n\n(d) in any criminal proceedings, other than proceedings against\nthe individual for an offence against section 133F or 133G.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12be0567a85da4b8d2a08aed22281578900f162c3f7089d2d5ee70ba8b3e8358"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133E Self-incrimination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from:\n\n(a) giving information or evidence; or\n\n(b) producing a document;\nas required by a disclosure notice given to the person on the ground\nthat the information or evidence, or production of the document,\nmight tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a\npenalty.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n\n(a) the information or evidence given, or the document\nproduced; and\n\n(b) giving the information or evidence, or producing the\ndocument;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n\n(c) in any proceedings instituted by the individual; or\n\n(d) in any criminal proceedings, other than proceedings against\nthe individual for an offence against section 133F or 133G."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133e-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133E(1) Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133e-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from:\n\n(a) giving information or evidence; or\n\n(b) producing a document;\nas required by a disclosure notice given to the person on the ground\nthat the information or evidence, or production of the document,\nmight tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a\npenalty.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is not excused from:\n\n(a) giving information or evidence; or\n\n(b) producing a document;\nas required by a disclosure notice given to the person on the ground\nthat the information or evidence, or production of the document,\nmight tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a\npenalty.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133e"
      },
