      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133e-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits admissibility of self-incrimination evidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) However, in the case of an individual:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133F Compliance with disclosure notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.141",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person refuses or fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person complies with the\ndisclosure notice to the extent to which the person is capable of\ncomplying with the notice.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n133G  False or misleading information etc.\n\nA person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in\npurported compliance with a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or\ndocument is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person refuses or fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person complies with the\ndisclosure notice to the extent to which the person is capable of\ncomplying with the notice.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n133G  False or misleading information etc.\n\nA person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in\npurported compliance with a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or\ndocument is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f84ad2a0ea761c0f6bb4e7275675c99cc2d0909c818147bc05e156a61cf2c299"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133F Compliance with disclosure notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 141,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person refuses or fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) if the person is a body corporate—200 penalty units; or\n\n(b) if the person is not a body corporate—40 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person complies with the\ndisclosure notice to the extent to which the person is capable of\ncomplying with the notice.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n133G  False or misleading information etc.\n\nA person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in\npurported compliance with a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or\ndocument is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
