    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133F(3) Compliance with disclosure notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133f-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.141",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n133G  False or misleading information etc.\n\nA person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in\npurported compliance with a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or\ndocument is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n133G  False or misleading information etc.\n\nA person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in\npurported compliance with a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or\ndocument is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "35d4892465fec96d10ddc63fa522a71ca140387d698e479c3865ffd58fbc19c8",
      "skos:note": "Compliance with disclosure notices is an offence of strict liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133F(3) Compliance with disclosure notices",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 141,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n133G  False or misleading information etc.\n\nA person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives information, evidence or a document in\npurported compliance with a disclosure notice; and\n\n(b) the person does so knowing that the information, evidence or\ndocument is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133f-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
