    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133H Court orders relating to consumer goods that do not comply",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.142",
      "values:originalText": "with a safety standard etc.\n\n(1) If a court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) a person possesses or has control of consumer goods of a\nparticular kind; and\n\n(b) any of the following apply:\n\n(i) the consumer goods do not comply with a safety\nstandard that is in force for consumer goods of that kind\nand the cause of that non-compliance cannot be\nremedied;\n\n(ii) a permanent ban on consumer goods of that kind is in\nforce;\n\n(iii) a recall notice for consumer goods of that kind is in\nforce and a defect or dangerous characteristic of such\nconsumer goods identified in the notice cannot be\nremedied;\nthe court may, on the application of an inspector, make an order of\na kind referred to in subsection (2).\n\n(2) The court may make an order under subsection (1) authorising one\nor more inspectors to do the following in accordance with any\nrequirements specified in the order:\n\n(a) to enter the premises of the person that are specified in the\norder;\n\n(b) to search the premises for consumer goods of a kind specified\nin the order;\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133J\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) to seize any such consumer goods that are found at those\npremises;\n\n(d) to destroy or otherwise dispose of any such consumer goods\nthat are so seized.\n\n(3) Before making an application under subsection (1), the inspector\nmust:\n\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nconsumer goods; and\n\n(b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the\ninspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed\napplication.\n\n(4) A person notified under subsection (3) is entitled to be heard in\nrelation to the application.",
      "skos:definition": "with a safety standard etc.\n\n(1) If a court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) a person possesses or has control of consumer goods of a\nparticular kind; and\n\n(b) any of the following apply:\n\n(i) the consumer goods do not comply with a safety\nstandard that is in force for consumer goods of that kind\nand the cause of that non-compliance cannot be\nremedied;\n\n(ii) a permanent ban on consumer goods of that kind is in\nforce;\n\n(iii) a recall notice for consumer goods of that kind is in\nforce and a defect or dangerous characteristic of such\nconsumer goods identified in the notice cannot be\nremedied;\nthe court may, on the application of an inspector, make an order of\na kind referred to in subsection (2).\n\n(2) The court may make an order under subsection (1) authorising one\nor more inspectors to do the following in accordance with any\nrequirements specified in the order:\n\n(a) to enter the premises of the person that are specified in the\norder;\n\n(b) to search the premises for consumer goods of a kind specified\nin the order;\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133J\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) to seize any such consumer goods that are found at those\npremises;\n\n(d) to destroy or otherwise dispose of any such consumer goods\nthat are so seized.\n\n(3) Before making an application under subsection (1), the inspector\nmust:\n\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nconsumer goods; and\n\n(b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the\ninspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed\napplication.\n\n(4) A person notified under subsection (3) is entitled to be heard in\nrelation to the application.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133h-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f5d8cf11a1bf6f6f36eb3d99e73aa0c2df8e3943ad3c3c129179b14c44484f5f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133H Court orders relating to consumer goods that do not comply",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 142,
      "values:originalText": "with a safety standard etc.\n\n(1) If a court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) a person possesses or has control of consumer goods of a\nparticular kind; and\n\n(b) any of the following apply:\n\n(i) the consumer goods do not comply with a safety\nstandard that is in force for consumer goods of that kind\nand the cause of that non-compliance cannot be\nremedied;\n\n(ii) a permanent ban on consumer goods of that kind is in\nforce;\n\n(iii) a recall notice for consumer goods of that kind is in\nforce and a defect or dangerous characteristic of such\nconsumer goods identified in the notice cannot be\nremedied;\nthe court may, on the application of an inspector, make an order of\na kind referred to in subsection (2).\n\n(2) The court may make an order under subsection (1) authorising one\nor more inspectors to do the following in accordance with any\nrequirements specified in the order:\n\n(a) to enter the premises of the person that are specified in the\norder;\n\n(b) to search the premises for consumer goods of a kind specified\nin the order;\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nEnforcement  Division 4\n\nSection 133J\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) to seize any such consumer goods that are found at those\npremises;\n\n(d) to destroy or otherwise dispose of any such consumer goods\nthat are so seized.\n\n(3) Before making an application under subsection (1), the inspector\nmust:\n\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nconsumer goods; and\n\n(b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the\ninspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed\napplication.\n\n(4) A person notified under subsection (3) is entitled to be heard in\nrelation to the application."
    },
