    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133J Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing, and destroying or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.143",
      "values:originalText": "disposing of, consumer goods\n\n(1) If an inspector seizes, and destroys or otherwise disposes of,\nconsumer goods in accordance with an order made under\nsubsection 133H(1):\n\n(a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized; or\n\n(b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods—\nthe owner of the consumer goods;\nis liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by\nthe inspector in seizing, and in destroying or disposing of, the\nconsumer goods.\n\n(2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "disposing of, consumer goods\n\n(1) If an inspector seizes, and destroys or otherwise disposes of,\nconsumer goods in accordance with an order made under\nsubsection 133H(1):\n\n(a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized; or\n\n(b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods—\nthe owner of the consumer goods;\nis liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by\nthe inspector in seizing, and in destroying or disposing of, the\nconsumer goods.\n\n(2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133j-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0d5874930d9cb3dc52eddedde94f482ae50230c66225e474bcd317edd6962abe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-133j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133J Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing, and destroying or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 143,
      "values:originalText": "disposing of, consumer goods\n\n(1) If an inspector seizes, and destroys or otherwise disposes of,\nconsumer goods in accordance with an order made under\nsubsection 133H(1):\n\n(a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized; or\n\n(b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods—\nthe owner of the consumer goods;\nis liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by\nthe inspector in seizing, and in destroying or disposing of, the\nconsumer goods.\n\n(2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
