      "cml:premiseText": "(2) This Division does not:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "134A Issuing an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.144",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that a person\nhas contravened an infringement notice provision, the Commission\nmay issue an infringement notice to the person.\n\n(2) Each of the following provisions of the Australian Consumer Law\nis an infringement notice provision:\n\n(a) a provision of Part 2-2;\n\n(b) a provision of Part 3-1 (other than subsection 32(1), 35(1) or\n36(1), (2) or (3) or section 40 or 43);\n\n(c) subsection 66(2);\n\n(d) a provision of Division 2 of Part 3-2 (other than section 85);\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 134B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) a provision of Division 3 of Part 3-2 (other than\nsubsection 96(2));\n\n(ea) subsection 99B(1), section 99C, subsection 99D(1),\nsection 99E or subsection 99F(2);\n\n(f) subsection 100(1) or (3), 101(3) or (4), 102(2) or 103(2);\n\n(g) subsection 106(1), (2), (3) or (5), 107(1) or (2), 118(1), (2),\n(3) or (5), 119(1) or (2), 125(4), 127(1) or (2), 128(2) or (6),\n131(1), 132(1), 136(1), (2) or (3) or 137(1) or (2);\n\n(h) subsection 221(1) or 222(1).\n\n(3) The Commission must not issue more than one infringement notice\nto the person for the same alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.\n\n(4) The infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:\n\n(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day on which the\ncontravention of the infringement notice provision is alleged\nto have occurred; or\n\n(b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of an\ninfringement notice provision by the person.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that a person\nhas contravened an infringement notice provision, the Commission\nmay issue an infringement notice to the person.\n\n(2) Each of the following provisions of the Australian Consumer Law\nis an infringement notice provision:\n\n(a) a provision of Part 2-2;\n\n(b) a provision of Part 3-1 (other than subsection 32(1), 35(1) or\n36(1), (2) or (3) or section 40 or 43);\n\n(c) subsection 66(2);\n\n(d) a provision of Division 2 of Part 3-2 (other than section 85);\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 134B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) a provision of Division 3 of Part 3-2 (other than\nsubsection 96(2));\n\n(ea) subsection 99B(1), section 99C, subsection 99D(1),\nsection 99E or subsection 99F(2);\n\n(f) subsection 100(1) or (3), 101(3) or (4), 102(2) or 103(2);\n\n(g) subsection 106(1), (2), (3) or (5), 107(1) or (2), 118(1), (2),\n(3) or (5), 119(1) or (2), 125(4), 127(1) or (2), 128(2) or (6),\n131(1), 132(1), 136(1), (2) or (3) or 137(1) or (2);\n\n(h) subsection 221(1) or 222(1).\n\n(3) The Commission must not issue more than one infringement notice\nto the person for the same alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.\n\n(4) The infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:\n\n(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day on which the\ncontravention of the infringement notice provision is alleged\nto have occurred; or\n\n(b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of an\ninfringement notice provision by the person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5643140f7b6c9c3546008c4e4f4384ab55719dd99557eed5f68dd536b7000f2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "134A Issuing an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 144,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that a person\nhas contravened an infringement notice provision, the Commission\nmay issue an infringement notice to the person.\n\n(2) Each of the following provisions of the Australian Consumer Law\nis an infringement notice provision:\n\n(a) a provision of Part 2-2;\n\n(b) a provision of Part 3-1 (other than subsection 32(1), 35(1) or\n36(1), (2) or (3) or section 40 or 43);\n\n(c) subsection 66(2);\n\n(d) a provision of Division 2 of Part 3-2 (other than section 85);\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 134B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(e) a provision of Division 3 of Part 3-2 (other than\nsubsection 96(2));\n\n(ea) subsection 99B(1), section 99C, subsection 99D(1),\nsection 99E or subsection 99F(2);\n\n(f) subsection 100(1) or (3), 101(3) or (4), 102(2) or 103(2);\n\n(g) subsection 106(1), (2), (3) or (5), 107(1) or (2), 118(1), (2),\n(3) or (5), 119(1) or (2), 125(4), 127(1) or (2), 128(2) or (6),\n131(1), 132(1), 136(1), (2) or (3) or 137(1) or (2);\n\n(h) subsection 221(1) or 222(1).\n\n(3) The Commission must not issue more than one infringement notice\nto the person for the same alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.\n\n(4) The infringement notice does not have any effect if the notice:\n\n(a) is issued more than 12 months after the day on which the\ncontravention of the infringement notice provision is alleged\nto have occurred; or\n\n(b) relates to more than one alleged contravention of an\ninfringement notice provision by the person."
    },
