      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) if the person is a listed corporation—600 penalty units...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "must be greater than or equal to that amount after a certain period"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "134D Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an infringement notice for an alleged contravention of an\ninfringement notice provision is issued to a person; and\n\n(b) the person pays the penalty specified in the infringement\nnotice within the infringement notice compliance period and\nin accordance with the notice; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 134E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the infringement notice is not withdrawn under section 134G.\n\n(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as:\n\n(a) having contravened the infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) having been convicted of an offence constituted by the same\nconduct that constituted the alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.\n\n(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to:\n\n(a) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(b) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted\nthe alleged contravention.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an infringement notice for an alleged contravention of an\ninfringement notice provision is issued to a person; and\n\n(b) the person pays the penalty specified in the infringement\nnotice within the infringement notice compliance period and\nin accordance with the notice; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 134E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the infringement notice is not withdrawn under section 134G.\n\n(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as:\n\n(a) having contravened the infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) having been convicted of an offence constituted by the same\nconduct that constituted the alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.\n\n(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to:\n\n(a) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(b) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted\nthe alleged contravention.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3dad32f8c8e92e88e5acfb1e25d0547c5ce3e39366ea5728a924ae17cf867533"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "134D Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an infringement notice for an alleged contravention of an\ninfringement notice provision is issued to a person; and\n\n(b) the person pays the penalty specified in the infringement\nnotice within the infringement notice compliance period and\nin accordance with the notice; and\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nInfringement notices  Division 5\n\nSection 134E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) the infringement notice is not withdrawn under section 134G.\n\n(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as:\n\n(a) having contravened the infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) having been convicted of an offence constituted by the same\nconduct that constituted the alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.\n\n(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to:\n\n(a) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(b) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted\nthe alleged contravention."
    },
    {
