    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "134D(2) Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134d-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as:\n\n(a) having contravened the infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) having been convicted of an offence constituted by the same\nconduct that constituted the alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as:\n\n(a) having contravened the infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) having been convicted of an offence constituted by the same\nconduct that constituted the alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "16fbc9ac02028b029a65b9add6887e2c82a1b7384a857d423cd5861e232f035c",
      "skos:note": "No obligation to admit guilt after payment"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134d-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "134D(2) Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as:\n\n(a) having contravened the infringement notice provision; or\n\n(b) having been convicted of an offence constituted by the same\nconduct that constituted the alleged contravention of the\ninfringement notice provision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Payment does not imply guilt",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Payment",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No guilt"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "134D(3) Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134d-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to:\n\n(a) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(b) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted\nthe alleged contravention.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to:\n\n(a) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(b) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted\nthe alleged contravention.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8587958489451ef9669e68858adf71bf9d580d6962ec2cd10c20f46df83944f",
      "skos:note": "No proceedings can be started or continued against the Commonwealth in relation to the alleged contravention of the infringement notice provision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "134D(3) Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to:\n\n(a) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(b) an offence constituted by the same conduct that constituted\nthe alleged contravention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134d-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
