    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134g-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "134G(5) Withdrawal of an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134g-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The withdrawal notice must state:\n\n(a) the name and address of the person; and\n\n(b) the day on which the infringement notice was issued to the\nperson; and\n\n(c) that the infringement notice is withdrawn; and\n\n(d) that proceedings under Chapter 4 or Part 5-2 of the\nAustralian Consumer Law may be started or continued\nagainst the person in relation to:\n\n(i) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(ii) an offence constituted by the same conduct that\nconstituted the alleged contravention.\nTime limit for giving withdrawal notices",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The withdrawal notice must state:\n\n(a) the name and address of the person; and\n\n(b) the day on which the infringement notice was issued to the\nperson; and\n\n(c) that the infringement notice is withdrawn; and\n\n(d) that proceedings under Chapter 4 or Part 5-2 of the\nAustralian Consumer Law may be started or continued\nagainst the person in relation to:\n\n(i) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(ii) an offence constituted by the same conduct that\nconstituted the alleged contravention.\nTime limit for giving withdrawal notices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134g"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134g-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-134g-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "690af6cd662b689952bcc5db80e4ab0df3ab4cf0dc77a779f43956cfad4f98bc",
      "skos:note": "Withdrawal notice must state certain information.",
      "dc:description": "Time limit for giving withdrawal notices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-134g-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "134G(5) Withdrawal of an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The withdrawal notice must state:\n\n(a) the name and address of the person; and\n\n(b) the day on which the infringement notice was issued to the\nperson; and\n\n(c) that the infringement notice is withdrawn; and\n\n(d) that proceedings under Chapter 4 or Part 5-2 of the\nAustralian Consumer Law may be started or continued\nagainst the person in relation to:\n\n(i) the alleged contravention of the infringement notice\nprovision; or\n\n(ii) an offence constituted by the same conduct that\nconstituted the alleged contravention.\nTime limit for giving withdrawal notices"
    },
