      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135A Search-related powers of inspectors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "Search-related powers—consumer goods\n\n(1) The following are the search-related powers that an inspector may\nexercise, under subsection 135(1), in relation to premises in or\nfrom which the inspector has reason to believe that a person\nsupplies consumer goods of a particular kind:\n\n(a) if entry to the premises is under a search warrant—the power\nto seize consumer goods of that kind;\n\n(b) the power to inspect, handle and measure consumer goods of\nthat kind;\n\n(c) the power to take samples of consumer goods of that kind;\n\n(d) the power:\n\n(i) to inspect, handle and read any documents relating to\nconsumer goods of that kind; and\n\n(ii) to make copies of, or take extracts from, those\ndocuments;\n\n(e) the power:\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Search-related powers—consumer goods\n\n(1) The following are the search-related powers that an inspector may\nexercise, under subsection 135(1), in relation to premises in or\nfrom which the inspector has reason to believe that a person\nsupplies consumer goods of a particular kind:\n\n(a) if entry to the premises is under a search warrant—the power\nto seize consumer goods of that kind;\n\n(b) the power to inspect, handle and measure consumer goods of\nthat kind;\n\n(c) the power to take samples of consumer goods of that kind;\n\n(d) the power:\n\n(i) to inspect, handle and read any documents relating to\nconsumer goods of that kind; and\n\n(ii) to make copies of, or take extracts from, those\ndocuments;\n\n(e) the power:\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
