    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135D Persons assisting inspectors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons\n\n(1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in\nexercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be\nassisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and\nreasonable.\n\n(2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector.\nPowers of a person assisting the inspector\n\n(3) A person assisting the inspector may:\n\n(a) enter the premises; and\n\n(b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but\nonly in accordance with a direction given to the person by the\ninspector.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 135E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned\nin subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by\nthe inspector.",
      "skos:definition": "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons\n\n(1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in\nexercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be\nassisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and\nreasonable.\n\n(2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector.\nPowers of a person assisting the inspector\n\n(3) A person assisting the inspector may:\n\n(a) enter the premises; and\n\n(b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but\nonly in accordance with a direction given to the person by the\ninspector.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 135E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned\nin subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by\nthe inspector.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66856edc540bc7beff27d40f88dfc0bb58ad5f467677634e23c89876ed9b16db"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135D Persons assisting inspectors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons\n\n(1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in\nexercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be\nassisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and\nreasonable.\n\n(2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector.\nPowers of a person assisting the inspector\n\n(3) A person assisting the inspector may:\n\n(a) enter the premises; and\n\n(b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but\nonly in accordance with a direction given to the person by the\ninspector.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 135E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned\nin subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by\nthe inspector."
    },
