      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135F Announcement before entry under warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.159",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector must, before entering premises under a search\nwarrant:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) show his or her identity card to the occupier of the premises,\nor to another person who apparently represents the occupier,\nif the occupier or other person is present at the premises; and\n\n(c) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) However, an inspector is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person (including the inspector or a\nperson assisting the inspector); or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the inspector does not comply with subsection (1) because of\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nthe inspector must, as soon as practicable after entering the\npremises, show his or her identity card to the occupier or other\nperson.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An inspector must, before entering premises under a search\nwarrant:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) show his or her identity card to the occupier of the premises,\nor to another person who apparently represents the occupier,\nif the occupier or other person is present at the premises; and\n\n(c) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) However, an inspector is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person (including the inspector or a\nperson assisting the inspector); or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the inspector does not comply with subsection (1) because of\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nthe inspector must, as soon as practicable after entering the\npremises, show his or her identity card to the occupier or other\nperson.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "71f44acb2ff6b0a13eb2fbbdb97e4f8ecf2686fd5608d975b12ddf67ec4259d2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135F Announcement before entry under warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 159,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector must, before entering premises under a search\nwarrant:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) show his or her identity card to the occupier of the premises,\nor to another person who apparently represents the occupier,\nif the occupier or other person is present at the premises; and\n\n(c) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) However, an inspector is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person (including the inspector or a\nperson assisting the inspector); or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the inspector does not comply with subsection (1) because of\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nthe inspector must, as soon as practicable after entering the\npremises, show his or her identity card to the occupier or other\nperson.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
