      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-2-logic-epistemic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135f-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0acb8112f6e59deff71bc63a4096f30ec6a455355403b702f3d6b2f1faa0c026",
      "skos:note": "Inspector may deviate from subsection (1) under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135f-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135F(2) Announcement before entry under warrant",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 159,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, an inspector is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person (including the inspector or a\nperson assisting the inspector); or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated."
    },
    {
