      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Inspector enters premises because occupier consents",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Occupier's consent is a relevant factor in determining the inspector's authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135J Details of search warrant etc. must be given to the occupier of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "the premises\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises;\nand\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nan inspector executing the warrant must, as soon as practicable:\n\n(c) do one of the following:\n\n(i) if the warrant was issued under section 135Z—make a\ncopy of the warrant available to the occupier or other\nperson (which need not include the signature of the\njudge who issued it);\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 135K\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) if the warrant was signed under section 136—make a\ncopy of the form of warrant completed under\nsubsection 136(7) available to the occupier or other\nperson; and\n\n(d) inform the occupier or other person of the rights and\nresponsibilities of the occupier or other person under\nSubdivision C.\nSubdivision C—Occupier’s etc. rights and responsibilities",
      "skos:definition": "the premises\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises;\nand\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nan inspector executing the warrant must, as soon as practicable:\n\n(c) do one of the following:\n\n(i) if the warrant was issued under section 135Z—make a\ncopy of the warrant available to the occupier or other\nperson (which need not include the signature of the\njudge who issued it);\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 135K\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) if the warrant was signed under section 136—make a\ncopy of the form of warrant completed under\nsubsection 136(7) available to the occupier or other\nperson; and\n\n(d) inform the occupier or other person of the rights and\nresponsibilities of the occupier or other person under\nSubdivision C.\nSubdivision C—Occupier’s etc. rights and responsibilities",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135j-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135j-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "477a0434c692ae4c422fbed26bf9dd9bed676cfe8e8df7143e76ef4e8496f488",
      "skos:note": "Must inform occupier of rights and responsibilities",
      "dc:description": "Copy of warrant or form of warrant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135J Details of search warrant etc. must be given to the occupier of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "the premises\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises;\nand\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nan inspector executing the warrant must, as soon as practicable:\n\n(c) do one of the following:\n\n(i) if the warrant was issued under section 135Z—make a\ncopy of the warrant available to the occupier or other\nperson (which need not include the signature of the\njudge who issued it);\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 135K\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(ii) if the warrant was signed under section 136—make a\ncopy of the form of warrant completed under\nsubsection 136(7) available to the occupier or other\nperson; and\n\n(d) inform the occupier or other person of the rights and\nresponsibilities of the occupier or other person under\nSubdivision C.\nSubdivision C—Occupier’s etc. rights and responsibilities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135j-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135j"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135j-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to inform occupier",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135K Occupier etc. entitled to observe execution of search warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.161",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises;\nand\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nthe occupier or other person is entitled to observe the execution of\nthe warrant.\n\n(2) The right to observe the execution of the search warrant ceases if\nthe occupier or other person impedes that execution.\n\n(3) This section does not prevent the execution of the search warrant in\n2 or more areas of the premises at the same time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises;\nand\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nthe occupier or other person is entitled to observe the execution of\nthe warrant.\n\n(2) The right to observe the execution of the search warrant ceases if\nthe occupier or other person impedes that execution.\n\n(3) This section does not prevent the execution of the search warrant in\n2 or more areas of the premises at the same time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135k-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77934fbb2a7a15a9ea7a556bc0e889f013f28a5dfd4ab7c383fd4c5e2141773c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135K Occupier etc. entitled to observe execution of search warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 161,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a search warrant is being executed in relation to premises;\nand\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\nthe occupier or other person is entitled to observe the execution of\nthe warrant.\n\n(2) The right to observe the execution of the search warrant ceases if\nthe occupier or other person impedes that execution.\n\n(3) This section does not prevent the execution of the search warrant in\n2 or more areas of the premises at the same time."
    },
