    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135M Receipts for seized consumer goods and equipment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.162",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If consumer goods are seized under a search warrant, an inspector\nmust provide a receipt for the goods.\n\n(2) If equipment is seized under a search warrant, an inspector must\nprovide a receipt for the equipment.\n\n(3) One receipt may cover:\n\n(a) consumer goods and equipment that have been so seized; and\n\n(b) 2 or more kinds of consumer goods or equipment that have\nbeen so seized.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If consumer goods are seized under a search warrant, an inspector\nmust provide a receipt for the goods.\n\n(2) If equipment is seized under a search warrant, an inspector must\nprovide a receipt for the equipment.\n\n(3) One receipt may cover:\n\n(a) consumer goods and equipment that have been so seized; and\n\n(b) 2 or more kinds of consumer goods or equipment that have\nbeen so seized.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135m-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135m-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5739b2797e3ec8a3ba8591780d670b2cf95d2340040d31965145e10831302a5e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135M Receipts for seized consumer goods and equipment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 162,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If consumer goods are seized under a search warrant, an inspector\nmust provide a receipt for the goods.\n\n(2) If equipment is seized under a search warrant, an inspector must\nprovide a receipt for the equipment.\n\n(3) One receipt may cover:\n\n(a) consumer goods and equipment that have been so seized; and\n\n(b) 2 or more kinds of consumer goods or equipment that have\nbeen so seized."
    },
