    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135P Judge may permit consumer goods or equipment to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "retained\n\n(1) An inspector who has seized consumer goods or equipment under a\nsearch warrant may, before the end of the period referred to in\nparagraph 135N(1)(b), apply to a judge of the Federal Court for an\norder that the inspector may retain the consumer goods or\nequipment for a further period of up to 60 days.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an application to a judge is made under subsection (1); and\n\n(b) the judge is satisfied that it is necessary in all the\ncircumstances for the inspector to continue to retain the\nconsumer goods or equipment;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "retained\n\n(1) An inspector who has seized consumer goods or equipment under a\nsearch warrant may, before the end of the period referred to in\nparagraph 135N(1)(b), apply to a judge of the Federal Court for an\norder that the inspector may retain the consumer goods or\nequipment for a further period of up to 60 days.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an application to a judge is made under subsection (1); and\n\n(b) the judge is satisfied that it is necessary in all the\ncircumstances for the inspector to continue to retain the\nconsumer goods or equipment;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135p-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ca67bd59cc4116ac80db5f64cbf4747f26ba929c85e8cc689a6123368d08719b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135P Judge may permit consumer goods or equipment to be",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 163,
      "values:originalText": "retained\n\n(1) An inspector who has seized consumer goods or equipment under a\nsearch warrant may, before the end of the period referred to in\nparagraph 135N(1)(b), apply to a judge of the Federal Court for an\norder that the inspector may retain the consumer goods or\nequipment for a further period of up to 60 days.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an application to a judge is made under subsection (1); and\n\n(b) the judge is satisfied that it is necessary in all the\ncircumstances for the inspector to continue to retain the\nconsumer goods or equipment;\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
