    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135Q Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing consumer goods or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "equipment\n\n(1) If an inspector seizes consumer goods or equipment under a search\nwarrant:\n\n(a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized, or\nthe equipment was seized; or\n\n(b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods or\nequipment—the owner of the consumer goods or equipment;\nis liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by\nthe inspector in seizing the consumer goods or equipment.\n\n(2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.",
      "skos:definition": "equipment\n\n(1) If an inspector seizes consumer goods or equipment under a search\nwarrant:\n\n(a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized, or\nthe equipment was seized; or\n\n(b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods or\nequipment—the owner of the consumer goods or equipment;\nis liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by\nthe inspector in seizing the consumer goods or equipment.\n\n(2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135q-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c09f5a7f47df2ee11dac3abd4010d9b70fb62c46446fd0c872c67a37609a52d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135Q Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing consumer goods or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "equipment\n\n(1) If an inspector seizes consumer goods or equipment under a search\nwarrant:\n\n(a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized, or\nthe equipment was seized; or\n\n(b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods or\nequipment—the owner of the consumer goods or equipment;\nis liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by\nthe inspector in seizing the consumer goods or equipment.\n\n(2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):\n\n(a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and\n\n(b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent\njurisdiction."
    },
