    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135T Embargo period for embargo notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.167",
      "values:originalText": "Embargo period\n\n(1) Subject to this section, the embargo period for an embargo notice\nmust not be longer than:\n\n(a) if the inspector giving the notice secures consumer goods\nunder section 135V or secures equipment under\nsection 135W—24 hours; or\n\n(b) otherwise—28 days.\nExtensions of embargo period\n\n(2) An inspector may, before the embargo period ends, apply to a\njudge of the Federal Court for an extension of the period.\n\n(3) If an inspector intends to make an application under subsection (2),\nthe inspector must, before making the application, notify the\noccupier of the premises to which the embargo notice relates of\nthat intention.\n\n(4) The occupier of the premises is entitled to be heard in relation to\nthe application.\n\n(5) The judge may extend the embargo period for a specified period if\nthe judge is satisfied that the extension is necessary in all the\ncircumstances.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Embargo period\n\n(1) Subject to this section, the embargo period for an embargo notice\nmust not be longer than:\n\n(a) if the inspector giving the notice secures consumer goods\nunder section 135V or secures equipment under\nsection 135W—24 hours; or\n\n(b) otherwise—28 days.\nExtensions of embargo period\n\n(2) An inspector may, before the embargo period ends, apply to a\njudge of the Federal Court for an extension of the period.\n\n(3) If an inspector intends to make an application under subsection (2),\nthe inspector must, before making the application, notify the\noccupier of the premises to which the embargo notice relates of\nthat intention.\n\n(4) The occupier of the premises is entitled to be heard in relation to\nthe application.\n\n(5) The judge may extend the embargo period for a specified period if\nthe judge is satisfied that the extension is necessary in all the\ncircumstances.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135t-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135t-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135t-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135t-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5240fa679154beae0c897b76ada40ae4df0dd37cf1fdc6b47364b6d545727b73"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135T Embargo period for embargo notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 167,
      "values:originalText": "Embargo period\n\n(1) Subject to this section, the embargo period for an embargo notice\nmust not be longer than:\n\n(a) if the inspector giving the notice secures consumer goods\nunder section 135V or secures equipment under\nsection 135W—24 hours; or\n\n(b) otherwise—28 days.\nExtensions of embargo period\n\n(2) An inspector may, before the embargo period ends, apply to a\njudge of the Federal Court for an extension of the period.\n\n(3) If an inspector intends to make an application under subsection (2),\nthe inspector must, before making the application, notify the\noccupier of the premises to which the embargo notice relates of\nthat intention.\n\n(4) The occupier of the premises is entitled to be heard in relation to\nthe application.\n\n(5) The judge may extend the embargo period for a specified period if\nthe judge is satisfied that the extension is necessary in all the\ncircumstances.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
