      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Inspector must not give embargo notice if earlier notice has not ended at least 5 days ago",
      "cml:conclusionText": "CogAI application for embargo notices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135V Power of inspectors to secure consumer goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) an embargo notice relates to consumer goods; and\n\n(b) the inspector who gives the notice believes on reasonable\ngrounds that it is necessary to secure the consumer goods in\norder to ensure that the notice is complied with;\nthe inspector may, during the embargo period for the embargo\nnotice, do anything that the inspector thinks is necessary to secure\nthose consumer goods (whether by locking them up, placing a\nguard or otherwise).",
      "skos:definition": "If:\n\n(a) an embargo notice relates to consumer goods; and\n\n(b) the inspector who gives the notice believes on reasonable\ngrounds that it is necessary to secure the consumer goods in\norder to ensure that the notice is complied with;\nthe inspector may, during the embargo period for the embargo\nnotice, do anything that the inspector thinks is necessary to secure\nthose consumer goods (whether by locking them up, placing a\nguard or otherwise).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135v-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135v-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b8dc252442188c8f8c954ec27f7209a00e783f1f30ddaa76fe69e5d323b4535",
      "skos:note": "Inspector may take actions to secure consumer goods during embargo period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135V Power of inspectors to secure consumer goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) an embargo notice relates to consumer goods; and\n\n(b) the inspector who gives the notice believes on reasonable\ngrounds that it is necessary to secure the consumer goods in\norder to ensure that the notice is complied with;\nthe inspector may, during the embargo period for the embargo\nnotice, do anything that the inspector thinks is necessary to secure\nthose consumer goods (whether by locking them up, placing a\nguard or otherwise)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135v-norm",
