    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135Z(2) Issue of search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135z-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The judge may issue the warrant if:\n\n(a) an affidavit has been given to the judge setting out the\ngrounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought;\nand\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 136\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the applicant, or some other person, has given to the judge\nsuch further information (if any) as the judge requires\nconcerning the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is\nbeing sought; and\n\n(c) the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for\nissuing the warrant.\nContent of warrant",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The judge may issue the warrant if:\n\n(a) an affidavit has been given to the judge setting out the\ngrounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought;\nand\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 136\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the applicant, or some other person, has given to the judge\nsuch further information (if any) as the judge requires\nconcerning the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is\nbeing sought; and\n\n(c) the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for\nissuing the warrant.\nContent of warrant",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-epistemic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3ec48d178b59a449df9262dc2879a21f08236c81153a5d0b8b716a104911a91d",
      "skos:note": "Grounds for issuing a search warrant",
      "dc:description": "(a) an affidavit has been given to the judge setting out the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought; (b) the applicant, or some other person, has given to the judge such further information (if any) as the judge requires concerning the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135z-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135Z(2) Issue of search warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The judge may issue the warrant if:\n\n(a) an affidavit has been given to the judge setting out the\ngrounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought;\nand\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nSearch, seizure and entry  Division 6\n\nSection 136\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the applicant, or some other person, has given to the judge\nsuch further information (if any) as the judge requires\nconcerning the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is\nbeing sought; and\n\n(c) the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for\nissuing the warrant.\nContent of warrant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Necessity",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Affidavit and further information must be provided",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) an affidavit has been given to the judge setting out the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought; (b) the applicant, or some other person, has given to the judge such further information (if any) as the judge requires concerning the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(a) and (b)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Necessity",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Judge must be satisfied with reasonable grounds for issuing the warrant",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for issuing the warrant",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(c)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-epistemic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Epistemic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Belief",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Judge must believe in reasonable grounds for issuing the warrant",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::epistemic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for issuing the warrant",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(c)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurring Trace",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Warrant must be issued in a recurring trace of events leading to its issuance",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Judge must issue the warrant if reasonable grounds exist",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for issuing the warrant",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(c)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135Z(3) Issue of search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135z-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(a) specify the purpose for which the warrant is issued; and\n\n(b) describe the premises to which the warrant relates; and\n\n(c) state that the warrant is issued under this section; and\n\n(d) name one or more inspectors; and\n\n(e) authorise the inspector or inspectors so named:\n\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n\n(ii) to exercise search-related powers in relation to the\npremises; and\n\n(f) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night, or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n\n(g) specify a day (which must not be more than 7 days after the\nday the warrant is issued) on which the warrant ceases to be\nin force.\n136  Search warrants by telephone, fax etc.\nApplication for warrant",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(a) specify the purpose for which the warrant is issued; and\n\n(b) describe the premises to which the warrant relates; and\n\n(c) state that the warrant is issued under this section; and\n\n(d) name one or more inspectors; and\n\n(e) authorise the inspector or inspectors so named:\n\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n\n(ii) to exercise search-related powers in relation to the\npremises; and\n\n(f) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night, or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n\n(g) specify a day (which must not be more than 7 days after the\nday the warrant is issued) on which the warrant ceases to be\nin force.\n136  Search warrants by telephone, fax etc.\nApplication for warrant",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b20be180bad7681f3137e44af091a9aeed1b0c3327cb72b56fe6a13bcd9966c4",
      "skos:note": "Warrant must specify purpose, premises, and inspectors",
      "dc:description": "a, b, c, d, e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135z-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135Z(3) Issue of search warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(a) specify the purpose for which the warrant is issued; and\n\n(b) describe the premises to which the warrant relates; and\n\n(c) state that the warrant is issued under this section; and\n\n(d) name one or more inspectors; and\n\n(e) authorise the inspector or inspectors so named:\n\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n\n(ii) to exercise search-related powers in relation to the\npremises; and\n\n(f) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night, or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n\n(g) specify a day (which must not be more than 7 days after the\nday the warrant is issued) on which the warrant ceases to be\nin force.\n136  Search warrants by telephone, fax etc.\nApplication for warrant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires specification of purpose and premises",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(a) specify the purpose for which the warrant is issued; and\n\n(b) describe the premises to which the warrant relates;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The warrant must specify the purpose and premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires naming of inspectors",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(d) name one or more inspectors;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The warrant must name the inspectors."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires authorisation of search powers",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(e) authorise the inspector or inspectors so named:\n\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n\n(ii) to exercise search-related powers in relation to the\npremises;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The warrant must authorise the search powers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires specification of entry times",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(f) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night, or during specified hours of the day or\nnight;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The warrant must specify the entry times."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-3-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires specification of warrant validity period",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The warrant must:\n\n(g) specify a day (which must not be more than 7 days after the\nday the warrant is issued) on which the warrant ceases to be\nin force.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The warrant must specify its validity period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135Z(1) Issue of search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135z-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector may apply to a judge of the Federal Court by\ntelephone, fax or other electronic means for a warrant under\nsection 135Z in relation to premises if the inspector believes on\nreasonable grounds that the delay that would occur if an\napplication were made in person would frustrate the effective\nexecution of the warrant.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An inspector may apply to a judge of the Federal Court by\ntelephone, fax or other electronic means for a warrant under\nsection 135Z in relation to premises if the inspector believes on\nreasonable grounds that the delay that would occur if an\napplication were made in person would frustrate the effective\nexecution of the warrant.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-1-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f95c515f3c30e1f59282fd1abf4bfe05df6c4e8c0d0fccb8dcf2df8e504cc2d7",
      "skos:note": "Inspector may apply for warrant by phone or fax under certain circumstances. An inspector may apply to a judge for a warrant in relation to premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-135z-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135Z(1) Issue of search warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector may apply to a judge of the Federal Court by\ntelephone, fax or other electronic means for a warrant under\nsection 135Z in relation to premises if the inspector believes on\nreasonable grounds that the delay that would occur if an\napplication were made in person would frustrate the effective\nexecution of the warrant.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135z-ss-1-norm",
