    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-136b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "136B Powers of judges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-136b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "Powers conferred personally\n\n(1) A power conferred on a judge by this Division is conferred on the\njudge:\n\n(a) in a personal capacity; and\n\n(b) not as a court or a member of a court.\nPowers need not be accepted\n\n(2) The judge need not accept the power conferred.\nProtection and immunity\n\n(3) A judge exercising a power conferred by this Division has the\nsame protection and immunity as if he or she were exercising the\npower:\n\n(a) as the court of which the judge is a member; or\n\n(b) as a member of the court of which the judge is a member.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nRemedies  Division 7\n\nSection 137\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "Powers conferred personally\n\n(1) A power conferred on a judge by this Division is conferred on the\njudge:\n\n(a) in a personal capacity; and\n\n(b) not as a court or a member of a court.\nPowers need not be accepted\n\n(2) The judge need not accept the power conferred.\nProtection and immunity\n\n(3) A judge exercising a power conferred by this Division has the\nsame protection and immunity as if he or she were exercising the\npower:\n\n(a) as the court of which the judge is a member; or\n\n(b) as a member of the court of which the judge is a member.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nRemedies  Division 7\n\nSection 137\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-136b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-136b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-136b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a3d9ce38f203e8b183955c1df3c707be225fa24ea2ebd96628bb6f45dc1fcae0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-136b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "136B Powers of judges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "Powers conferred personally\n\n(1) A power conferred on a judge by this Division is conferred on the\njudge:\n\n(a) in a personal capacity; and\n\n(b) not as a court or a member of a court.\nPowers need not be accepted\n\n(2) The judge need not accept the power conferred.\nProtection and immunity\n\n(3) A judge exercising a power conferred by this Division has the\nsame protection and immunity as if he or she were exercising the\npower:\n\n(a) as the court of which the judge is a member; or\n\n(b) as a member of the court of which the judge is a member.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nRemedies  Division 7\n\nSection 137\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
