    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "137A Contributory acts or omissions to reduce compensation in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-137a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "defective goods actions\n\n(1) If the loss or damage to which a defective goods action under\nsection 138 or 139 of the Australian Consumer Law relates was\ncaused by both:\n\n(a) an act or omission of:\n\n(i) the individual who suffers the injuries referred to in that\nsection; or\n\n(ii) a person for whom that individual is responsible; and\n\n(b) a safety defect of the goods to which the action relates;\nthe amount of the loss or damage is to be reduced to such extent\n(which may be to nil) as the court thinks fit having regard to that\nindividual’s share in the responsibility for the loss or damage.\n\n(2) If the loss or damage to which a defective goods action under\nsection 140 or 141 of the Australian Consumer Law relates was\ncaused by both:\n\n(a) an act or omission of:\n\n(i) the person who suffered the loss or damage; or\n\n(ii) another person for whom that person is responsible; and\n\n(b) a safety defect of the goods to which the action relates;\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nRemedies  Division 7\n\nSection 137B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe amount of the loss or damage is to be reduced to such extent\n(which may be to nil) as the court thinks fit having regard to the\nperson’s share in the responsibility for the loss or damage.",
      "skos:definition": "defective goods actions\n\n(1) If the loss or damage to which a defective goods action under\nsection 138 or 139 of the Australian Consumer Law relates was\ncaused by both:\n\n(a) an act or omission of:\n\n(i) the individual who suffers the injuries referred to in that\nsection; or\n\n(ii) a person for whom that individual is responsible; and\n\n(b) a safety defect of the goods to which the action relates;\nthe amount of the loss or damage is to be reduced to such extent\n(which may be to nil) as the court thinks fit having regard to that\nindividual’s share in the responsibility for the loss or damage.\n\n(2) If the loss or damage to which a defective goods action under\nsection 140 or 141 of the Australian Consumer Law relates was\ncaused by both:\n\n(a) an act or omission of:\n\n(i) the person who suffered the loss or damage; or\n\n(ii) another person for whom that person is responsible; and\n\n(b) a safety defect of the goods to which the action relates;\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nRemedies  Division 7\n\nSection 137B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe amount of the loss or damage is to be reduced to such extent\n(which may be to nil) as the court thinks fit having regard to the\nperson’s share in the responsibility for the loss or damage.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b4b29e048e97e288f4edb153cef8ec8605858679bb00e7619c83d08b8729b4e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-137a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "137A Contributory acts or omissions to reduce compensation in",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "defective goods actions\n\n(1) If the loss or damage to which a defective goods action under\nsection 138 or 139 of the Australian Consumer Law relates was\ncaused by both:\n\n(a) an act or omission of:\n\n(i) the individual who suffers the injuries referred to in that\nsection; or\n\n(ii) a person for whom that individual is responsible; and\n\n(b) a safety defect of the goods to which the action relates;\nthe amount of the loss or damage is to be reduced to such extent\n(which may be to nil) as the court thinks fit having regard to that\nindividual’s share in the responsibility for the loss or damage.\n\n(2) If the loss or damage to which a defective goods action under\nsection 140 or 141 of the Australian Consumer Law relates was\ncaused by both:\n\n(a) an act or omission of:\n\n(i) the person who suffered the loss or damage; or\n\n(ii) another person for whom that person is responsible; and\n\n(b) a safety defect of the goods to which the action relates;\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nRemedies  Division 7\n\nSection 137B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nthe amount of the loss or damage is to be reduced to such extent\n(which may be to nil) as the court thinks fit having regard to the\nperson’s share in the responsibility for the loss or damage."
    },
