      "cml:integrityHash": "41a6526a6e7db85019ae5ddf4e0639d1fbac31f21ba9b7bdf6446c69ad0eb34a",
      "skos:note": "Court may consider conduct of parties in determining whether to make an order under the Australian Consumer Law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-137d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "137D Compensation orders etc. arising out of unconscionable",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "conduct or unfair contract term\n\nIn determining whether to make an order under subsection 237(1)\nor 238(1) of the Australian Consumer Law in relation to a\ncontravention of a provision of Part 2-2 or 2-3 of the Australian\nConsumer Law, the court may have regard to the conduct of the\nparties to the proceeding referred to in that subsection since the\ncontravention occurred."
    },
