    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "138 Conferring jurisdiction on the Federal Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-138"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.185",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Jurisdiction is conferred on the Federal Court in relation to any\nmatter arising under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law in\nrespect of which a civil proceeding has been instituted under this\nPart or the Australian Consumer Law.\n\n(2) The jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1) on the Federal Court is\nexclusive of the jurisdiction of any other court other than:\n\n(a) the jurisdiction of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) under section 138A; and\n\n(b) the jurisdiction of the several courts of the States and\nTerritories under section 138B; and\n\n(c) the jurisdiction of the High Court under section 75 of the\nConstitution.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Jurisdiction is conferred on the Federal Court in relation to any\nmatter arising under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law in\nrespect of which a civil proceeding has been instituted under this\nPart or the Australian Consumer Law.\n\n(2) The jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1) on the Federal Court is\nexclusive of the jurisdiction of any other court other than:\n\n(a) the jurisdiction of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) under section 138A; and\n\n(b) the jurisdiction of the several courts of the States and\nTerritories under section 138B; and\n\n(c) the jurisdiction of the High Court under section 75 of the\nConstitution.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "01f0f566b7d4a1ccc3c8bb2dd6d8e3b00ba7b077522598c2a0b1f8618c8af7c7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-138",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "138 Conferring jurisdiction on the Federal Court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 185,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Jurisdiction is conferred on the Federal Court in relation to any\nmatter arising under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law in\nrespect of which a civil proceeding has been instituted under this\nPart or the Australian Consumer Law.\n\n(2) The jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1) on the Federal Court is\nexclusive of the jurisdiction of any other court other than:\n\n(a) the jurisdiction of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) under section 138A; and\n\n(b) the jurisdiction of the several courts of the States and\nTerritories under section 138B; and\n\n(c) the jurisdiction of the High Court under section 75 of the\nConstitution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138-ss-1",
