      "skos:definition": "(2) If proceedings under Part 3-5, or section 236, of the Australian\nConsumer Law are instituted in, or transferred to, the Federal\nCircuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2), the Court does\nnot have jurisdiction to award an amount for loss or damage that\nexceeds:\n\n(a) $750,000; or\n\n(b) if another amount is specified in the regulations—that other\namount.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
