    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "138D Transfer of matters by a State or Territory court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-138d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.187",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a proceeding is pending in a court (other than the Supreme\nCourt) of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this\nPart or the Australian Consumer Law, other than under\nChapter 4 of the Australian Consumer Law.\n\n(2) The court must, if directed to do so by the Federal Court, transfer\nto the Federal Court:\n\n(a) the matter; and\n\n(b) such other matters for determination in the proceeding, the\ndetermination of which would (apart from any law of a State\nor of the Northern Territory relating to cross-vesting of\njurisdiction) be within the jurisdiction of the Federal Court,\nas the Federal Court determines.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a proceeding is pending in a court (other than the Supreme\nCourt) of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this\nPart or the Australian Consumer Law, other than under\nChapter 4 of the Australian Consumer Law.\n\n(2) The court must, if directed to do so by the Federal Court, transfer\nto the Federal Court:\n\n(a) the matter; and\n\n(b) such other matters for determination in the proceeding, the\ndetermination of which would (apart from any law of a State\nor of the Northern Territory relating to cross-vesting of\njurisdiction) be within the jurisdiction of the Federal Court,\nas the Federal Court determines.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7febf2ae73eaa074feac9bbb625fff052c9f4a893c74763c1c344a502d8aa5a4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-138d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "138D Transfer of matters by a State or Territory court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 187,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a proceeding is pending in a court (other than the Supreme\nCourt) of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this\nPart or the Australian Consumer Law, other than under\nChapter 4 of the Australian Consumer Law.\n\n(2) The court must, if directed to do so by the Federal Court, transfer\nto the Federal Court:\n\n(a) the matter; and\n\n(b) such other matters for determination in the proceeding, the\ndetermination of which would (apart from any law of a State\nor of the Northern Territory relating to cross-vesting of\njurisdiction) be within the jurisdiction of the Federal Court,\nas the Federal Court determines.\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
