    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139B Conduct of directors, employees or agents of bodies corporate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.192",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, in a proceeding under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law\nin respect of conduct that is engaged in by a body corporate and to\nwhich this Part or the Australian Consumer Law applies, it is\nnecessary to establish the state of mind of the body corporate, it is\nsufficient to show:\n\n(a) that a director, employee or agent of the body corporate\nengaged in that conduct within the scope of the actual or\napparent authority of the director, employee or agent; and\n\n(b) that the director, employee or agent had that state of mind.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nMiscellaneous  Division 9\n\nSection 139C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a body corporate:\n\n(a) by a director, employee or agent of the body corporate within\nthe scope of the actual or apparent authority of the director,\nemployee or agent; or\n\n(b) by any other person:\n\n(i) at the direction of a director, employee or agent of the\nbody corporate; or\n\n(ii) with the consent or agreement (whether express or\nimplied) of such a director, employee or agent;\n\nif the giving of the direction, consent or agreement is within\nthe scope of the actual or apparent authority of the director,\nemployee or agent;\nis taken, for the purposes of this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw, to have been engaged in also by the body corporate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, in a proceeding under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law\nin respect of conduct that is engaged in by a body corporate and to\nwhich this Part or the Australian Consumer Law applies, it is\nnecessary to establish the state of mind of the body corporate, it is\nsufficient to show:\n\n(a) that a director, employee or agent of the body corporate\nengaged in that conduct within the scope of the actual or\napparent authority of the director, employee or agent; and\n\n(b) that the director, employee or agent had that state of mind.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nMiscellaneous  Division 9\n\nSection 139C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a body corporate:\n\n(a) by a director, employee or agent of the body corporate within\nthe scope of the actual or apparent authority of the director,\nemployee or agent; or\n\n(b) by any other person:\n\n(i) at the direction of a director, employee or agent of the\nbody corporate; or\n\n(ii) with the consent or agreement (whether express or\nimplied) of such a director, employee or agent;\n\nif the giving of the direction, consent or agreement is within\nthe scope of the actual or apparent authority of the director,\nemployee or agent;\nis taken, for the purposes of this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw, to have been engaged in also by the body corporate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b8c8546ed7f37f38594fd4bb92df46751c2aed6fa99304376d57d71825449d1e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "139B Conduct of directors, employees or agents of bodies corporate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 192,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, in a proceeding under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law\nin respect of conduct that is engaged in by a body corporate and to\nwhich this Part or the Australian Consumer Law applies, it is\nnecessary to establish the state of mind of the body corporate, it is\nsufficient to show:\n\n(a) that a director, employee or agent of the body corporate\nengaged in that conduct within the scope of the actual or\napparent authority of the director, employee or agent; and\n\n(b) that the director, employee or agent had that state of mind.\n\nOther provisions  Chapter 6\nApplication of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI\nMiscellaneous  Division 9\n\nSection 139C\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a body corporate:\n\n(a) by a director, employee or agent of the body corporate within\nthe scope of the actual or apparent authority of the director,\nemployee or agent; or\n\n(b) by any other person:\n\n(i) at the direction of a director, employee or agent of the\nbody corporate; or\n\n(ii) with the consent or agreement (whether express or\nimplied) of such a director, employee or agent;\n\nif the giving of the direction, consent or agreement is within\nthe scope of the actual or apparent authority of the director,\nemployee or agent;\nis taken, for the purposes of this Part or the Australian Consumer\nLaw, to have been engaged in also by the body corporate."
    },
