      "cml:operator": "if-then",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conditional obligation discharge",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If person pays instalments, then enforcement order is discharged.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Enforcement order is discharged if person pays instalments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139d-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139D(6) Enforcement and recovery of certain fines",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139d-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.194",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The term of a sentence of imprisonment imposed by an order under\na law of a State or a Territory applied by section 15A of the Crimes\nAct 1914 (including an order described in subsection 15A(1AA) of\nthat Act) in respect of a fine is to be calculated at the rate of one\nday’s imprisonment for each $25 of the amount of the fine that is\nfrom time to time unpaid.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The term of a sentence of imprisonment imposed by an order under\na law of a State or a Territory applied by section 15A of the Crimes\nAct 1914 (including an order described in subsection 15A(1AA) of\nthat Act) in respect of a fine is to be calculated at the rate of one\nday’s imprisonment for each $25 of the amount of the fine that is\nfrom time to time unpaid.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139d-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139d-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "415a79a1376119154438aafd030d279d8a85a50a0247c2a00b6d8f6e2ce4167b",
      "skos:note": "Term of imprisonment for unpaid fine"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139d-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "139D(6) Enforcement and recovery of certain fines",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 194,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The term of a sentence of imprisonment imposed by an order under\na law of a State or a Territory applied by section 15A of the Crimes\nAct 1914 (including an order described in subsection 15A(1AA) of\nthat Act) in respect of a fine is to be calculated at the rate of one\nday’s imprisonment for each $25 of the amount of the fine that is\nfrom time to time unpaid."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139d-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139d-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
