    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139F Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.197",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the operation of this Part (including Schedule 2 as applied by this\nPart) would result in an acquisition of property from a person\notherwise than on just terms, the Commonwealth is liable to pay a\nreasonable amount of compensation to the person.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the operation of this Part (including Schedule 2 as applied by this\nPart) would result in an acquisition of property from a person\notherwise than on just terms, the Commonwealth is liable to pay a\nreasonable amount of compensation to the person.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a5f8bdc55527b23a1deb4ceac288cc2b6d5a7e063d991a6eee52f13d3934c2d5"
    },
    {
