    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139G Regulations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.197",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by Schedule 2 to be prescribed; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to that Schedule.\n\n(2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes\nof paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a\ncontract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the\nCommonwealth Minister must take into consideration:\n\n(a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to\nconsumers; and\n\n(aa) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to persons\nwho carry on a business and employ fewer than 100 persons;\nand\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by Schedule 2 to be prescribed; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to that Schedule.\n\n(2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes\nof paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a\ncontract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the\nCommonwealth Minister must take into consideration:\n\n(a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to\nconsumers; and\n\n(aa) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to persons\nwho carry on a business and employ fewer than 100 persons;\nand\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8550b46387c223a65657e907cb14c466e8fc8aebfbec44ca69d6302e737f8100"
    },
    {
