      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "75ff3c416d5a5023e0c85940f0311771befd4b8616800901bc285159669ca88a",
      "skos:note": "Consider detriment to consumers and persons with fewer than 100 employees when making regulations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-139g-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "139G(2) Regulations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 197,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes\nof paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a\ncontract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the\nCommonwealth Minister must take into consideration:\n\n(a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to\nconsumers; and\n\n(aa) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to persons\nwho carry on a business and employ fewer than 100 persons;\nand\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139g-ss-2-norm",
