      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.203",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Subsections (1) to (5) do not limit section 140E.\n140G  When an application law imposes a duty\n\nFor the purposes of this Part, an application law imposes a duty on\na Commonwealth entity if:\n\n(a) the law confers a function or power on the entity; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which the function or power is\nconferred give rise to an obligation on the entity to perform\nthe function or to exercise the power.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Subsections (1) to (5) do not limit section 140E.\n140G  When an application law imposes a duty\n\nFor the purposes of this Part, an application law imposes a duty on\na Commonwealth entity if:\n\n(a) the law confers a function or power on the entity; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which the function or power is\nconferred give rise to an obligation on the entity to perform\nthe function or to exercise the power.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-140f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-140f-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-140f-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2832342ce6713c704b67471b791d7fae0d14ee35818255f3538c844f12ea574b",
      "skos:note": "Application law imposes a duty on Commonwealth entity if it confers a function or power."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-140f-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "140F(6) How duty is imposed",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 203,
      "values:originalText": "(6) Subsections (1) to (5) do not limit section 140E.\n140G  When an application law imposes a duty\n\nFor the purposes of this Part, an application law imposes a duty on\na Commonwealth entity if:\n\n(a) the law confers a function or power on the entity; and\n\n(b) the circumstances in which the function or power is\nconferred give rise to an obligation on the entity to perform\nthe function or to exercise the power."
    },
