    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-150fa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "150FA How duty is imposed",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-150fa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.209",
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) This section applies if an application law purports to impose a duty\non a Commonwealth entity.\nNote:\nSection 150FB sets out when such a law imposes a duty on a\nCommonwealth entity.\nState or Territory legislative power sufficient to support duty\n\n(2) The duty is taken not to be imposed by this Act (or any other law\nof the Commonwealth) to the extent to which:\n\n(a) imposing the duty is within the legislative powers of the State\nor Territory concerned; and\n\n(b) imposing the duty by the law of the State or Territory is\nconsistent with the constitutional doctrines restricting the\nduties that may be imposed on the entity.\nNote:\nIf this subsection applies, the duty will be taken to be imposed by\nforce of the law of the State or Territory (the Commonwealth having\nconsented under section 150F to the imposition of the duty by that\nlaw).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Application\n\n(1) This section applies if an application law purports to impose a duty\non a Commonwealth entity.\nNote:\nSection 150FB sets out when such a law imposes a duty on a\nCommonwealth entity.\nState or Territory legislative power sufficient to support duty\n\n(2) The duty is taken not to be imposed by this Act (or any other law\nof the Commonwealth) to the extent to which:\n\n(a) imposing the duty is within the legislative powers of the State\nor Territory concerned; and\n\n(b) imposing the duty by the law of the State or Territory is\nconsistent with the constitutional doctrines restricting the\nduties that may be imposed on the entity.\nNote:\nIf this subsection applies, the duty will be taken to be imposed by\nforce of the law of the State or Territory (the Commonwealth having\nconsented under section 150F to the imposition of the duty by that\nlaw).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-150fa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-150fa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7ad522ea327e5ba95534ef8355038ef7f7b86328c7cf9175886f60464c40d28"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-150fa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "150FA How duty is imposed",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 209,
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) This section applies if an application law purports to impose a duty\non a Commonwealth entity.\nNote:\nSection 150FB sets out when such a law imposes a duty on a\nCommonwealth entity.\nState or Territory legislative power sufficient to support duty\n\n(2) The duty is taken not to be imposed by this Act (or any other law\nof the Commonwealth) to the extent to which:\n\n(a) imposing the duty is within the legislative powers of the State\nor Territory concerned; and\n\n(b) imposing the duty by the law of the State or Territory is\nconsistent with the constitutional doctrines restricting the\nduties that may be imposed on the entity.\nNote:\nIf this subsection applies, the duty will be taken to be imposed by\nforce of the law of the State or Territory (the Commonwealth having\nconsented under section 150F to the imposition of the duty by that\nlaw).\n\nChapter 6  Other provisions"
    },
