    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151as",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151AS Exemption orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151as"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.233",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may apply to the Commission for an order exempting\nspecified conduct of the person from the scope of section 151AJ\n(which deals with anti-competitive conduct). The order is called an\nexemption order.\n\n(2) An exemption order is not invalid only because the conduct\nspecified in the order is conduct of a kind that, apart from the\norder, is outside the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with\nanti-competitive conduct).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may apply to the Commission for an order exempting\nspecified conduct of the person from the scope of section 151AJ\n(which deals with anti-competitive conduct). The order is called an\nexemption order.\n\n(2) An exemption order is not invalid only because the conduct\nspecified in the order is conduct of a kind that, apart from the\norder, is outside the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with\nanti-competitive conduct).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151as-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151as-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "429b00672cc9c533846f9efc5a7e18b1eaa3e3d01a32328306336a689dfb9a0f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151as",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151AS Exemption orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 233,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may apply to the Commission for an order exempting\nspecified conduct of the person from the scope of section 151AJ\n(which deals with anti-competitive conduct). The order is called an\nexemption order.\n\n(2) An exemption order is not invalid only because the conduct\nspecified in the order is conduct of a kind that, apart from the\norder, is outside the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with\nanti-competitive conduct)."
    },
