        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) the Commission receives, or has received, an application for\nan exemption order; and\n\n(b) the Commission receives, or has received, a notice under\nsubsection 93(1) or 93AB(1A) or (1);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Commission's refusal diffuses to the public."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ay-ss-1-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "infer",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Commission's refusal inferences about application and notice.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the Commission receives, or has received, an application for\nan exemption order; and\n(b) the Commission receives, or has received, a notice under\nsubsection 93(1) or 93AB(1A) or (1);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Commission's refusal infers about the application and notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ay-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151AY(2) Commission may refuse to consider application if it relates to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ay-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.235",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Commission may refuse to:\n\n(a) consider the application for the exemption order; or\n\n(b) convene a conference under section 151AZ to discuss the\napplication for the exemption order;\nuntil:\n\n(c) the Commission decides whether or not to give a notice\nunder subsection 93(3) or (3A) or 93AC(1) or (2); or\n\n(d) if the Commission gives such a notice—the expiry of the\ntime limit allowed for a person to apply to the Tribunal for\nreview of the decision; or\n\n(e) if a person applies to the Tribunal for a review of the\ndecision—the review (including any court proceedings\narising out of the review) is finalised.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Commission may refuse to:\n\n(a) consider the application for the exemption order; or\n\n(b) convene a conference under section 151AZ to discuss the\napplication for the exemption order;\nuntil:\n\n(c) the Commission decides whether or not to give a notice\nunder subsection 93(3) or (3A) or 93AC(1) or (2); or\n\n(d) if the Commission gives such a notice—the expiry of the\ntime limit allowed for a person to apply to the Tribunal for\nreview of the decision; or\n\n(e) if a person applies to the Tribunal for a review of the\ndecision—the review (including any court proceedings\narising out of the review) is finalised.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ay"
      },
