      "cml:premiseText": "if a person applies to the Tribunal for a review of the decision—the review (including any court proceedings arising out of the review) is finalised."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151az",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151AZ Commission may convene conference to discuss application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151az"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.236",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission receives an application for an exemption order,\nthe Commission may convene a conference to discuss the\napplication.\n\n(2) If the Commission decides to convene a conference, the\nCommission must give:\n\n(a) the applicant (or a representative of the applicant); and\n\n(b) any other persons whom the Commission considers\ninterested;\na reasonable opportunity to attend and take part in the conference.\n\n(3) This Act does not prevent a conference under this section from\nbeing combined with a conference under section 90A or 93A if the\ncombined conference relates to the same conduct.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission receives an application for an exemption order,\nthe Commission may convene a conference to discuss the\napplication.\n\n(2) If the Commission decides to convene a conference, the\nCommission must give:\n\n(a) the applicant (or a representative of the applicant); and\n\n(b) any other persons whom the Commission considers\ninterested;\na reasonable opportunity to attend and take part in the conference.\n\n(3) This Act does not prevent a conference under this section from\nbeing combined with a conference under section 90A or 93A if the\ncombined conference relates to the same conduct.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151az-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151az-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151az-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ad0a6e87a6c3a1c55aa43d9a6eb8a7b172840f48161f0a96601d7139ad5c9609"
    },
