    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151bz",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151BZ Criminal proceedings not to be brought for contraventions of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151bz"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.268",
      "values:originalText": "the competition rule, record-keeping rules or disclosure\ndirections\n\n(1) Criminal proceedings do not lie against a person only because the\nperson:\n\n(a) has contravened the competition rule, a record-keeping rule\nor a disclosure direction; or\n\n(b) has attempted to contravene the competition rule, a\nrecord-keeping rule or a disclosure direction; or\n\n(c) has been involved in a contravention of the competition rule,\na record-keeping rule or a disclosure direction.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to\nproceedings for an offence against section 45AF or 45AG.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules",
      "skos:definition": "the competition rule, record-keeping rules or disclosure\ndirections\n\n(1) Criminal proceedings do not lie against a person only because the\nperson:\n\n(a) has contravened the competition rule, a record-keeping rule\nor a disclosure direction; or\n\n(b) has attempted to contravene the competition rule, a\nrecord-keeping rule or a disclosure direction; or\n\n(c) has been involved in a contravention of the competition rule,\na record-keeping rule or a disclosure direction.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to\nproceedings for an offence against section 45AF or 45AG.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151bz-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151bz-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1381628577af3decc84758eabda18d8e0bdf35329660a535ad00547a99162183"
    },
