        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.269",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) an application for an injunction under subsection (1) has been\nmade; and\n\n(b) the Court determines it to be appropriate to do so;\nthe Court may grant an injunction by consent of all the parties to\nthe proceedings, whether or not the Court is satisfied that a person\nhas engaged, or is proposing to engage, in conduct of a kind\nmentioned in subsection (1).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n\n(a) an application for an injunction under subsection (1) has been\nmade; and\n\n(b) the Court determines it to be appropriate to do so;\nthe Court may grant an injunction by consent of all the parties to\nthe proceedings, whether or not the Court is satisfied that a person\nhas engaged, or is proposing to engage, in conduct of a kind\nmentioned in subsection (1).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ca"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ca-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ca-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b94d01d5cd2b92b5ff430253bc4ba2066288a7422553f9a1e6d1c71288f39300",
      "skos:note": "Court may grant injunction by consent of all parties to proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ca-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151CA(2) Injunctions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 269,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) an application for an injunction under subsection (1) has been\nmade; and\n\n(b) the Court determines it to be appropriate to do so;\nthe Court may grant an injunction by consent of all the parties to\nthe proceedings, whether or not the Court is satisfied that a person\nhas engaged, or is proposing to engage, in conduct of a kind\nmentioned in subsection (1).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
