    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ce",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151CE Other orders—compensation for breach of the competition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ce"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.272",
      "values:originalText": "rule\n\n(1) If, in a proceeding instituted under this Division in relation to a\ncontravention of the competition rule, the Federal Court finds that\na person who is a party to the proceeding has suffered, or is likely\nto suffer, loss or damage by conduct of another person that was\nengaged in in contravention of the competition rule, the Court may,\non the application of a party to the proceedings, make such orders\nas it thinks appropriate against:\n\n(a) the person who engaged in the conduct; or\n\n(b) a person who was involved in the contravention;\nif the Court considers that the orders concerned will:\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules",
      "skos:definition": "rule\n\n(1) If, in a proceeding instituted under this Division in relation to a\ncontravention of the competition rule, the Federal Court finds that\na person who is a party to the proceeding has suffered, or is likely\nto suffer, loss or damage by conduct of another person that was\nengaged in in contravention of the competition rule, the Court may,\non the application of a party to the proceedings, make such orders\nas it thinks appropriate against:\n\n(a) the person who engaged in the conduct; or\n\n(b) a person who was involved in the contravention;\nif the Court considers that the orders concerned will:\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ce-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ce-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a26067d2963c6c4211b98e3abd8e7d38f4559f140271a8358534b7f52eda0e6b",
      "skos:note": "Court may make orders against a person who engaged in contravention of the competition rule or a person involved in the contravention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ce",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151CE Other orders—compensation for breach of the competition",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 272,
      "values:originalText": "rule\n\n(1) If, in a proceeding instituted under this Division in relation to a\ncontravention of the competition rule, the Federal Court finds that\na person who is a party to the proceeding has suffered, or is likely\nto suffer, loss or damage by conduct of another person that was\nengaged in in contravention of the competition rule, the Court may,\non the application of a party to the proceedings, make such orders\nas it thinks appropriate against:\n\n(a) the person who engaged in the conduct; or\n\n(b) a person who was involved in the contravention;\nif the Court considers that the orders concerned will:\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules"
    },
