    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ch",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151CH Treatment of partnerships",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ch"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.277",
      "values:originalText": "This Part applies to a partnership as if the partnership was a person,\nbut it applies with the following changes:\n\n(a) obligations that would be imposed on the partnership are\nimposed instead on each partner, but may be discharged by\nany of the partners;\n\n(b) any offence against this Part that would otherwise be\ncommitted by the partnership is taken to have been\ncommitted by each partner who:\n\n(i) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the relevant act or\nomission; or\n\n(ii) was in any way knowingly concerned in, or party to, the\nrelevant act or omission (whether directly or indirectly\nand whether by any act or omission of the partner).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "This Part applies to a partnership as if the partnership was a person,\nbut it applies with the following changes:\n\n(a) obligations that would be imposed on the partnership are\nimposed instead on each partner, but may be discharged by\nany of the partners;\n\n(b) any offence against this Part that would otherwise be\ncommitted by the partnership is taken to have been\ncommitted by each partner who:\n\n(i) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the relevant act or\nomission; or\n\n(ii) was in any way knowingly concerned in, or party to, the\nrelevant act or omission (whether directly or indirectly\nand whether by any act or omission of the partner).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ch-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ch-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5b3de5f0333cbbb554d23b0a0095ecabb3e0115d7897ffba8be40d5a05473ff0",
      "skos:note": "Partnership treated as a person with modified obligations and liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ch",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151CH Treatment of partnerships",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 277,
      "values:originalText": "This Part applies to a partnership as if the partnership was a person,\nbut it applies with the following changes:\n\n(a) obligations that would be imposed on the partnership are\nimposed instead on each partner, but may be discharged by\nany of the partners;\n\n(b) any offence against this Part that would otherwise be\ncommitted by the partnership is taken to have been\ncommitted by each partner who:\n\n(i) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the relevant act or\nomission; or\n\n(ii) was in any way knowingly concerned in, or party to, the\nrelevant act or omission (whether directly or indirectly\nand whether by any act or omission of the partner).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ch-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ch"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ch-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Partnership's obligations are imposed on each partner.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Partnership is treated as a person.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Obligations are imposed on each partner."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ci",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151CI Review by Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ci"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.278",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission makes a decision under section 151BA to refuse\nto make an exemption order relating to conduct of a person, the\nperson may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(2) If the Commission makes a decision under section 151BG to\nrevoke an exemption order relating to conduct of a person, the\nperson may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3A) If the Commission:\n\n(a) makes a decision under section 151BUA to make a report\nobtained from a person, or an extract from such a report,\navailable for inspection and purchase; or\n\n(b) makes a decision under section 151BUB or 151BUC to give\na person a written direction to make a report or extract\navailable for inspection and purchase;\nthe person may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(4) An application under this section for a review of a decision must\nbe:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application under subsection (1) or (2)—\nmade within 21 days after the Commission made the\ndecision; and\n\n(c) in the case of an application under subsection (3)—made\nwithin 7 days after the Commission made the decision; and\n\n(d) in the case of an application under subsection (3A)—made\nwithin 28 days after the Commission made the decision.\n\n(5) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission makes a decision under section 151BA to refuse\nto make an exemption order relating to conduct of a person, the\nperson may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(2) If the Commission makes a decision under section 151BG to\nrevoke an exemption order relating to conduct of a person, the\nperson may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3A) If the Commission:\n\n(a) makes a decision under section 151BUA to make a report\nobtained from a person, or an extract from such a report,\navailable for inspection and purchase; or\n\n(b) makes a decision under section 151BUB or 151BUC to give\na person a written direction to make a report or extract\navailable for inspection and purchase;\nthe person may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(4) An application under this section for a review of a decision must\nbe:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application under subsection (1) or (2)—\nmade within 21 days after the Commission made the\ndecision; and\n\n(c) in the case of an application under subsection (3)—made\nwithin 7 days after the Commission made the decision; and\n\n(d) in the case of an application under subsection (3A)—made\nwithin 28 days after the Commission made the decision.\n\n(5) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ci-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ci-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ci-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ci-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151ci-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02040ec29e1a16bb75f36f0614a6cb65e6deb034e6b2fcc302d3a9ef912f408c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-151ci",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151CI Review by Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 278,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission makes a decision under section 151BA to refuse\nto make an exemption order relating to conduct of a person, the\nperson may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(2) If the Commission makes a decision under section 151BG to\nrevoke an exemption order relating to conduct of a person, the\nperson may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3A) If the Commission:\n\n(a) makes a decision under section 151BUA to make a report\nobtained from a person, or an extract from such a report,\navailable for inspection and purchase; or\n\n(b) makes a decision under section 151BUB or 151BUC to give\na person a written direction to make a report or extract\navailable for inspection and purchase;\nthe person may apply to the Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(4) An application under this section for a review of a decision must\nbe:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application under subsection (1) or (2)—\nmade within 21 days after the Commission made the\ndecision; and\n\n(c) in the case of an application under subsection (3)—made\nwithin 7 days after the Commission made the decision; and\n\n(d) in the case of an application under subsection (3A)—made\nwithin 28 days after the Commission made the decision.\n\n(5) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a\nreview of a decision, the Tribunal must review the decision.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules"
    },
