      },
      "cml:operator": "takes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on carriers and providers.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ag",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152AG Access seeker",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ag"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.302",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section sets out the circumstances in which a person is taken\nto be an access seeker in relation to a declared service for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\n(2) A service provider is an access seeker in relation to a declared\nservice if the provider makes, or proposes to make, a request in\nrelation to that service under section 152AR (which deals with the\ncategory A standard access obligations) or section 152AXB (which\ndeals with the category B standard access obligations), whether or\nnot:\n\n(a) the request is refused; or\n\n(b) the request is being complied with.\n\n(3) A service provider is an access seeker in relation to a declared\nservice if:\n\n(a) the provider wants access to the service; or\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 152AH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the provider wants to change some aspect of the provider’s\nexisting access to the service; or\n\n(c) the supplier of the service wants to change some aspect of the\nprovider’s existing access to the service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section sets out the circumstances in which a person is taken\nto be an access seeker in relation to a declared service for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\n(2) A service provider is an access seeker in relation to a declared\nservice if the provider makes, or proposes to make, a request in\nrelation to that service under section 152AR (which deals with the\ncategory A standard access obligations) or section 152AXB (which\ndeals with the category B standard access obligations), whether or\nnot:\n\n(a) the request is refused; or\n\n(b) the request is being complied with.\n\n(3) A service provider is an access seeker in relation to a declared\nservice if:\n\n(a) the provider wants access to the service; or\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 152AH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the provider wants to change some aspect of the provider’s\nexisting access to the service; or\n\n(c) the supplier of the service wants to change some aspect of the\nprovider’s existing access to the service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ag-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ag-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ag-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d40c77d1996c4dab46933b24da2f963730b0aed0e1934bd4738a4187255bf355"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ag",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152AG Access seeker",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 302,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section sets out the circumstances in which a person is taken\nto be an access seeker in relation to a declared service for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\n(2) A service provider is an access seeker in relation to a declared\nservice if the provider makes, or proposes to make, a request in\nrelation to that service under section 152AR (which deals with the\ncategory A standard access obligations) or section 152AXB (which\ndeals with the category B standard access obligations), whether or\nnot:\n\n(a) the request is refused; or\n\n(b) the request is being complied with.\n\n(3) A service provider is an access seeker in relation to a declared\nservice if:\n\n(a) the provider wants access to the service; or\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 152AH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(b) the provider wants to change some aspect of the provider’s\nexisting access to the service; or\n\n(c) the supplier of the service wants to change some aspect of the\nprovider’s existing access to the service."
    },
