    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152AL Declared services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152al"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.305",
      "values:originalText": "Eligible service\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, an eligible service is:\n\n(a) a listed carriage service (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997); or\n\n(b) a service that facilitates the supply of a listed carriage service\n(within the meaning of that Act);\nwhere the service is supplied, or is capable of being supplied, by a\ncarrier or a carriage service provider (whether to itself or to other\npersons).\nDeclaration made after public inquiry—services not supplied by an\nNBN corporation\n\n(3) The Commission may, by written instrument, declare that a\nspecified eligible service is a declared service if:\n\n(a) the Commission has held a public inquiry under Part 25 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997 about a proposal to make\nthe declaration; and\n\n(b) the Commission has prepared a report about the inquiry\nunder section 505 of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(c) the report was published during the 180-day period ending\nwhen the declaration was made; and\n\n(d) the Commission is satisfied that the making of the\ndeclaration will promote the long-term interests of end-users\nof carriage services or of services provided by means of\ncarriage services.\nNote:\nEligible services may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified\nclass or in any other way.\n\n(3A) A declaration under subsection (3) does not apply to an eligible\nservice to the extent to which the service is supplied, or is capable\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Eligible service\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, an eligible service is:\n\n(a) a listed carriage service (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997); or\n\n(b) a service that facilitates the supply of a listed carriage service\n(within the meaning of that Act);\nwhere the service is supplied, or is capable of being supplied, by a\ncarrier or a carriage service provider (whether to itself or to other\npersons).\nDeclaration made after public inquiry—services not supplied by an\nNBN corporation\n\n(3) The Commission may, by written instrument, declare that a\nspecified eligible service is a declared service if:\n\n(a) the Commission has held a public inquiry under Part 25 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997 about a proposal to make\nthe declaration; and\n\n(b) the Commission has prepared a report about the inquiry\nunder section 505 of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(c) the report was published during the 180-day period ending\nwhen the declaration was made; and\n\n(d) the Commission is satisfied that the making of the\ndeclaration will promote the long-term interests of end-users\nof carriage services or of services provided by means of\ncarriage services.\nNote:\nEligible services may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified\nclass or in any other way.\n\n(3A) A declaration under subsection (3) does not apply to an eligible\nservice to the extent to which the service is supplied, or is capable\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al-ss-3a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "97c26ebcdce23b61809373ff794c0f51f036dd2426d791c1fa3137f991170968"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152al",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152AL Declared services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 305,
      "values:originalText": "Eligible service\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, an eligible service is:\n\n(a) a listed carriage service (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997); or\n\n(b) a service that facilitates the supply of a listed carriage service\n(within the meaning of that Act);\nwhere the service is supplied, or is capable of being supplied, by a\ncarrier or a carriage service provider (whether to itself or to other\npersons).\nDeclaration made after public inquiry—services not supplied by an\nNBN corporation\n\n(3) The Commission may, by written instrument, declare that a\nspecified eligible service is a declared service if:\n\n(a) the Commission has held a public inquiry under Part 25 of\nthe Telecommunications Act 1997 about a proposal to make\nthe declaration; and\n\n(b) the Commission has prepared a report about the inquiry\nunder section 505 of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(c) the report was published during the 180-day period ending\nwhen the declaration was made; and\n\n(d) the Commission is satisfied that the making of the\ndeclaration will promote the long-term interests of end-users\nof carriage services or of services provided by means of\ncarriage services.\nNote:\nEligible services may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified\nclass or in any other way.\n\n(3A) A declaration under subsection (3) does not apply to an eligible\nservice to the extent to which the service is supplied, or is capable\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152AL(1) Declared services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152al-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.305",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, an eligible service is:\n\n(a) a listed carriage service (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997); or\n\n(b) a service that facilitates the supply of a listed carriage service\n(within the meaning of that Act);\nwhere the service is supplied, or is capable of being supplied, by a\ncarrier or a carriage service provider (whether to itself or to other\npersons).\nDeclaration made after public inquiry—services not supplied by an\nNBN corporation",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this section, an eligible service is:\n\n(a) a listed carriage service (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997); or\n\n(b) a service that facilitates the supply of a listed carriage service\n(within the meaning of that Act);\nwhere the service is supplied, or is capable of being supplied, by a\ncarrier or a carriage service provider (whether to itself or to other\npersons).\nDeclaration made after public inquiry—services not supplied by an\nNBN corporation",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al-ss-1-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cc73fb002d58931d1e2a3d89ac1812795e41ea05c2627cf2f1dd80ea9218f926",
      "skos:note": "Defines eligible services for section 152AL(1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152al-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152AL(1) Declared services",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 305,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, an eligible service is:\n\n(a) a listed carriage service (within the meaning of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997); or\n\n(b) a service that facilitates the supply of a listed carriage service\n(within the meaning of that Act);\nwhere the service is supplied, or is capable of being supplied, by a\ncarrier or a carriage service provider (whether to itself or to other\npersons).\nDeclaration made after public inquiry—services not supplied by an\nNBN corporation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152al-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
