    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152an",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152AN Combined inquiries about proposals to declare services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152an"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.313",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may decide to combine 2 or more public inquiries\nof a kind mentioned in paragraph 152AL(3)(a), or (8A)(a) or\n152ALA(7)(a).\n\n(2) If the Commission makes such a decision:\n\n(a) the Commission may publish a single notice relating to the\ncombined inquiry under section 498 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(b) the Commission may prepare a single discussion paper about\nthe combined inquiry under section 499 of that Act; and\n\n(c) the Commission may hold hearings relating to the combined\ninquiry under section 501 of that Act; and\n\n(d) the Commission must ensure that each inquiry is covered by\na report under section 505 of that Act, whether the report\nrelates:\n\n(i) to a single one of those inquiries; or\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may decide to combine 2 or more public inquiries\nof a kind mentioned in paragraph 152AL(3)(a), or (8A)(a) or\n152ALA(7)(a).\n\n(2) If the Commission makes such a decision:\n\n(a) the Commission may publish a single notice relating to the\ncombined inquiry under section 498 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(b) the Commission may prepare a single discussion paper about\nthe combined inquiry under section 499 of that Act; and\n\n(c) the Commission may hold hearings relating to the combined\ninquiry under section 501 of that Act; and\n\n(d) the Commission must ensure that each inquiry is covered by\na report under section 505 of that Act, whether the report\nrelates:\n\n(i) to a single one of those inquiries; or\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152an-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152an-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0e65bc382682e698332752e546ebcce1158ffe88e4c021eab9b12a5498a2071"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152an",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152AN Combined inquiries about proposals to declare services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 313,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may decide to combine 2 or more public inquiries\nof a kind mentioned in paragraph 152AL(3)(a), or (8A)(a) or\n152ALA(7)(a).\n\n(2) If the Commission makes such a decision:\n\n(a) the Commission may publish a single notice relating to the\ncombined inquiry under section 498 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(b) the Commission may prepare a single discussion paper about\nthe combined inquiry under section 499 of that Act; and\n\n(c) the Commission may hold hearings relating to the combined\ninquiry under section 501 of that Act; and\n\n(d) the Commission must ensure that each inquiry is covered by\na report under section 505 of that Act, whether the report\nrelates:\n\n(i) to a single one of those inquiries; or\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
