    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152AR(3) Category A standard access obligations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ar-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.316",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An access provider must, if requested to do so by a service\nprovider:\n\n(a) supply an active declared service to the service provider in\norder that the service provider can provide carriage services\nand/or content services; and\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the technical and\noperational quality of the active declared service supplied to\nthe service provider is equivalent to that which the access\nprovider provides to itself; and\n\n(c) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the service provider\nreceives, in relation to the active declared service supplied to\nthe service provider, fault detection, handling and\nrectification of a technical and operational quality and timing\nthat is equivalent to that which the access provider provides\nto itself.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nStandard access obligations  Division 3\n\nSection 152AR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nLimit on paragraph (3)(a) obligation",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An access provider must, if requested to do so by a service\nprovider:\n\n(a) supply an active declared service to the service provider in\norder that the service provider can provide carriage services\nand/or content services; and\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the technical and\noperational quality of the active declared service supplied to\nthe service provider is equivalent to that which the access\nprovider provides to itself; and\n\n(c) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the service provider\nreceives, in relation to the active declared service supplied to\nthe service provider, fault detection, handling and\nrectification of a technical and operational quality and timing\nthat is equivalent to that which the access provider provides\nto itself.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nStandard access obligations  Division 3\n\nSection 152AR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nLimit on paragraph (3)(a) obligation",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar-ss-3-logic-linearlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f0b96fe456aae3281d1bc089df68d7b6882c69175832ec122225af79c6fbd2f",
      "skos:note": "Access provider must supply active declared service to service provider.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ar-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152AR(3) Category A standard access obligations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 316,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An access provider must, if requested to do so by a service\nprovider:\n\n(a) supply an active declared service to the service provider in\norder that the service provider can provide carriage services\nand/or content services; and\n\n(b) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the technical and\noperational quality of the active declared service supplied to\nthe service provider is equivalent to that which the access\nprovider provides to itself; and\n\n(c) take all reasonable steps to ensure that the service provider\nreceives, in relation to the active declared service supplied to\nthe service provider, fault detection, handling and\nrectification of a technical and operational quality and timing\nthat is equivalent to that which the access provider provides\nto itself.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nStandard access obligations  Division 3\n\nSection 152AR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nLimit on paragraph (3)(a) obligation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ar-ss-3-norm",
