    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152au",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152AU Individual exemptions—request for further information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152au"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.327",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to an application under\nsubsection 152ATA(1).\n\n(2) The Commission may request the applicant to give the\nCommission further information about the application.\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) the Procedural Rules make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information; and\n\n(b) the applicant does not give the Commission the information\nwithin the time limit allowed by the Procedural Rules;\nthe Commission may, by written notice given to the applicant,\nrefuse the application.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2A) has effect despite anything in this Division.\n\n(3) If the Procedural Rules do not make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information, the Commission may refuse\nto consider the application until the applicant gives the\nCommission the information.\n\n(4) The Commission may withdraw its request for further information,\nin whole or in part.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to an application under\nsubsection 152ATA(1).\n\n(2) The Commission may request the applicant to give the\nCommission further information about the application.\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) the Procedural Rules make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information; and\n\n(b) the applicant does not give the Commission the information\nwithin the time limit allowed by the Procedural Rules;\nthe Commission may, by written notice given to the applicant,\nrefuse the application.\n\n(2B) Subsection (2A) has effect despite anything in this Division.\n\n(3) If the Procedural Rules do not make provision for or in relation to a\ntime limit for giving the information, the Commission may refuse\nto consider the application until the applicant gives the\nCommission the information.\n\n(4) The Commission may withdraw its request for further information,\nin whole or in part.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152au-ss-1"
        },
