    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152bb-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152BB(1) Judicial enforcement of standard access obligations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152bb-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.336",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has contravened any\nof the conditions or limitations of:\n\n(a) a determination under section 152ASA; or\n\n(b) an order under section 152ATA;\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(c) the Commission; or\n\n(d) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(e) an order directing the person to comply with the condition or\nlimitation;\n\n(f) an order directing the person to compensate any other person\nwho had suffered loss or damage as a result of the\ncontravention;\n\n(g) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has contravened any\nof the conditions or limitations of:\n\n(a) a determination under section 152ASA; or\n\n(b) an order under section 152ATA;\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(c) the Commission; or\n\n(d) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(e) an order directing the person to comply with the condition or\nlimitation;\n\n(f) an order directing the person to compensate any other person\nwho had suffered loss or damage as a result of the\ncontravention;\n\n(g) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152bb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152bb-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152bb-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f672bef920be86c38322679c79e827ef30a8bbaf6eec906c52d0ade48607be7",
      "skos:note": "Court may order person to comply with condition or limitation Federal Court may make orders to enforce standard access obligations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152bb-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152BB(1) Judicial enforcement of standard access obligations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 336,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has contravened any\nof the conditions or limitations of:\n\n(a) a determination under section 152ASA; or\n\n(b) an order under section 152ATA;\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(c) the Commission; or\n\n(d) any person whose interests are affected by the contravention;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(e) an order directing the person to comply with the condition or\nlimitation;\n\n(f) an order directing the person to compensate any other person\nwho had suffered loss or damage as a result of the\ncontravention;\n\n(g) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate."
    },
