    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152cd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152CD Enforcement of access undertakings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152cd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.411",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an access undertaking given by a person (the\nfirst person) is in operation.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person (the affected person) whose interests are affected\nby the undertaking;\nthinks that the first person has breached the access undertaking, the\nCommission or affected person may apply to the Federal Court for\nan order under subsection (3).\n\n(3) If the Federal Court is satisfied that the first person has breached\nthe undertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing the first person to comply with the\nundertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the first person to compensate any other\nperson who has suffered loss or damage as a result of the\nbreach;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The Federal Court may discharge or vary an order granted under\nthis section.\n152CDA  Deferral of consideration of an access undertaking etc.\n\n(1) The Procedural Rules may authorise the Commission to defer\nconsideration of:\n\n(a) an access undertaking; or\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an access undertaking given by a person (the\nfirst person) is in operation.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person (the affected person) whose interests are affected\nby the undertaking;\nthinks that the first person has breached the access undertaking, the\nCommission or affected person may apply to the Federal Court for\nan order under subsection (3).\n\n(3) If the Federal Court is satisfied that the first person has breached\nthe undertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing the first person to comply with the\nundertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the first person to compensate any other\nperson who has suffered loss or damage as a result of the\nbreach;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The Federal Court may discharge or vary an order granted under\nthis section.\n152CDA  Deferral of consideration of an access undertaking etc.\n\n(1) The Procedural Rules may authorise the Commission to defer\nconsideration of:\n\n(a) an access undertaking; or\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152cd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152cd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152cd-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152cd-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152cd-ss-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77761abf2f29f978033c71e6016ec893c7ffe27a7fc403d13c0939bcd4186789"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152cd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152CD Enforcement of access undertakings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 411,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an access undertaking given by a person (the\nfirst person) is in operation.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Commission; or\n\n(b) any person (the affected person) whose interests are affected\nby the undertaking;\nthinks that the first person has breached the access undertaking, the\nCommission or affected person may apply to the Federal Court for\nan order under subsection (3).\n\n(3) If the Federal Court is satisfied that the first person has breached\nthe undertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing the first person to comply with the\nundertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the first person to compensate any other\nperson who has suffered loss or damage as a result of the\nbreach;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The Federal Court may discharge or vary an order granted under\nthis section.\n152CDA  Deferral of consideration of an access undertaking etc.\n\n(1) The Procedural Rules may authorise the Commission to defer\nconsideration of:\n\n(a) an access undertaking; or\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
