    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152CH Ministerial pricing determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ch"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.413",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\nsetting out principles dealing with price-related terms and\nconditions relating to the standard access obligations. The\ndetermination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing\ndetermination.\nNote 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept\na special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with\nany Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 4:\nSubsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access\nundertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5:\nSubsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access\ndetermination has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of\nconduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent\nwith any Ministerial pricing determination.\n\n(3) In this section:\nprice-related terms and conditions means terms and conditions\nrelating to price or a method of ascertaining price.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\nsetting out principles dealing with price-related terms and\nconditions relating to the standard access obligations. The\ndetermination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing\ndetermination.\nNote 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept\na special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with\nany Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 4:\nSubsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access\nundertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5:\nSubsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access\ndetermination has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of\nconduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent\nwith any Ministerial pricing determination.\n\n(3) In this section:\nprice-related terms and conditions means terms and conditions\nrelating to price or a method of ascertaining price.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b211c58c0d05c1ba24618fe171b6f88c8d90be92dafe5f41770f51a76f039d7a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ch",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152CH Ministerial pricing determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 413,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\nsetting out principles dealing with price-related terms and\nconditions relating to the standard access obligations. The\ndetermination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing\ndetermination.\nNote 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept\na special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with\nany Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 4:\nSubsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access\nundertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5:\nSubsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access\ndetermination has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of\nconduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent\nwith any Ministerial pricing determination.\n\n(3) In this section:\nprice-related terms and conditions means terms and conditions\nrelating to price or a method of ascertaining price."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152CH(1) Ministerial pricing determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ch-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.413",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\nsetting out principles dealing with price-related terms and\nconditions relating to the standard access obligations. The\ndetermination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing\ndetermination.\nNote 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept\na special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with\nany Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 4:\nSubsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access\nundertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5:\nSubsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access\ndetermination has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of\nconduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent\nwith any Ministerial pricing determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\nsetting out principles dealing with price-related terms and\nconditions relating to the standard access obligations. The\ndetermination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing\ndetermination.\nNote 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept\na special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with\nany Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 4:\nSubsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access\nundertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5:\nSubsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access\ndetermination has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of\nconduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent\nwith any Ministerial pricing determination.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch-ss-1-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d74c318daa065357b79b43b4e858914bb5cc9ee0650b74da7ebfb112dcfce86b",
      "skos:note": "Ministerial pricing determination"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ch-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152CH(1) Ministerial pricing determinations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 413,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\nsetting out principles dealing with price-related terms and\nconditions relating to the standard access obligations. The\ndetermination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing\ndetermination.\nNote 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept\na special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with\nany Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 4:\nSubsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access\nundertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5:\nSubsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access\ndetermination has no effect to the extent that the provision is\ninconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.\nNote 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of\nconduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent\nwith any Ministerial pricing determination."
    },
    {
