    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ef",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152EF Prohibition on hindering the fulfilment of a standard access",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ef"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.422",
      "values:originalText": "obligation etc.\n\n(1) A person must not engage in conduct for the purpose of preventing\nor hindering the fulfilment of:\n\n(a) a standard access obligation; or\n\n(b) a requirement imposed by an access determination; or\n\n(ba) a requirement imposed by binding rules of conduct;\nif the person is:\n\n(c) a carrier or a carriage service provider who supplies a\ndeclared service; or\n\n(d) a service provider to whom a declared service is being\nsupplied by a carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(e) a body corporate that is related to a carrier or provider\nreferred to in paragraph (c) or (d).\n\n(2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose\nreferred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has\nbeen considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only\nby inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant\ncircumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which\nthe purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not have effect before 1 July 1997.",
      "skos:definition": "obligation etc.\n\n(1) A person must not engage in conduct for the purpose of preventing\nor hindering the fulfilment of:\n\n(a) a standard access obligation; or\n\n(b) a requirement imposed by an access determination; or\n\n(ba) a requirement imposed by binding rules of conduct;\nif the person is:\n\n(c) a carrier or a carriage service provider who supplies a\ndeclared service; or\n\n(d) a service provider to whom a declared service is being\nsupplied by a carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(e) a body corporate that is related to a carrier or provider\nreferred to in paragraph (c) or (d).\n\n(2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose\nreferred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has\nbeen considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only\nby inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant\ncircumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which\nthe purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not have effect before 1 July 1997.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ef-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ef-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ef-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "46151f8acaa0133ee8ed6597ba7124e43ac7a43659839f582a79544d40f77a29"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152ef",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152EF Prohibition on hindering the fulfilment of a standard access",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 422,
      "values:originalText": "obligation etc.\n\n(1) A person must not engage in conduct for the purpose of preventing\nor hindering the fulfilment of:\n\n(a) a standard access obligation; or\n\n(b) a requirement imposed by an access determination; or\n\n(ba) a requirement imposed by binding rules of conduct;\nif the person is:\n\n(c) a carrier or a carriage service provider who supplies a\ndeclared service; or\n\n(d) a service provider to whom a declared service is being\nsupplied by a carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(e) a body corporate that is related to a carrier or provider\nreferred to in paragraph (c) or (d).\n\n(2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose\nreferred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has\nbeen considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only\nby inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant\ncircumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which\nthe purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not have effect before 1 July 1997."
    },
