    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152EG Enforcement of prohibition on hindering the fulfilment of a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152eg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.422",
      "values:originalText": "standard access obligation etc.\n\n(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied, on the application of any person,\nthat another person (the obstructor) has engaged, is engaging, or is\nproposing to engage in conduct constituting a contravention of\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nHindering the fulfilment of a standard access obligation etc.  Division 10\n\nSection 152EH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nsection 152EF, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the obstructor from engaging in the conduct;\nor\n\n(ii) if the conduct involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the obstructor to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order directing the obstructor to compensate a person who\nhas suffered loss or damage as a result of the contravention;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) If the Federal Court has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who was involved in the\ncontravention concerned.",
      "skos:definition": "standard access obligation etc.\n\n(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied, on the application of any person,\nthat another person (the obstructor) has engaged, is engaging, or is\nproposing to engage in conduct constituting a contravention of\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nHindering the fulfilment of a standard access obligation etc.  Division 10\n\nSection 152EH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nsection 152EF, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the obstructor from engaging in the conduct;\nor\n\n(ii) if the conduct involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the obstructor to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order directing the obstructor to compensate a person who\nhas suffered loss or damage as a result of the contravention;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) If the Federal Court has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who was involved in the\ncontravention concerned.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d79422ec5258200773410943e4613fbc6514bb94ffa029b6827b9b2c85da7b08"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152eg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152EG Enforcement of prohibition on hindering the fulfilment of a",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 422,
      "values:originalText": "standard access obligation etc.\n\n(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied, on the application of any person,\nthat another person (the obstructor) has engaged, is engaging, or is\nproposing to engage in conduct constituting a contravention of\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nHindering the fulfilment of a standard access obligation etc.  Division 10\n\nSection 152EH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nsection 152EF, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the obstructor from engaging in the conduct;\nor\n\n(ii) if the conduct involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the obstructor to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order directing the obstructor to compensate a person who\nhas suffered loss or damage as a result of the contravention;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) If the Federal Court has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who was involved in the\ncontravention concerned."
    },
