    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152EQ Assistance to independent telecommunications adjudicator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152eq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.429",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the independent\ntelecommunications adjudicator is a company that:\n\n(a) is limited by guarantee; and\n\n(b) is identified, in an undertaking in force under section 577A\nof the Telecommunications Act 1997, as the independent\ntelecommunications adjudicator for the purpose of this\nsection.\n\n(2) The Commission may assist the independent telecommunications\nadjudicator.\n\n(3) The assistance may include the following:\n\n(a) the provision of information (including protected information\nwithin the meaning of section 155AAA);\n\n(b) the provision of advice;\n\n(c) the making available of resources and facilities (including\nsecretariat services and clerical assistance).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the independent\ntelecommunications adjudicator is a company that:\n\n(a) is limited by guarantee; and\n\n(b) is identified, in an undertaking in force under section 577A\nof the Telecommunications Act 1997, as the independent\ntelecommunications adjudicator for the purpose of this\nsection.\n\n(2) The Commission may assist the independent telecommunications\nadjudicator.\n\n(3) The assistance may include the following:\n\n(a) the provision of information (including protected information\nwithin the meaning of section 155AAA);\n\n(b) the provision of advice;\n\n(c) the making available of resources and facilities (including\nsecretariat services and clerical assistance).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eq-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152eq-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80b8295d8d8e6437e96757fd7d4fa56b20e16401387f0753553edf03b6684d99"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152eq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152EQ Assistance to independent telecommunications adjudicator",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 429,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the independent\ntelecommunications adjudicator is a company that:\n\n(a) is limited by guarantee; and\n\n(b) is identified, in an undertaking in force under section 577A\nof the Telecommunications Act 1997, as the independent\ntelecommunications adjudicator for the purpose of this\nsection.\n\n(2) The Commission may assist the independent telecommunications\nadjudicator.\n\n(3) The assistance may include the following:\n\n(a) the provision of information (including protected information\nwithin the meaning of section 155AAA);\n\n(b) the provision of advice;\n\n(c) the making available of resources and facilities (including\nsecretariat services and clerical assistance).\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
