    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152er",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152ER Voluntary undertakings given by Telstra",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152er"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.430",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an undertaking given by Telstra is in force\nunder section 577C or 577E of the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nNote 2:\nSection 577C of the Telecommunications Act 1997 deals with\nundertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks.\nNote 3:\nSection 577E of the Telecommunications Act 1997 deals with\nundertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nMiscellaneous  Division 11\n\nSection 152ER\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nCommission must have regard to Telstra’s conduct\n\n(2) If Telstra has engaged, or is required to engage, in conduct in order\nto comply with the undertaking, then, in performing a function, or\nexercising a power, under this Part in relation to Telstra, the\nCommission must have regard to the conduct to the extent that the\nconduct is relevant.\nCommission must not prevent Telstra from complying with the\nundertaking\n\n(3) The Commission must not perform a function, or exercise a power,\nunder this Part so as to prevent Telstra from complying with the\nundertaking.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an undertaking given by Telstra is in force\nunder section 577C or 577E of the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nNote 2:\nSection 577C of the Telecommunications Act 1997 deals with\nundertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks.\nNote 3:\nSection 577E of the Telecommunications Act 1997 deals with\nundertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nMiscellaneous  Division 11\n\nSection 152ER\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nCommission must have regard to Telstra’s conduct\n\n(2) If Telstra has engaged, or is required to engage, in conduct in order\nto comply with the undertaking, then, in performing a function, or\nexercising a power, under this Part in relation to Telstra, the\nCommission must have regard to the conduct to the extent that the\nconduct is relevant.\nCommission must not prevent Telstra from complying with the\nundertaking\n\n(3) The Commission must not perform a function, or exercise a power,\nunder this Part so as to prevent Telstra from complying with the\nundertaking.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152er-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152er-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152er-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-152er",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152ER Voluntary undertakings given by Telstra",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 430,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an undertaking given by Telstra is in force\nunder section 577C or 577E of the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nNote 2:\nSection 577C of the Telecommunications Act 1997 deals with\nundertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks.\nNote 3:\nSection 577E of the Telecommunications Act 1997 deals with\nundertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nTelecommunications access regime  Part XIC\nMiscellaneous  Division 11\n\nSection 152ER\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nCommission must have regard to Telstra’s conduct\n\n(2) If Telstra has engaged, or is required to engage, in conduct in order\nto comply with the undertaking, then, in performing a function, or\nexercising a power, under this Part in relation to Telstra, the\nCommission must have regard to the conduct to the extent that the\nconduct is relevant.\nCommission must not prevent Telstra from complying with the\nundertaking\n\n(3) The Commission must not perform a function, or exercise a power,\nunder this Part so as to prevent Telstra from complying with the\nundertaking.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
