      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153C Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.433",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nassociate has the same meaning as in the Foreign Acquisitions and\nTakeovers Act 1975.\nconnected body corporate has the meaning given by section 153D.\ncontracting order means an order of the Treasurer under\nsection 153X.\nCourt means the Federal Court of Australia.\ndivestiture order means an order of the Court under\nsection 153ZB.\nelectricity financial contract: a contract is an electricity financial\ncontract if:\n\n(a) rights under the contract are derived from or relate to the\nprice of electricity on an electricity spot market; and\n\n(b) the operator of that electricity spot market is not a party to\nthe contract.\nelectricity market means any of the following:\n\n(a) a market in relation to the supply of electricity;\n\n(b) a market for electricity financial contracts.\nelectricity spot market means a spot market for the supply of\nelectricity.\ninterest, in an asset or a security, has the same meaning as in the\nForeign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975.\nno Treasurer action notice means a notice under section 153U.\nprohibited conduct: a corporation engages in prohibited conduct if\nthe corporation engages in conduct that contravenes section 153E,\n153F, 153G or 153H.\nprohibited conduct notice means a notice under section 153P.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\nassociate has the same meaning as in the Foreign Acquisitions and\nTakeovers Act 1975.\nconnected body corporate has the meaning given by section 153D.\ncontracting order means an order of the Treasurer under\nsection 153X.\nCourt means the Federal Court of Australia.\ndivestiture order means an order of the Court under\nsection 153ZB.\nelectricity financial contract: a contract is an electricity financial\ncontract if:\n\n(a) rights under the contract are derived from or relate to the\nprice of electricity on an electricity spot market; and\n\n(b) the operator of that electricity spot market is not a party to\nthe contract.\nelectricity market means any of the following:\n\n(a) a market in relation to the supply of electricity;\n\n(b) a market for electricity financial contracts.\nelectricity spot market means a spot market for the supply of\nelectricity.\ninterest, in an asset or a security, has the same meaning as in the\nForeign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975.\nno Treasurer action notice means a notice under section 153U.\nprohibited conduct: a corporation engages in prohibited conduct if\nthe corporation engages in conduct that contravenes section 153E,\n153F, 153G or 153H.\nprohibited conduct notice means a notice under section 153P.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153c-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153c-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153c-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5f8027c989ff0f5c20920f9188c00fe0f8fc7e8f2d8a422a54d3a245a27e89e2",
      "skos:note": "Definition of terms used in Part VIIA"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153C Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 433,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nassociate has the same meaning as in the Foreign Acquisitions and\nTakeovers Act 1975.\nconnected body corporate has the meaning given by section 153D.\ncontracting order means an order of the Treasurer under\nsection 153X.\nCourt means the Federal Court of Australia.\ndivestiture order means an order of the Court under\nsection 153ZB.\nelectricity financial contract: a contract is an electricity financial\ncontract if:\n\n(a) rights under the contract are derived from or relate to the\nprice of electricity on an electricity spot market; and\n\n(b) the operator of that electricity spot market is not a party to\nthe contract.\nelectricity market means any of the following:\n\n(a) a market in relation to the supply of electricity;\n\n(b) a market for electricity financial contracts.\nelectricity spot market means a spot market for the supply of\nelectricity.\ninterest, in an asset or a security, has the same meaning as in the\nForeign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act 1975.\nno Treasurer action notice means a notice under section 153U.\nprohibited conduct: a corporation engages in prohibited conduct if\nthe corporation engages in conduct that contravenes section 153E,\n153F, 153G or 153H.\nprohibited conduct notice means a notice under section 153P.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
