      },
      "cml:premiseText": "connected body corporate has the meaning given by section 153D.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "connected body corporate is defined"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153D Meaning of connected body corporate in relation to prohibited",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.434",
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) A corporation is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct engaged in by the corporation.\n\n(2) A body corporate is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct engaged in by a corporation if:\n\n(a) the body corporate is related to the corporation; and\n\n(b) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the prohibited conduct involves the direct or indirect use\nof assets held by the body corporate;\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct involves direct or indirect\ndealings between the body corporate and the\ncorporation.\n\n(3) A body corporate is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct if:\n\n(a) the body corporate is a holding company of another body\ncorporate; and\n\n(b) the other body corporate is a connected body corporate in\nrelation to the prohibited conduct because of a previous\noperation of this section.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Electricity Industry  Part XICA\nProhibited conduct  Division 2\n\nSection 153E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "conduct\n\n(1) A corporation is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct engaged in by the corporation.\n\n(2) A body corporate is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct engaged in by a corporation if:\n\n(a) the body corporate is related to the corporation; and\n\n(b) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the prohibited conduct involves the direct or indirect use\nof assets held by the body corporate;\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct involves direct or indirect\ndealings between the body corporate and the\ncorporation.\n\n(3) A body corporate is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct if:\n\n(a) the body corporate is a holding company of another body\ncorporate; and\n\n(b) the other body corporate is a connected body corporate in\nrelation to the prohibited conduct because of a previous\noperation of this section.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Electricity Industry  Part XICA\nProhibited conduct  Division 2\n\nSection 153E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85ca6d6d291c070dbcb28efa667bbed81c9c789b5bb515725a7bad753f6171ba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153D Meaning of connected body corporate in relation to prohibited",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 434,
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) A corporation is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct engaged in by the corporation.\n\n(2) A body corporate is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct engaged in by a corporation if:\n\n(a) the body corporate is related to the corporation; and\n\n(b) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the prohibited conduct involves the direct or indirect use\nof assets held by the body corporate;\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct involves direct or indirect\ndealings between the body corporate and the\ncorporation.\n\n(3) A body corporate is a connected body corporate in relation to\nprohibited conduct if:\n\n(a) the body corporate is a holding company of another body\ncorporate; and\n\n(b) the other body corporate is a connected body corporate in\nrelation to the prohibited conduct because of a previous\noperation of this section.\n\nFurther provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7\nThe Electricity Industry  Part XICA\nProhibited conduct  Division 2\n\nSection 153E\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
