    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153E Prohibited conduct—retail pricing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.435",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corporation contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the corporation offers to supply electricity, or supplies\nelectricity, to small customers; and\n\n(b) the corporation fails to make reasonable adjustments to the\nprice of those offers, or to the price of those supplies, to\nreflect sustained and substantial reductions in its underlying\ncost of procuring electricity.\nNote 1:\nThe Treasurer cannot make a contracting order in respect of a\ncontravention of this section (see paragraph 153W(e)).\nNote 2:\nThe Treasurer cannot apply for a divestiture order in respect of a\ncontravention of this section (see paragraph 153ZA(e)).\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the corporation does not contravene this\nsection if the price is a standing offer price (within the meaning of\nthe Competition and Consumer (Industry Code—Electricity Retail)\nRegulations 2019).\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), the corporation does not contravene this\nsection if the adjustments would contravene:\n\n(a) an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or\n\n(b) an instrument made under such an Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A corporation contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the corporation offers to supply electricity, or supplies\nelectricity, to small customers; and\n\n(b) the corporation fails to make reasonable adjustments to the\nprice of those offers, or to the price of those supplies, to\nreflect sustained and substantial reductions in its underlying\ncost of procuring electricity.\nNote 1:\nThe Treasurer cannot make a contracting order in respect of a\ncontravention of this section (see paragraph 153W(e)).\nNote 2:\nThe Treasurer cannot apply for a divestiture order in respect of a\ncontravention of this section (see paragraph 153ZA(e)).\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the corporation does not contravene this\nsection if the price is a standing offer price (within the meaning of\nthe Competition and Consumer (Industry Code—Electricity Retail)\nRegulations 2019).\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), the corporation does not contravene this\nsection if the adjustments would contravene:\n\n(a) an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or\n\n(b) an instrument made under such an Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153e-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8ba43c5d49cb2c852779cc24b06fcbf31e698a6587dbc3c98fd59ed64fdd677a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153E Prohibited conduct—retail pricing",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 435,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corporation contravenes this section if:\n\n(a) the corporation offers to supply electricity, or supplies\nelectricity, to small customers; and\n\n(b) the corporation fails to make reasonable adjustments to the\nprice of those offers, or to the price of those supplies, to\nreflect sustained and substantial reductions in its underlying\ncost of procuring electricity.\nNote 1:\nThe Treasurer cannot make a contracting order in respect of a\ncontravention of this section (see paragraph 153W(e)).\nNote 2:\nThe Treasurer cannot apply for a divestiture order in respect of a\ncontravention of this section (see paragraph 153ZA(e)).\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the corporation does not contravene this\nsection if the price is a standing offer price (within the meaning of\nthe Competition and Consumer (Industry Code—Electricity Retail)\nRegulations 2019).\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), the corporation does not contravene this\nsection if the adjustments would contravene:\n\n(a) an Act of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or\n\n(b) an instrument made under such an Act."
    },
