    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153m-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153M(2) Commission may issue public warning notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153m-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.439",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Commission may issue to the public a written notice\ncontaining a warning about the prohibited conduct if the\nCommission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the corporation has engaged in the prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the corporation is engaging in the prohibited conduct;\nand\n\n(b) one or more persons has suffered, or is likely to suffer,\ndetriment as a result of the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(c) it is in the public interest to issue the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Commission may issue to the public a written notice\ncontaining a warning about the prohibited conduct if the\nCommission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the corporation has engaged in the prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the corporation is engaging in the prohibited conduct;\nand\n\n(b) one or more persons has suffered, or is likely to suffer,\ndetriment as a result of the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(c) it is in the public interest to issue the notice.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153m"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153m-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153m-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3575974e1f36bf6b22f63056c856d424caf8c5a4cd7c9ac05685cef1ca5b983d",
      "skos:note": "Commission may issue public warning notice for prohibited conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153m-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153M(2) Commission may issue public warning notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 439,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Commission may issue to the public a written notice\ncontaining a warning about the prohibited conduct if the\nCommission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the corporation has engaged in the prohibited conduct;\n\n(ii) the corporation is engaging in the prohibited conduct;\nand\n\n(b) one or more persons has suffered, or is likely to suffer,\ndetriment as a result of the prohibited conduct; and\n\n(c) it is in the public interest to issue the notice."
    },
