      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153r-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide a prohibited conduct recommendation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153S Prohibited conduct recommendations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.445",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may give the Treasurer a notice in writing (a\nprohibited conduct recommendation) in respect of the prohibited\nconduct notice, stating one or more recommendations for the kind\nor kinds of order the Treasurer or the Court could make under\nDivision 5 or 6, if the Commission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the corporation has engaged in the kind of prohibited\nconduct specified in the prohibited conduct notice;\n\n(ii) the corporation is continuing to engage in the kind of\nprohibited conduct specified in the prohibited conduct\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the Treasurer or the Court making that kind or those kinds of\norder in relation to the corporation, or any other connected\nbody corporate in relation to the prohibited conduct, is a\nproportionate means of preventing the corporation, or any\nrelated body corporate, from engaging in that kind of\nprohibited conduct in the future; and\n\n(c) if that kind of order is, or those kinds of order include, a\ndivestiture order—the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result,\nin a benefit to the public;\n\n(ii) if such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to\nresult, in a detriment to the public—the benefit\nmentioned in subparagraph (i) would, or is likely to,\noutweigh that detriment.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be expressed to be given under this section; and\n\n(b) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(c) identify:\n\n(i) the corporation; and\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct mentioned in paragraph (1)(a);\nand\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may give the Treasurer a notice in writing (a\nprohibited conduct recommendation) in respect of the prohibited\nconduct notice, stating one or more recommendations for the kind\nor kinds of order the Treasurer or the Court could make under\nDivision 5 or 6, if the Commission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the corporation has engaged in the kind of prohibited\nconduct specified in the prohibited conduct notice;\n\n(ii) the corporation is continuing to engage in the kind of\nprohibited conduct specified in the prohibited conduct\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the Treasurer or the Court making that kind or those kinds of\norder in relation to the corporation, or any other connected\nbody corporate in relation to the prohibited conduct, is a\nproportionate means of preventing the corporation, or any\nrelated body corporate, from engaging in that kind of\nprohibited conduct in the future; and\n\n(c) if that kind of order is, or those kinds of order include, a\ndivestiture order—the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result,\nin a benefit to the public;\n\n(ii) if such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to\nresult, in a detriment to the public—the benefit\nmentioned in subparagraph (i) would, or is likely to,\noutweigh that detriment.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be expressed to be given under this section; and\n\n(b) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(c) identify:\n\n(i) the corporation; and\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct mentioned in paragraph (1)(a);\nand\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "266ae81ad6a4ad16747fa5e548507599e97899477b4ad32e14edd75f6e86d21f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153S Prohibited conduct recommendations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 445,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may give the Treasurer a notice in writing (a\nprohibited conduct recommendation) in respect of the prohibited\nconduct notice, stating one or more recommendations for the kind\nor kinds of order the Treasurer or the Court could make under\nDivision 5 or 6, if the Commission reasonably believes that:\n\n(a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the corporation has engaged in the kind of prohibited\nconduct specified in the prohibited conduct notice;\n\n(ii) the corporation is continuing to engage in the kind of\nprohibited conduct specified in the prohibited conduct\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the Treasurer or the Court making that kind or those kinds of\norder in relation to the corporation, or any other connected\nbody corporate in relation to the prohibited conduct, is a\nproportionate means of preventing the corporation, or any\nrelated body corporate, from engaging in that kind of\nprohibited conduct in the future; and\n\n(c) if that kind of order is, or those kinds of order include, a\ndivestiture order—the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result,\nin a benefit to the public;\n\n(ii) if such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to\nresult, in a detriment to the public—the benefit\nmentioned in subparagraph (i) would, or is likely to,\noutweigh that detriment.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be expressed to be given under this section; and\n\n(b) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(c) identify:\n\n(i) the corporation; and\n\n(ii) the prohibited conduct mentioned in paragraph (1)(a);\nand\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
