        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Treasurer has made a contracting order in relation to the prohibited conduct recommendation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Treasurer has applied to Court for divestiture order in relation to the prohibited conduct recommendation. During this time, the Commission cannot make variation or revocation under subsection (1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153t-ss-3-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Cannot",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of Commission's action",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Treasurer has applied to Court for divestiture order in relation to the prohibited conduct recommendation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Commission cannot make variation or revocation under subsection (1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153t-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153T(4) Commission may vary or revoke prohibited conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153t-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.446",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission cannot make a variation under subsection (1)\nunless the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the variation is minor or insubstantial; or\n\n(b) all of the following conditions are met:\n\n(i) the corporation or any related body corporate gave the\nCommission information relevant to the prohibited\nconduct notice that is false or misleading in a material\nparticular, or failed to give the Commission information\nrelevant to the prohibited conduct notice that is not\npublicly available;\n\n(ii) the variation is reasonably necessary to address the\ncircumstances described in subparagraph (i); or\n\n(c) the variation is reasonably necessary to address information\nthat was not in existence, or that the Commission did not\nhave, when the prohibited conduct notice was given.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Commission cannot make a variation under subsection (1)\nunless the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the variation is minor or insubstantial; or\n\n(b) all of the following conditions are met:\n\n(i) the corporation or any related body corporate gave the\nCommission information relevant to the prohibited\nconduct notice that is false or misleading in a material\nparticular, or failed to give the Commission information\nrelevant to the prohibited conduct notice that is not\npublicly available;\n\n(ii) the variation is reasonably necessary to address the\ncircumstances described in subparagraph (i); or\n\n(c) the variation is reasonably necessary to address information\nthat was not in existence, or that the Commission did not\nhave, when the prohibited conduct notice was given.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153t"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153t-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153t-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f05119fc7b33f609461d8427a7f34a3d444b9acb82b50efadb1d952d95d19f96",
      "skos:note": "Commission may not make a variation under subsection (1) unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153t-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153T(4) Commission may vary or revoke prohibited conduct",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 446,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission cannot make a variation under subsection (1)\nunless the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the variation is minor or insubstantial; or\n\n(b) all of the following conditions are met:\n\n(i) the corporation or any related body corporate gave the\nCommission information relevant to the prohibited\nconduct notice that is false or misleading in a material\nparticular, or failed to give the Commission information\nrelevant to the prohibited conduct notice that is not\npublicly available;\n\n(ii) the variation is reasonably necessary to address the\ncircumstances described in subparagraph (i); or\n\n(c) the variation is reasonably necessary to address information\nthat was not in existence, or that the Commission did not\nhave, when the prohibited conduct notice was given."
    },
