    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153U No Treasurer action notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.448",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission must give the Treasurer a notice in writing (a no\nTreasurer action notice) in respect of the prohibited conduct\nnotice mentioned in section 153R if the Commission considers that\nit is not appropriate to give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct\nrecommendation in respect of the prohibited conduct notice.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be expressed to be given under this section; and\n\n(b) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(c) explain the reasons why the Commission considers that it is\nnot appropriate to give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct\nrecommendation in respect of the prohibited conduct notice.\n\n(3) The Commission must give a copy of the notice to the corporation:\n\n(a) unless paragraph (b) applies—45 days after issuing it; or\n\n(b) if the Commission and the Treasurer agree that it is\nappropriate to give a copy of the notice to the corporation at\nan earlier time—at that earlier time.\n\n(4) A no Treasurer action notice is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission must give the Treasurer a notice in writing (a no\nTreasurer action notice) in respect of the prohibited conduct\nnotice mentioned in section 153R if the Commission considers that\nit is not appropriate to give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct\nrecommendation in respect of the prohibited conduct notice.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be expressed to be given under this section; and\n\n(b) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(c) explain the reasons why the Commission considers that it is\nnot appropriate to give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct\nrecommendation in respect of the prohibited conduct notice.\n\n(3) The Commission must give a copy of the notice to the corporation:\n\n(a) unless paragraph (b) applies—45 days after issuing it; or\n\n(b) if the Commission and the Treasurer agree that it is\nappropriate to give a copy of the notice to the corporation at\nan earlier time—at that earlier time.\n\n(4) A no Treasurer action notice is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153u-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153u-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153u-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153u-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04ccf0bf1599d4fd187425fd80d55938b593ec5f68495e014102979f0490ce9a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153U No Treasurer action notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 448,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission must give the Treasurer a notice in writing (a no\nTreasurer action notice) in respect of the prohibited conduct\nnotice mentioned in section 153R if the Commission considers that\nit is not appropriate to give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct\nrecommendation in respect of the prohibited conduct notice.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) be expressed to be given under this section; and\n\n(b) state the day on which the notice is given; and\n\n(c) explain the reasons why the Commission considers that it is\nnot appropriate to give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct\nrecommendation in respect of the prohibited conduct notice.\n\n(3) The Commission must give a copy of the notice to the corporation:\n\n(a) unless paragraph (b) applies—45 days after issuing it; or\n\n(b) if the Commission and the Treasurer agree that it is\nappropriate to give a copy of the notice to the corporation at\nan earlier time—at that earlier time.\n\n(4) A no Treasurer action notice is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153u-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153U(1) No Treasurer action notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
