    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153v-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153V(5) Commission may vary or revoke no Treasurer action notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153v-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.448",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The condition in this subsection is met if the Commission\nreasonably believes that it is appropriate to:\n\n(a) give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct recommendation in\nrespect of the prohibited conduct notice; or\n\n(b) give the corporation a new prohibited conduct notice in\nrespect of the prohibited conduct identified in the prohibited\nconduct notice (in accordance with\nsubparagraph 153P(2)(c)(ii)).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The condition in this subsection is met if the Commission\nreasonably believes that it is appropriate to:\n\n(a) give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct recommendation in\nrespect of the prohibited conduct notice; or\n\n(b) give the corporation a new prohibited conduct notice in\nrespect of the prohibited conduct identified in the prohibited\nconduct notice (in accordance with\nsubparagraph 153P(2)(c)(ii)).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153v"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153v-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153v-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7d143fec1d0ad98c8549663d5e60133649d6e42b362c0f76159a6251f220372",
      "skos:note": "Commission may give Treasurer a prohibited conduct recommendation or corporation a new notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153v-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153V(5) Commission may vary or revoke no Treasurer action notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 448,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The condition in this subsection is met if the Commission\nreasonably believes that it is appropriate to:\n\n(a) give the Treasurer a prohibited conduct recommendation in\nrespect of the prohibited conduct notice; or\n\n(b) give the corporation a new prohibited conduct notice in\nrespect of the prohibited conduct identified in the prohibited\nconduct notice (in accordance with\nsubparagraph 153P(2)(c)(ii))."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153v-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153v-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
