      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.453",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Treasurer may, in writing, vary or revoke a contracting order\nin respect of a body corporate, on the Treasurer’s own initiative or\non application made by the body corporate.\n\n(2) The Treasurer cannot make a variation under subsection (1) unless\nthe Treasurer is satisfied that:\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Treasurer may, in writing, vary or revoke a contracting order\nin respect of a body corporate, on the Treasurer’s own initiative or\non application made by the body corporate.\n\n(2) The Treasurer cannot make a variation under subsection (1) unless\nthe Treasurer is satisfied that:\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
