    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153Z Enforcement of contracting orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.455",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the Treasurer has made a contracting order\nin respect of a body corporate.\n\n(2) If the Commission considers that the body corporate has failed to\ncomply with the contracting order, the Commission may apply to\nthe Court for an order under subsection (3).\n\n(3) If the Court is satisfied that the body corporate has failed to comply\nwith the contracting order, the Court may make all or any of the\nfollowing orders:\n\n(a) an order directing the body corporate to comply with the\ncontracting order;\n\n(b) if the period or periods specified in the contracting order (in\naccordance with paragraph 153X(3)(d)) have already\npassed—an order directing the body corporate to comply\nwith the contracting order, within a new period, or new\nperiods, specified in the order;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the Treasurer has made a contracting order\nin respect of a body corporate.\n\n(2) If the Commission considers that the body corporate has failed to\ncomply with the contracting order, the Commission may apply to\nthe Court for an order under subsection (3).\n\n(3) If the Court is satisfied that the body corporate has failed to comply\nwith the contracting order, the Court may make all or any of the\nfollowing orders:\n\n(a) an order directing the body corporate to comply with the\ncontracting order;\n\n(b) if the period or periods specified in the contracting order (in\naccordance with paragraph 153X(3)(d)) have already\npassed—an order directing the body corporate to comply\nwith the contracting order, within a new period, or new\nperiods, specified in the order;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153z-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153z-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153z-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "036330628c4552ed79a5682da50f02719160a5c894238b6666b5a9cae00ca2d3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-153z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153Z Enforcement of contracting orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 455,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the Treasurer has made a contracting order\nin respect of a body corporate.\n\n(2) If the Commission considers that the body corporate has failed to\ncomply with the contracting order, the Commission may apply to\nthe Court for an order under subsection (3).\n\n(3) If the Court is satisfied that the body corporate has failed to comply\nwith the contracting order, the Court may make all or any of the\nfollowing orders:\n\n(a) an order directing the body corporate to comply with the\ncontracting order;\n\n(b) if the period or periods specified in the contracting order (in\naccordance with paragraph 153X(3)(d)) have already\npassed—an order directing the body corporate to comply\nwith the contracting order, within a new period, or new\nperiods, specified in the order;\n\n(c) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."
    },
