    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154D Entry with consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.496",
      "values:originalText": "Entry\n\n(1) An inspector may enter premises if:\n\n(a) the Commission, the Chairperson or a Deputy Chairperson\nhas reasonable grounds for suspecting that there may be\nevidential material on the premises; and\n\n(b) the inspector obtains the consent of the occupier of the\npremises to enter the premises.\n\n(2) The inspector may be accompanied by any one or more of the\nfollowing persons (each of whom is an assistant):\n\n(a) another member of the staff assisting the Commission;\n\n(b) a consultant.\nObtaining consent\n\n(3) Before obtaining the consent of a person to enter premises under\nthis Division, the inspector must inform the person that the person\nmay refuse consent.\n\n(4) A consent of a person is not effective for the purposes of this\nsection unless it is voluntary.",
      "skos:definition": "Entry\n\n(1) An inspector may enter premises if:\n\n(a) the Commission, the Chairperson or a Deputy Chairperson\nhas reasonable grounds for suspecting that there may be\nevidential material on the premises; and\n\n(b) the inspector obtains the consent of the occupier of the\npremises to enter the premises.\n\n(2) The inspector may be accompanied by any one or more of the\nfollowing persons (each of whom is an assistant):\n\n(a) another member of the staff assisting the Commission;\n\n(b) a consultant.\nObtaining consent\n\n(3) Before obtaining the consent of a person to enter premises under\nthis Division, the inspector must inform the person that the person\nmay refuse consent.\n\n(4) A consent of a person is not effective for the purposes of this\nsection unless it is voluntary.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154d-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2649e082d9a2ba377ac918877028c3f1885e2e9ab926b216943aaf06064b92a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154D Entry with consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 496,
      "values:originalText": "Entry\n\n(1) An inspector may enter premises if:\n\n(a) the Commission, the Chairperson or a Deputy Chairperson\nhas reasonable grounds for suspecting that there may be\nevidential material on the premises; and\n\n(b) the inspector obtains the consent of the occupier of the\npremises to enter the premises.\n\n(2) The inspector may be accompanied by any one or more of the\nfollowing persons (each of whom is an assistant):\n\n(a) another member of the staff assisting the Commission;\n\n(b) a consultant.\nObtaining consent\n\n(3) Before obtaining the consent of a person to enter premises under\nthis Division, the inspector must inform the person that the person\nmay refuse consent.\n\n(4) A consent of a person is not effective for the purposes of this\nsection unless it is voluntary."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154d-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154D(1) Entry with consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
