      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.496",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The inspector or an assistant may do any of the following after\nentering premises under this Division:\n\n(a) search the premises, and any thing on the premises, for the\nevidential material;\n\n(b) make copies of the evidential material found on the premises;\n\n(c) operate electronic equipment at the premises to see whether\nthe evidential material is accessible by doing so;\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises with consent  Division 3\n\nSection 154F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nSee also Division 5 (which contains provisions relating to the\noperation of electronic equipment at the premises).\n\n(d) remove the evidential material from the premises with the\nconsent of the owner of the material;\nNote:\nSee also subsection (2).\n\n(e) secure the evidential material, pending the obtaining of a\nsearch warrant to seize it;\n\n(f) take equipment and material onto the premises, and use it, for\nany of the above purposes.\nObtaining consent to remove evidential material",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The inspector or an assistant may do any of the following after\nentering premises under this Division:\n\n(a) search the premises, and any thing on the premises, for the\nevidential material;\n\n(b) make copies of the evidential material found on the premises;\n\n(c) operate electronic equipment at the premises to see whether\nthe evidential material is accessible by doing so;\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises with consent  Division 3\n\nSection 154F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nSee also Division 5 (which contains provisions relating to the\noperation of electronic equipment at the premises).\n\n(d) remove the evidential material from the premises with the\nconsent of the owner of the material;\nNote:\nSee also subsection (2).\n\n(e) secure the evidential material, pending the obtaining of a\nsearch warrant to seize it;\n\n(f) take equipment and material onto the premises, and use it, for\nany of the above purposes.\nObtaining consent to remove evidential material",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bd162f7d48591f711a7ec03a5ab7b73112e79c778a05984a7901075bdee22e1e",
      "skos:note": "Inspectors and assistants have the obligation to search premises, make copies of evidential material, operate electronic equipment, remove evidential material with consent, secure it pending a warrant, and take equipment onto premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154e-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154E(1) Powers in relation to premises",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 496,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The inspector or an assistant may do any of the following after\nentering premises under this Division:\n\n(a) search the premises, and any thing on the premises, for the\nevidential material;\n\n(b) make copies of the evidential material found on the premises;\n\n(c) operate electronic equipment at the premises to see whether\nthe evidential material is accessible by doing so;\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises with consent  Division 3\n\nSection 154F\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNote:\nSee also Division 5 (which contains provisions relating to the\noperation of electronic equipment at the premises).\n\n(d) remove the evidential material from the premises with the\nconsent of the owner of the material;\nNote:\nSee also subsection (2).\n\n(e) secure the evidential material, pending the obtaining of a\nsearch warrant to seize it;\n\n(f) take equipment and material onto the premises, and use it, for\nany of the above purposes.\nObtaining consent to remove evidential material"
    },
