    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154E(2) Powers in relation to premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154e-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.496",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before obtaining the consent of a person to remove evidential\nmaterial from premises under paragraph (1)(d), the inspector or an\nassistant must inform the person of the purpose for which the\nmaterial is required and that the person may refuse consent. A\nconsent of a person is not effective for the purposes of that\nparagraph unless the consent is voluntary.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Before obtaining the consent of a person to remove evidential\nmaterial from premises under paragraph (1)(d), the inspector or an\nassistant must inform the person of the purpose for which the\nmaterial is required and that the person may refuse consent. A\nconsent of a person is not effective for the purposes of that\nparagraph unless the consent is voluntary.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154e-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9eea6d67082b14c88c0d3cb20976c3810dd69d74667d17f9faa3f0d3021fa3c",
      "skos:note": "Inspector must inform person of purpose and obtain voluntary consent before removing evidential material.",
      "dc:description": "Consent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154e-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154E(2) Powers in relation to premises",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 496,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before obtaining the consent of a person to remove evidential\nmaterial from premises under paragraph (1)(d), the inspector or an\nassistant must inform the person of the purpose for which the\nmaterial is required and that the person may refuse consent. A\nconsent of a person is not effective for the purposes of that\nparagraph unless the consent is voluntary."
    },
    {
