      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.500",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A thing found at the premises may be moved to another place for\nexamination or processing in order to determine whether it may be\nseized under a search warrant if:\n\n(a) both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) it is significantly more practicable to do so having\nregard to the timeliness and cost of examining or\nprocessing the thing at another place and the availability\nof expert assistance;\n\n(ii) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the thing\ncontains or constitutes evidential material; or\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises consents in writing.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154H\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNotice to occupier",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A thing found at the premises may be moved to another place for\nexamination or processing in order to determine whether it may be\nseized under a search warrant if:\n\n(a) both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) it is significantly more practicable to do so having\nregard to the timeliness and cost of examining or\nprocessing the thing at another place and the availability\nof expert assistance;\n\n(ii) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the thing\ncontains or constitutes evidential material; or\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises consents in writing.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154H\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNotice to occupier",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ga"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ga-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ga-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e3751c56ba4cc23b13440b398f8c7e423b250a9e047ad6a6d16d46a074416d0d",
      "skos:note": "Move thing for examination or processing with reasonable grounds and consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154ga-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154GA(1) Removing things for examination or processing",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 500,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A thing found at the premises may be moved to another place for\nexamination or processing in order to determine whether it may be\nseized under a search warrant if:\n\n(a) both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) it is significantly more practicable to do so having\nregard to the timeliness and cost of examining or\nprocessing the thing at another place and the availability\nof expert assistance;\n\n(ii) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the thing\ncontains or constitutes evidential material; or\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises consents in writing.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154H\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nNotice to occupier"
    },
