    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154J Securing electronic equipment for use by experts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.503",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable\ngrounds that:\n\n(a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may\nbe accessible by operating electronic equipment at the\npremises; and\n\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.\nNotice to occupier\n\n(2) The executing officer or officer assisting must give notice to the\noccupier of the premises of his or her intention to secure the\nequipment and of the fact that the equipment may be secured for up\nto 24 hours.\nPeriod equipment may be secured\n\n(3) The equipment may be secured:\n\n(a) for a period not exceeding 24 hours; or\n\n(b) until the equipment has been operated by the expert;\nwhichever happens first.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable\ngrounds that:\n\n(a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may\nbe accessible by operating electronic equipment at the\npremises; and\n\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.\nNotice to occupier\n\n(2) The executing officer or officer assisting must give notice to the\noccupier of the premises of his or her intention to secure the\nequipment and of the fact that the equipment may be secured for up\nto 24 hours.\nPeriod equipment may be secured\n\n(3) The equipment may be secured:\n\n(a) for a period not exceeding 24 hours; or\n\n(b) until the equipment has been operated by the expert;\nwhichever happens first.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "39d7956e7c480ace3c5ba2edfc434a333a8948baf4443f08fde1351be5d48df0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154J Securing electronic equipment for use by experts",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 503,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable\ngrounds that:\n\n(a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may\nbe accessible by operating electronic equipment at the\npremises; and\n\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.\nNotice to occupier\n\n(2) The executing officer or officer assisting must give notice to the\noccupier of the premises of his or her intention to secure the\nequipment and of the fact that the equipment may be secured for up\nto 24 hours.\nPeriod equipment may be secured\n\n(3) The equipment may be secured:\n\n(a) for a period not exceeding 24 hours; or\n\n(b) until the equipment has been operated by the expert;\nwhichever happens first.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
