    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154j-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154J(1) Securing electronic equipment for use by experts",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 503,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable\ngrounds that:\n\n(a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may\nbe accessible by operating electronic equipment at the\npremises; and\n\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.\nNotice to occupier"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
