    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154L Availability of assistance and use of force in executing a search",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.504",
      "values:originalText": "warrant\n\nIn executing a search warrant:\n\n(a) the executing officer may obtain such assistance as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(b) the executing officer, or another inspector who is an officer\nassisting, may use such force against persons and things as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(ba) a member of the Australian Federal Police who is an officer\nassisting may use such force against persons and things as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) a person who is not an inspector, but who is an officer\nassisting, may use such force against things as is necessary\nand reasonable in the circumstances.\nSubdivision C—Obligations of executing officer and officers\nassisting",
      "skos:definition": "warrant\n\nIn executing a search warrant:\n\n(a) the executing officer may obtain such assistance as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(b) the executing officer, or another inspector who is an officer\nassisting, may use such force against persons and things as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(ba) a member of the Australian Federal Police who is an officer\nassisting may use such force against persons and things as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) a person who is not an inspector, but who is an officer\nassisting, may use such force against things as is necessary\nand reasonable in the circumstances.\nSubdivision C—Obligations of executing officer and officers\nassisting",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154l-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154l-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e778ecea7a97f84403872e450d20c51df0f8cd2bfdebf1dc159aaff07ff3f47b",
      "skos:note": "Executing officer may obtain assistance and use force as necessary and reasonable in circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154L Availability of assistance and use of force in executing a search",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 504,
      "values:originalText": "warrant\n\nIn executing a search warrant:\n\n(a) the executing officer may obtain such assistance as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(b) the executing officer, or another inspector who is an officer\nassisting, may use such force against persons and things as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\n(ba) a member of the Australian Federal Police who is an officer\nassisting may use such force against persons and things as is\nnecessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154M\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(c) a person who is not an inspector, but who is an officer\nassisting, may use such force against things as is necessary\nand reasonable in the circumstances.\nSubdivision C—Obligations of executing officer and officers\nassisting"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154l-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154l"
      },
