      },
      "cml:operator": "May",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Executing officer has a duty to obtain assistance and use force as necessary and reasonable in circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154M Announcement before entry",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.505",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before any person enters premises under a search warrant, the\nexecuting officer must:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) However, the executing officer is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required to ensure that the\neffective execution of the warrant is not frustrated.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before any person enters premises under a search warrant, the\nexecuting officer must:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) However, the executing officer is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required to ensure that the\neffective execution of the warrant is not frustrated.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154m-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "94387bcb44c0e610050819f08fe3378e623bb3e83bd4c35d77edf1370d0d02e7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154M Announcement before entry",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 505,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before any person enters premises under a search warrant, the\nexecuting officer must:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) However, the executing officer is not required to comply with\nsubsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that\nimmediate entry to the premises is required to ensure that the\neffective execution of the warrant is not frustrated."
    },
