    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "149 Section 149",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-149"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.506",
      "values:originalText": "1 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Part.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154RA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n154RA  Person with computer knowledge to assist access etc.\n\n(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a\nmagistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any\ninformation or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow\nthe officer to do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer that is on\npremises to which the warrant relates;\n\n(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;\n\n(c) convert the data into documentary form.\n\n(2) The magistrate may grant the order if the magistrate is satisfied\nthat:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that evidential\nmaterial is held in, or is accessible from, the computer; and\n\n(b) the specified person is:\n\n(i) reasonably suspected of having committed the\ncontravention, or one or more of the contraventions,\nstated in the search warrant; or\n\n(ii) the owner or lessee of the computer; or\n\n(iii) an employee of the owner or lessee of the computer; and\n\n(c) the specified person has relevant knowledge of:\n\n(i) the computer or a computer network of which the\ncomputer forms a part; or\n\n(ii) measures applied to protect data held in, or accessible\nfrom, the computer.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under this section; and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the order.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "1 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Part.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154RA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n154RA  Person with computer knowledge to assist access etc.\n\n(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a\nmagistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any\ninformation or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow\nthe officer to do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer that is on\npremises to which the warrant relates;\n\n(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;\n\n(c) convert the data into documentary form.\n\n(2) The magistrate may grant the order if the magistrate is satisfied\nthat:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that evidential\nmaterial is held in, or is accessible from, the computer; and\n\n(b) the specified person is:\n\n(i) reasonably suspected of having committed the\ncontravention, or one or more of the contraventions,\nstated in the search warrant; or\n\n(ii) the owner or lessee of the computer; or\n\n(iii) an employee of the owner or lessee of the computer; and\n\n(c) the specified person has relevant knowledge of:\n\n(i) the computer or a computer network of which the\ncomputer forms a part; or\n\n(ii) measures applied to protect data held in, or accessible\nfrom, the computer.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under this section; and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the order.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43263c1c898f92a7085247bb35e6ce7d97c04f0ca46ff2a4aaf4bf6341c137af"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-149",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "149 Section 149",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 506,
      "values:originalText": "1 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Part.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154RA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n154RA  Person with computer knowledge to assist access etc.\n\n(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a\nmagistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any\ninformation or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow\nthe officer to do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer that is on\npremises to which the warrant relates;\n\n(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;\n\n(c) convert the data into documentary form.\n\n(2) The magistrate may grant the order if the magistrate is satisfied\nthat:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that evidential\nmaterial is held in, or is accessible from, the computer; and\n\n(b) the specified person is:\n\n(i) reasonably suspected of having committed the\ncontravention, or one or more of the contraventions,\nstated in the search warrant; or\n\n(ii) the owner or lessee of the computer; or\n\n(iii) an employee of the owner or lessee of the computer; and\n\n(c) the specified person has relevant knowledge of:\n\n(i) the computer or a computer network of which the\ncomputer forms a part; or\n\n(ii) measures applied to protect data held in, or accessible\nfrom, the computer.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under this section; and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the order.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "149(1) Section 149",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-149-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.506",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a\nmagistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any\ninformation or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow\nthe officer to do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer that is on\npremises to which the warrant relates;\n\n(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;\n\n(c) convert the data into documentary form.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a\nmagistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any\ninformation or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow\nthe officer to do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer that is on\npremises to which the warrant relates;\n\n(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;\n\n(c) convert the data into documentary form.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9ed57f3cf236f48d52bdeaaf3021cf3cd9e22a838581b9359408fefd7675d978",
      "skos:note": "The executing officer may request a specified person to provide information or assistance."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-149-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "149(1) Section 149",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 506,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a\nmagistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any\ninformation or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow\nthe officer to do one or more of the following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer that is on\npremises to which the warrant relates;\n\n(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;\n\n(c) convert the data into documentary form."
    },
    {
