      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) The executing officer for a search warrant may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any information or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow the officer to do one or more of the following:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Potential impact on data access",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) transfer the data to a disk, tape or other storage device;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "149(2) Section 149",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-149-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.506",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The magistrate may grant the order if the magistrate is satisfied\nthat:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that evidential\nmaterial is held in, or is accessible from, the computer; and\n\n(b) the specified person is:\n\n(i) reasonably suspected of having committed the\ncontravention, or one or more of the contraventions,\nstated in the search warrant; or\n\n(ii) the owner or lessee of the computer; or\n\n(iii) an employee of the owner or lessee of the computer; and\n\n(c) the specified person has relevant knowledge of:\n\n(i) the computer or a computer network of which the\ncomputer forms a part; or\n\n(ii) measures applied to protect data held in, or accessible\nfrom, the computer.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The magistrate may grant the order if the magistrate is satisfied\nthat:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that evidential\nmaterial is held in, or is accessible from, the computer; and\n\n(b) the specified person is:\n\n(i) reasonably suspected of having committed the\ncontravention, or one or more of the contraventions,\nstated in the search warrant; or\n\n(ii) the owner or lessee of the computer; or\n\n(iii) an employee of the owner or lessee of the computer; and\n\n(c) the specified person has relevant knowledge of:\n\n(i) the computer or a computer network of which the\ncomputer forms a part; or\n\n(ii) measures applied to protect data held in, or accessible\nfrom, the computer.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-149-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "00e2acc269d5a681c535cd273ede907b4518ff11d43bd85ae9676fa4c4686ebd",
      "skos:note": "Grant order if reasonable grounds exist for suspecting evidential material is held in or accessible from the computer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-149-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "149(2) Section 149",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 506,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The magistrate may grant the order if the magistrate is satisfied\nthat:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that evidential\nmaterial is held in, or is accessible from, the computer; and\n\n(b) the specified person is:\n\n(i) reasonably suspected of having committed the\ncontravention, or one or more of the contraventions,\nstated in the search warrant; or\n\n(ii) the owner or lessee of the computer; or\n\n(iii) an employee of the owner or lessee of the computer; and\n\n(c) the specified person has relevant knowledge of:\n\n(i) the computer or a computer network of which the\ncomputer forms a part; or\n\n(ii) measures applied to protect data held in, or accessible\nfrom, the computer."
    },
