    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154S Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.508",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, under a search warrant relating to premises, the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting seizes:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthen he or she must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, give a copy of the thing or the information to the\noccupier as soon as practicable after the seizure.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply if possession of the\ndocument, film, computer file, thing or information by the occupier\ncould constitute an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, under a search warrant relating to premises, the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting seizes:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthen he or she must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, give a copy of the thing or the information to the\noccupier as soon as practicable after the seizure.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply if possession of the\ndocument, film, computer file, thing or information by the occupier\ncould constitute an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f09f9f8f06c493d970c5f577a3ebe46c180bd351440f41cb4e5ca68dad228c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154S Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 508,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, under a search warrant relating to premises, the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting seizes:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthen he or she must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, give a copy of the thing or the information to the\noccupier as soon as practicable after the seizure.\n\n(2) However, subsection (1) does not apply if possession of the\ndocument, film, computer file, thing or information by the occupier\ncould constitute an offence against a law of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154S(1) Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154s-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.508",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, under a search warrant relating to premises, the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting seizes:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthen he or she must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, give a copy of the thing or the information to the\noccupier as soon as practicable after the seizure.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, under a search warrant relating to premises, the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting seizes:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthen he or she must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, give a copy of the thing or the information to the\noccupier as soon as practicable after the seizure.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154s-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "54abf73ac95b2236909efd8a2df084a0e9ff4788f861ce20aac0da1c16c6c8de",
      "skos:note": "Must provide a copy of seized documents or information to the occupier upon request.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154s-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154S(1) Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 508,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, under a search warrant relating to premises, the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting seizes:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthen he or she must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, give a copy of the thing or the information to the\noccupier as soon as practicable after the seizure."
    },
