    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154u-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154U(2) Return of seized things",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154u-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.508",
      "values:originalText": "(2) At the end of the 120 days specified in subsection (1), the seizer\nmust take reasonable steps to return the thing to the person from\nwhom it was seized (or to the owner if that person is not entitled to\npossess it), unless:\n\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 120 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n\n(b) an inspector may retain the thing because of an order under\nsection 154V; or\n\n(c) the seizer is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an order of a\ncourt, of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory) to\nretain, destroy or dispose of the thing.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) At the end of the 120 days specified in subsection (1), the seizer\nmust take reasonable steps to return the thing to the person from\nwhom it was seized (or to the owner if that person is not entitled to\npossess it), unless:\n\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 120 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n\n(b) an inspector may retain the thing because of an order under\nsection 154V; or\n\n(c) the seizer is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an order of a\ncourt, of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory) to\nretain, destroy or dispose of the thing.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154u"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154u-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154u-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b54d64d193c4e69782557119ddb2d1a256806c4cf2e6c4ede5aff84b37be9c7e",
      "skos:note": "Return seized thing within 120 days or face legal consequences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154u-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154U(2) Return of seized things",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 508,
      "values:originalText": "(2) At the end of the 120 days specified in subsection (1), the seizer\nmust take reasonable steps to return the thing to the person from\nwhom it was seized (or to the owner if that person is not entitled to\npossess it), unless:\n\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 120 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n\n(b) an inspector may retain the thing because of an order under\nsection 154V; or\n\n(c) the seizer is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an order of a\ncourt, of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory) to\nretain, destroy or dispose of the thing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154u-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
