      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.509",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the magistrate is satisfied that it is necessary for the inspector to\ncontinue to retain the thing for the purposes of an investigation as\nto whether there has been:\n\n(a) a contravention of this Act, a gas market instrument or the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(b) a contravention of Part 20 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n\n(c) a contravention of Part 9 of the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the magistrate is satisfied that it is necessary for the inspector to\ncontinue to retain the thing for the purposes of an investigation as\nto whether there has been:\n\n(a) a contravention of this Act, a gas market instrument or the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(b) a contravention of Part 20 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n\n(c) a contravention of Part 9 of the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154v"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154v-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154v-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2562924cb6223d61ae799c51ca0ac130282c74fecf0eaa4b2ea51763b38ade3",
      "skos:note": "Magistrate may permit a thing to be retained"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154v-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154V(2) Magistrate may permit a thing to be retained",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 509,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the magistrate is satisfied that it is necessary for the inspector to\ncontinue to retain the thing for the purposes of an investigation as\nto whether there has been:\n\n(a) a contravention of this Act, a gas market instrument or the\nconsumer data rules; or\n\n(b) a contravention of Part 20 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n\n(c) a contravention of Part 9 of the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154v-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
