    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154w",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154W Disposal of things if there is no owner or owner cannot be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154w"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.510",
      "values:originalText": "located\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a thing is seized under this Division; and\n\n(b) a person would otherwise be required to return the thing to its\nowner; and\n\n(c) there is no owner or the person cannot, despite making\nreasonable efforts, locate the owner;\nthe person may dispose of the thing in such manner as he or she\nthinks appropriate.\nSubdivision F—Search warrants",
      "skos:definition": "located\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a thing is seized under this Division; and\n\n(b) a person would otherwise be required to return the thing to its\nowner; and\n\n(c) there is no owner or the person cannot, despite making\nreasonable efforts, locate the owner;\nthe person may dispose of the thing in such manner as he or she\nthinks appropriate.\nSubdivision F—Search warrants",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154w-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154w-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26dc5989c899d9ca19f21be056334467c1409dc89c13af19195e6faeba25eb73",
      "skos:note": "Dispose of thing if owner cannot be located"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154w",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154W Disposal of things if there is no owner or owner cannot be",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 510,
      "values:originalText": "located\n\nIf:\n\n(a) a thing is seized under this Division; and\n\n(b) a person would otherwise be required to return the thing to its\nowner; and\n\n(c) there is no owner or the person cannot, despite making\nreasonable efforts, locate the owner;\nthe person may dispose of the thing in such manner as he or she\nthinks appropriate.\nSubdivision F—Search warrants"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154w-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154w"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154w-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Grant permission to dispose of thing",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "No owner or person cannot locate owner",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Dispose of thing in appropriate manner"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154x",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154X Issue of search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154x"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.510",
      "values:originalText": "Application for warrant\n\n(1) An inspector may apply to a magistrate for a warrant under this\nsection in relation to premises.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154X\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nIssue of warrant\n\n(2) The magistrate may issue the warrant if the magistrate is satisfied,\nby information on oath or affirmation, that there are reasonable\ngrounds for suspecting that:\n\n(a) there is evidential material on the premises; or\n\n(b) there may be evidential material on the premises within the\nnext 72 hours.\nNote:\nA magistrate who holds office under a law of a State or Territory may\nissue a warrant in relation to premises even if those premises are not\nin that State or Territory.\n\n(3) However, the magistrate must not issue the warrant unless the\ninspector or some other person has given to the magistrate, either\norally or by affidavit, such further information (if any) as the\nmagistrate requires concerning the grounds on which the issue of\nthe warrant is being sought.\nContent of warrant\n\n(4) The warrant must state:\n\n(a) a description of the premises to which the warrant relates;\nand\n\n(b) the kind of evidential material that is to be searched for under\nthe warrant (including stating the contraventions to which the\nwarrant relates); and\n\n(c) the name of the inspector who is to be responsible for\nexecuting the warrant; and\n\n(d) whether the warrant may be executed at any time of the day\nor night or during specified hours of the day or night; and\n\n(e) the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "Application for warrant\n\n(1) An inspector may apply to a magistrate for a warrant under this\nsection in relation to premises.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154X\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nIssue of warrant\n\n(2) The magistrate may issue the warrant if the magistrate is satisfied,\nby information on oath or affirmation, that there are reasonable\ngrounds for suspecting that:\n\n(a) there is evidential material on the premises; or\n\n(b) there may be evidential material on the premises within the\nnext 72 hours.\nNote:\nA magistrate who holds office under a law of a State or Territory may\nissue a warrant in relation to premises even if those premises are not\nin that State or Territory.\n\n(3) However, the magistrate must not issue the warrant unless the\ninspector or some other person has given to the magistrate, either\norally or by affidavit, such further information (if any) as the\nmagistrate requires concerning the grounds on which the issue of\nthe warrant is being sought.\nContent of warrant\n\n(4) The warrant must state:\n\n(a) a description of the premises to which the warrant relates;\nand\n\n(b) the kind of evidential material that is to be searched for under\nthe warrant (including stating the contraventions to which the\nwarrant relates); and\n\n(c) the name of the inspector who is to be responsible for\nexecuting the warrant; and\n\n(d) whether the warrant may be executed at any time of the day\nor night or during specified hours of the day or night; and\n\n(e) the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154x-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154x-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154x-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154x-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8642386535e56cb21f292843aef8a764cdcc5e226d757ff570290f1f9732914b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154x",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154X Issue of search warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 510,
      "values:originalText": "Application for warrant\n\n(1) An inspector may apply to a magistrate for a warrant under this\nsection in relation to premises.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nEntry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4\n\nSection 154X\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nIssue of warrant\n\n(2) The magistrate may issue the warrant if the magistrate is satisfied,\nby information on oath or affirmation, that there are reasonable\ngrounds for suspecting that:\n\n(a) there is evidential material on the premises; or\n\n(b) there may be evidential material on the premises within the\nnext 72 hours.\nNote:\nA magistrate who holds office under a law of a State or Territory may\nissue a warrant in relation to premises even if those premises are not\nin that State or Territory.\n\n(3) However, the magistrate must not issue the warrant unless the\ninspector or some other person has given to the magistrate, either\norally or by affidavit, such further information (if any) as the\nmagistrate requires concerning the grounds on which the issue of\nthe warrant is being sought.\nContent of warrant\n\n(4) The warrant must state:\n\n(a) a description of the premises to which the warrant relates;\nand\n\n(b) the kind of evidential material that is to be searched for under\nthe warrant (including stating the contraventions to which the\nwarrant relates); and\n\n(c) the name of the inspector who is to be responsible for\nexecuting the warrant; and\n\n(d) whether the warrant may be executed at any time of the day\nor night or during specified hours of the day or night; and\n\n(e) the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
