    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154za",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZA Powers conferred on magistrates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154za"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.515",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A power conferred on a magistrate by this Division is conferred on\nthe magistrate in a personal capacity and not as a court or a\nmember of a court. The magistrate need not accept the power\nconferred.\n\n(2) A magistrate exercising such a power has the same protection and\nimmunity as if he or she were exercising that power as, or as a\nmember of, the court of which the magistrate is a member.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A power conferred on a magistrate by this Division is conferred on\nthe magistrate in a personal capacity and not as a court or a\nmember of a court. The magistrate need not accept the power\nconferred.\n\n(2) A magistrate exercising such a power has the same protection and\nimmunity as if he or she were exercising that power as, or as a\nmember of, the court of which the magistrate is a member.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154za-ss-1"
        },
