    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZB Operation of electronic equipment at premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.516",
      "values:originalText": "A person may operate electronic equipment at premises in order to\nexercise a power under this Part only if he or she believes on\nreasonable grounds that the operation of the equipment can be\ncarried out without damage to the equipment.",
      "skos:definition": "A person may operate electronic equipment at premises in order to\nexercise a power under this Part only if he or she believes on\nreasonable grounds that the operation of the equipment can be\ncarried out without damage to the equipment.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zb-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7456acfc44804491627e7ea9aa1f5e252fbc5d7f4de4c2486c748a6da028ab79",
      "skos:note": "Permission to operate electronic equipment under reasonable grounds."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZB Operation of electronic equipment at premises",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 516,
      "values:originalText": "A person may operate electronic equipment at premises in order to\nexercise a power under this Part only if he or she believes on\nreasonable grounds that the operation of the equipment can be\ncarried out without damage to the equipment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zb-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zb"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:NaturalPerson"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: NaturalPerson"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZC Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.516",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) as a result of electronic equipment being operated as\nmentioned in section 154E, 154F, 154G, 154H or 154J:\n\n(i) damage is caused to the equipment; or\n\n(ii) the data recorded on the equipment is damaged; or\n\n(iii) programs associated with the use of the equipment, or\nwith the use of the data, are damaged or corrupted; and\n\n(b) the damage or corruption occurs because:\n\n(i) insufficient care was exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the equipment; or\n\n(ii) insufficient care was exercised by the person operating\nthe equipment.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must pay the owner of the equipment, or the\nuser of the data or programs, such reasonable compensation for the\ndamage or corruption as the Commonwealth and the owner or user\nagree on.\n\n(3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to\nagree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal\nCourt of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as\nthe Court determines.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nGeneral provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5\n\nSection 154ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises, or the occupier’s\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, provided\nany appropriate warning or guidance on the operation of the\nequipment.\n\n(5) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament.\n\n(6) For the purposes of subsection (1):\ndamage, in relation to data, includes damage by erasure of data or\naddition of other data.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) as a result of electronic equipment being operated as\nmentioned in section 154E, 154F, 154G, 154H or 154J:\n\n(i) damage is caused to the equipment; or\n\n(ii) the data recorded on the equipment is damaged; or\n\n(iii) programs associated with the use of the equipment, or\nwith the use of the data, are damaged or corrupted; and\n\n(b) the damage or corruption occurs because:\n\n(i) insufficient care was exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the equipment; or\n\n(ii) insufficient care was exercised by the person operating\nthe equipment.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must pay the owner of the equipment, or the\nuser of the data or programs, such reasonable compensation for the\ndamage or corruption as the Commonwealth and the owner or user\nagree on.\n\n(3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to\nagree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal\nCourt of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as\nthe Court determines.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nGeneral provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5\n\nSection 154ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises, or the occupier’s\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, provided\nany appropriate warning or guidance on the operation of the\nequipment.\n\n(5) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament.\n\n(6) For the purposes of subsection (1):\ndamage, in relation to data, includes damage by erasure of data or\naddition of other data.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa46e0afac51d9fa8dc82310146ab30092035277c12821763e989e654be15e70"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZC Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 516,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) as a result of electronic equipment being operated as\nmentioned in section 154E, 154F, 154G, 154H or 154J:\n\n(i) damage is caused to the equipment; or\n\n(ii) the data recorded on the equipment is damaged; or\n\n(iii) programs associated with the use of the equipment, or\nwith the use of the data, are damaged or corrupted; and\n\n(b) the damage or corruption occurs because:\n\n(i) insufficient care was exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the equipment; or\n\n(ii) insufficient care was exercised by the person operating\nthe equipment.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must pay the owner of the equipment, or the\nuser of the data or programs, such reasonable compensation for the\ndamage or corruption as the Commonwealth and the owner or user\nagree on.\n\n(3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to\nagree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal\nCourt of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as\nthe Court determines.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nGeneral provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5\n\nSection 154ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(4) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises, or the occupier’s\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, provided\nany appropriate warning or guidance on the operation of the\nequipment.\n\n(5) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament.\n\n(6) For the purposes of subsection (1):\ndamage, in relation to data, includes damage by erasure of data or\naddition of other data.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
