    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZC(3) Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zc-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.516",
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to\nagree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal\nCourt of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as\nthe Court determines.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nGeneral provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5\n\nSection 154ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to\nagree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal\nCourt of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as\nthe Court determines.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nGeneral provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5\n\nSection 154ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af34f4a965ce0182adcafc851a00011b51390d215567634f8a3d46106e2bfaf2",
      "skos:note": "Owner/user may institute proceedings for compensation if Commonwealth fails to agree."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zc-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZC(3) Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 516,
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to\nagree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal\nCourt of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as\nthe Court determines.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nSearch and seizure  Part XID\nGeneral provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5\n\nSection 154ZC\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
