    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ze",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZE Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154ze"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.518",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\napproval means an approval as a designated complainant granted\nunder subsection 154ZQ(1).\ndesignated complainant means an entity that has an approval that\nis in force.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 154ZE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\ndesignated complaints determination means the determination\nmade by the Minister under section 154ZZ.\nentity means any of the following:\n\n(a) a corporation;\n\n(b) an individual;\n\n(c) a body corporate;\n\n(d) a corporation sole;\n\n(e) a body politic;\n\n(f) a partnership;\n\n(g) any other unincorporated association or body of entities;\n\n(h) a trust.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\napproval means an approval as a designated complainant granted\nunder subsection 154ZQ(1).\ndesignated complainant means an entity that has an approval that\nis in force.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 154ZE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\ndesignated complaints determination means the determination\nmade by the Minister under section 154ZZ.\nentity means any of the following:\n\n(a) a corporation;\n\n(b) an individual;\n\n(c) a body corporate;\n\n(d) a corporation sole;\n\n(e) a body politic;\n\n(f) a partnership;\n\n(g) any other unincorporated association or body of entities;\n\n(h) a trust.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ze-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "102336a3442d6ab746bfd43e25f706697b3f26fdcd0be0b634705fe1b75ff81b",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for designated complaints determination and entity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154ze",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZE Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 518,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\napproval means an approval as a designated complainant granted\nunder subsection 154ZQ(1).\ndesignated complainant means an entity that has an approval that\nis in force.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 154ZE\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\ndesignated complaints determination means the determination\nmade by the Minister under section 154ZZ.\nentity means any of the following:\n\n(a) a corporation;\n\n(b) an individual;\n\n(c) a body corporate;\n\n(d) a corporation sole;\n\n(e) a body politic;\n\n(f) a partnership;\n\n(g) any other unincorporated association or body of entities;\n\n(h) a trust.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ze-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154ze"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZF Designated complaints",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.520",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A designated complainant may make a complaint under this\nsection to the Commission.\n\n(2) The complaint must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) if the Commission has approved a manner for making the\ncomplaint—be made in that manner; and\n\n(c) if the Commission has approved a form for making the\ncomplaint:\n\n(i) be made in the approved form; and\n\n(ii) include the information required by the form; and\n\n(iii) be accompanied by any documents required by the\nform; and\n\n(d) meet the requirements (if any) prescribed in the designated\ncomplaints determination relating to the number and types of\ndesignated complaints that a designated complainant may\nmake during a specified period.\n\n(3) The complaint is a designated complaint starting from the day it\nmeets the requirements mentioned in subsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A designated complainant may make a complaint under this\nsection to the Commission.\n\n(2) The complaint must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) if the Commission has approved a manner for making the\ncomplaint—be made in that manner; and\n\n(c) if the Commission has approved a form for making the\ncomplaint:\n\n(i) be made in the approved form; and\n\n(ii) include the information required by the form; and\n\n(iii) be accompanied by any documents required by the\nform; and\n\n(d) meet the requirements (if any) prescribed in the designated\ncomplaints determination relating to the number and types of\ndesignated complaints that a designated complainant may\nmake during a specified period.\n\n(3) The complaint is a designated complaint starting from the day it\nmeets the requirements mentioned in subsection (2).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zf-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zf-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9835814bd115469fc1af9f734d042ad6d3602e26825723231456201cb8ded92"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZF Designated complaints",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 520,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A designated complainant may make a complaint under this\nsection to the Commission.\n\n(2) The complaint must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) if the Commission has approved a manner for making the\ncomplaint—be made in that manner; and\n\n(c) if the Commission has approved a form for making the\ncomplaint:\n\n(i) be made in the approved form; and\n\n(ii) include the information required by the form; and\n\n(iii) be accompanied by any documents required by the\nform; and\n\n(d) meet the requirements (if any) prescribed in the designated\ncomplaints determination relating to the number and types of\ndesignated complaints that a designated complainant may\nmake during a specified period.\n\n(3) The complaint is a designated complaint starting from the day it\nmeets the requirements mentioned in subsection (2)."
    },
