    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZG Commission to respond by giving notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.520",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission receives a designated complaint from a\ndesignated complainant, the Commission must, within 90 days,\nassess the complaint and give the complainant one of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a notice under subsection 154ZH(1) (no further action on\ncomplaint);\n\n(b) a notice under subsection 154ZK(1) (further action to deal\nwith complaint).\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nCommission handling of designated complaints  Division 2\n\nSection 154ZH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) If, before the Commission gives a notice mentioned in\nsubsection (1) to the complainant, it ceases to be a designated\ncomplainant, for the purposes of subsection (1), the complaint is\ntaken never to have been made.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission receives a designated complaint from a\ndesignated complainant, the Commission must, within 90 days,\nassess the complaint and give the complainant one of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a notice under subsection 154ZH(1) (no further action on\ncomplaint);\n\n(b) a notice under subsection 154ZK(1) (further action to deal\nwith complaint).\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nCommission handling of designated complaints  Division 2\n\nSection 154ZH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) If, before the Commission gives a notice mentioned in\nsubsection (1) to the complainant, it ceases to be a designated\ncomplainant, for the purposes of subsection (1), the complaint is\ntaken never to have been made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f30d2d859851a4e7c931419ec3acb310a9441f2f94830705af5c3a04674d09c6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZG Commission to respond by giving notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 520,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission receives a designated complaint from a\ndesignated complainant, the Commission must, within 90 days,\nassess the complaint and give the complainant one of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a notice under subsection 154ZH(1) (no further action on\ncomplaint);\n\n(b) a notice under subsection 154ZK(1) (further action to deal\nwith complaint).\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nCommission handling of designated complaints  Division 2\n\nSection 154ZH\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(2) If, before the Commission gives a notice mentioned in\nsubsection (1) to the complainant, it ceases to be a designated\ncomplainant, for the purposes of subsection (1), the complaint is\ntaken never to have been made."
    },
