        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZK Notice—further action to deal with complaint",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.523",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may give the designated complainant a notice\nunder this subsection if the Commission is satisfied that the\ncomplaint:\n\n(a) relates to a significant or systemic market issue that affects\nconsumers or small businesses in Australia (or both); and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) relates to a potential breach of this Act; or\n\n(ii) relates to one or more of the Commission’s powers or\nfunctions under this Act.\n\n(2) The notice must set out:\n\n(a) a summary of the complaint; and\n\n(b) the actions the Commission proposes to take in response to\nthe complaint.\n\n(3) The Commission must:\n\n(a) use its best endeavours to commence the actions set out in\nthe notice as soon as practicable after giving the notice; and\n\n(b) in any case, commence the actions set out in the notice within\nthe period of 6 months after giving the notice; and\n\n(c) when the actions set out in the notice have been completed,\nuse its best endeavours to notify this to the entity that made\nthe complaint (even if the entity has ceased to be a designated\ncomplainant).\nCircumstances in which Commission not required to take further\naction\n\n(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply if the Commission is\nsatisfied that circumstances prescribed in the designated\ncomplaints determination apply.\n\n(5) If subsection (4) applies, the Commission must use its best\nendeavours to notify this to the entity that made the complaint\n(even if the entity has ceased to be a designated complainant).\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may give the designated complainant a notice\nunder this subsection if the Commission is satisfied that the\ncomplaint:\n\n(a) relates to a significant or systemic market issue that affects\nconsumers or small businesses in Australia (or both); and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) relates to a potential breach of this Act; or\n\n(ii) relates to one or more of the Commission’s powers or\nfunctions under this Act.\n\n(2) The notice must set out:\n\n(a) a summary of the complaint; and\n\n(b) the actions the Commission proposes to take in response to\nthe complaint.\n\n(3) The Commission must:\n\n(a) use its best endeavours to commence the actions set out in\nthe notice as soon as practicable after giving the notice; and\n\n(b) in any case, commence the actions set out in the notice within\nthe period of 6 months after giving the notice; and\n\n(c) when the actions set out in the notice have been completed,\nuse its best endeavours to notify this to the entity that made\nthe complaint (even if the entity has ceased to be a designated\ncomplainant).\nCircumstances in which Commission not required to take further\naction\n\n(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply if the Commission is\nsatisfied that circumstances prescribed in the designated\ncomplaints determination apply.\n\n(5) If subsection (4) applies, the Commission must use its best\nendeavours to notify this to the entity that made the complaint\n(even if the entity has ceased to be a designated complainant).\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43aad4b050be15629eb73938ee88328a4ba3a4bd8ae3dba35859cdf648dce11e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZK Notice—further action to deal with complaint",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 523,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may give the designated complainant a notice\nunder this subsection if the Commission is satisfied that the\ncomplaint:\n\n(a) relates to a significant or systemic market issue that affects\nconsumers or small businesses in Australia (or both); and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) relates to a potential breach of this Act; or\n\n(ii) relates to one or more of the Commission’s powers or\nfunctions under this Act.\n\n(2) The notice must set out:\n\n(a) a summary of the complaint; and\n\n(b) the actions the Commission proposes to take in response to\nthe complaint.\n\n(3) The Commission must:\n\n(a) use its best endeavours to commence the actions set out in\nthe notice as soon as practicable after giving the notice; and\n\n(b) in any case, commence the actions set out in the notice within\nthe period of 6 months after giving the notice; and\n\n(c) when the actions set out in the notice have been completed,\nuse its best endeavours to notify this to the entity that made\nthe complaint (even if the entity has ceased to be a designated\ncomplainant).\nCircumstances in which Commission not required to take further\naction\n\n(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply if the Commission is\nsatisfied that circumstances prescribed in the designated\ncomplaints determination apply.\n\n(5) If subsection (4) applies, the Commission must use its best\nendeavours to notify this to the entity that made the complaint\n(even if the entity has ceased to be a designated complainant).\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
