      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZK(3) Notice—further action to deal with complaint",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zk-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.523",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Commission must:\n\n(a) use its best endeavours to commence the actions set out in\nthe notice as soon as practicable after giving the notice; and\n\n(b) in any case, commence the actions set out in the notice within\nthe period of 6 months after giving the notice; and\n\n(c) when the actions set out in the notice have been completed,\nuse its best endeavours to notify this to the entity that made\nthe complaint (even if the entity has ceased to be a designated\ncomplainant).\nCircumstances in which Commission not required to take further\naction",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Commission must:\n\n(a) use its best endeavours to commence the actions set out in\nthe notice as soon as practicable after giving the notice; and\n\n(b) in any case, commence the actions set out in the notice within\nthe period of 6 months after giving the notice; and\n\n(c) when the actions set out in the notice have been completed,\nuse its best endeavours to notify this to the entity that made\nthe complaint (even if the entity has ceased to be a designated\ncomplainant).\nCircumstances in which Commission not required to take further\naction",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zk-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ced8ecd2591358179b434ac083c2390ecd98da8ad634de530f28faab616499e",
      "skos:note": "Commission must take further action within 6 months after notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zk-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZK(3) Notice—further action to deal with complaint",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 523,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Commission must:\n\n(a) use its best endeavours to commence the actions set out in\nthe notice as soon as practicable after giving the notice; and\n\n(b) in any case, commence the actions set out in the notice within\nthe period of 6 months after giving the notice; and\n\n(c) when the actions set out in the notice have been completed,\nuse its best endeavours to notify this to the entity that made\nthe complaint (even if the entity has ceased to be a designated\ncomplainant).\nCircumstances in which Commission not required to take further\naction"
    },
