    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZL Replacement notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.524",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission has given the designated complainant a notice\nunder subsection 154ZK(1), the Commission may replace that\nnotice with either of the following:\n\n(a) if the Commission considers it appropriate—a replacement\nnotice under subsection 154ZK(1);\n\n(b) if subsection 154ZH(4) (other inquiry or action) or (5)\n(appropriate to take no further action) applies—a notice\nunder subsection 154ZH(1).\n\n(2) If paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(a) the Commission must give the designated complainant the\nreplacement notice; and\n\n(b) the replacement notice must set out the matters specified in\nsubsection 154ZK(2); and\n\n(c) the replacement notice is taken to be the notice given to the\ndesignated complainant under subsection 154ZK(1) from the\nday the replacement notice is given; and\n\n(d) treat paragraphs 154ZK(3)(a) and (b) as requiring the\nCommission to commence the actions set out in the\nreplacement notice as soon as practicable after it is given.\n\n(3) If paragraph (1)(b) applies:\n\n(a) the Commission must give the designated complainant the\nnotice mentioned in that paragraph; and\n\n(b) subsection 154ZK(3) ceases to apply in relation to the\ncomplaint.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commission has given the designated complainant a notice\nunder subsection 154ZK(1), the Commission may replace that\nnotice with either of the following:\n\n(a) if the Commission considers it appropriate—a replacement\nnotice under subsection 154ZK(1);\n\n(b) if subsection 154ZH(4) (other inquiry or action) or (5)\n(appropriate to take no further action) applies—a notice\nunder subsection 154ZH(1).\n\n(2) If paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(a) the Commission must give the designated complainant the\nreplacement notice; and\n\n(b) the replacement notice must set out the matters specified in\nsubsection 154ZK(2); and\n\n(c) the replacement notice is taken to be the notice given to the\ndesignated complainant under subsection 154ZK(1) from the\nday the replacement notice is given; and\n\n(d) treat paragraphs 154ZK(3)(a) and (b) as requiring the\nCommission to commence the actions set out in the\nreplacement notice as soon as practicable after it is given.\n\n(3) If paragraph (1)(b) applies:\n\n(a) the Commission must give the designated complainant the\nnotice mentioned in that paragraph; and\n\n(b) subsection 154ZK(3) ceases to apply in relation to the\ncomplaint.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zl-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zl-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "feb0ed64b1df018d2f1138a32270d9c06c9ab7559a96d014113b45804bc3feba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZL Replacement notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 524,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commission has given the designated complainant a notice\nunder subsection 154ZK(1), the Commission may replace that\nnotice with either of the following:\n\n(a) if the Commission considers it appropriate—a replacement\nnotice under subsection 154ZK(1);\n\n(b) if subsection 154ZH(4) (other inquiry or action) or (5)\n(appropriate to take no further action) applies—a notice\nunder subsection 154ZH(1).\n\n(2) If paragraph (1)(a) applies:\n\n(a) the Commission must give the designated complainant the\nreplacement notice; and\n\n(b) the replacement notice must set out the matters specified in\nsubsection 154ZK(2); and\n\n(c) the replacement notice is taken to be the notice given to the\ndesignated complainant under subsection 154ZK(1) from the\nday the replacement notice is given; and\n\n(d) treat paragraphs 154ZK(3)(a) and (b) as requiring the\nCommission to commence the actions set out in the\nreplacement notice as soon as practicable after it is given.\n\n(3) If paragraph (1)(b) applies:\n\n(a) the Commission must give the designated complainant the\nnotice mentioned in that paragraph; and\n\n(b) subsection 154ZK(3) ceases to apply in relation to the\ncomplaint."
    },
