    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZQ Minister may grant approval",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.528",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, grant the approval if:\n\n(a) where the approval is to be subject to conditions:\n\n(i) the Minister has given the entity a notice under\nsubsection 154ZR(3) setting out those conditions; and\n\n(ii) 14 business days have passed since that notice was\ngiven; and\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval.\nConsiderations\n\n(2) For the purposes of being satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the experience and ability of the applicant in representing the\ninterests of consumers or small businesses (or both) in\nAustralia in relation to a range of market issues that affect\nthem;\n\n(b) the extent to which the Minister is satisfied that the applicant\nwill, if approved as a designated complainant, act with\nintegrity in connection with being a designated complainant;\n\n(c) any other matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(a).\n\n(3) The Minister may also have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) any matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(b);\n\n(b) any other matter the Minister considers relevant.\n\n(4) For the purposes of paragraphs (2)(c) and (3)(a), the designated\ncomplaints determination may prescribe matters to which the\nMinister:\n\n(a) must have regard; or\n\n(b) may have regard.\nMaximum number of designated complainants\n\n(5) However, the Minister must not grant the approval if doing so\nwould result in the number of designated complainants being\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nDesignated complainants  Division 3\n\nSection 154ZR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nabove the limit prescribed in the designated complaints\ndetermination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, grant the approval if:\n\n(a) where the approval is to be subject to conditions:\n\n(i) the Minister has given the entity a notice under\nsubsection 154ZR(3) setting out those conditions; and\n\n(ii) 14 business days have passed since that notice was\ngiven; and\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval.\nConsiderations\n\n(2) For the purposes of being satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the experience and ability of the applicant in representing the\ninterests of consumers or small businesses (or both) in\nAustralia in relation to a range of market issues that affect\nthem;\n\n(b) the extent to which the Minister is satisfied that the applicant\nwill, if approved as a designated complainant, act with\nintegrity in connection with being a designated complainant;\n\n(c) any other matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(a).\n\n(3) The Minister may also have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) any matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(b);\n\n(b) any other matter the Minister considers relevant.\n\n(4) For the purposes of paragraphs (2)(c) and (3)(a), the designated\ncomplaints determination may prescribe matters to which the\nMinister:\n\n(a) must have regard; or\n\n(b) may have regard.\nMaximum number of designated complainants\n\n(5) However, the Minister must not grant the approval if doing so\nwould result in the number of designated complainants being\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nDesignated complainants  Division 3\n\nSection 154ZR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nabove the limit prescribed in the designated complaints\ndetermination.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd1ac06dc8ed9bf4653ba32f9fc65b5a3f60e32d4ec0448d7f12667aaff820ab"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZQ Minister may grant approval",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 528,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, grant the approval if:\n\n(a) where the approval is to be subject to conditions:\n\n(i) the Minister has given the entity a notice under\nsubsection 154ZR(3) setting out those conditions; and\n\n(ii) 14 business days have passed since that notice was\ngiven; and\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval.\nConsiderations\n\n(2) For the purposes of being satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the experience and ability of the applicant in representing the\ninterests of consumers or small businesses (or both) in\nAustralia in relation to a range of market issues that affect\nthem;\n\n(b) the extent to which the Minister is satisfied that the applicant\nwill, if approved as a designated complainant, act with\nintegrity in connection with being a designated complainant;\n\n(c) any other matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(a).\n\n(3) The Minister may also have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) any matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(b);\n\n(b) any other matter the Minister considers relevant.\n\n(4) For the purposes of paragraphs (2)(c) and (3)(a), the designated\ncomplaints determination may prescribe matters to which the\nMinister:\n\n(a) must have regard; or\n\n(b) may have regard.\nMaximum number of designated complainants\n\n(5) However, the Minister must not grant the approval if doing so\nwould result in the number of designated complainants being\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nDesignated complainants  Division 3\n\nSection 154ZR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nabove the limit prescribed in the designated complaints\ndetermination."
    },
