      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of being satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the experience and ability of the applicant in representing the\ninterests of consumers or small businesses (or both) in\nAustralia in relation to a range of market issues that affect\nthem;\n\n(b) the extent to which the Minister is satisfied that the applicant\nwill, if approved as a designated complainant, act with\nintegrity in connection with being a designated complainant;\n\n(c) any other matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(a).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of being satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the experience and ability of the applicant in representing the\ninterests of consumers or small businesses (or both) in\nAustralia in relation to a range of market issues that affect\nthem;\n\n(b) the extent to which the Minister is satisfied that the applicant\nwill, if approved as a designated complainant, act with\nintegrity in connection with being a designated complainant;\n\n(c) any other matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(a).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "301533d50a924bd7a4e67397f4bab2dba9fd4926c18dc509460266dbcd20860e",
      "skos:note": "Minister must consider experience and ability of applicant in representing consumer interests."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zq-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZQ(2) Minister may grant approval",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 528,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of being satisfied that it is appropriate to grant the\napproval, the Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the experience and ability of the applicant in representing the\ninterests of consumers or small businesses (or both) in\nAustralia in relation to a range of market issues that affect\nthem;\n\n(b) the extent to which the Minister is satisfied that the applicant\nwill, if approved as a designated complainant, act with\nintegrity in connection with being a designated complainant;\n\n(c) any other matter prescribed under paragraph (4)(a)."
    },
