    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZQ(5) Minister may grant approval",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zq-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.528",
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, the Minister must not grant the approval if doing so\nwould result in the number of designated complainants being\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nDesignated complainants  Division 3\n\nSection 154ZR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nabove the limit prescribed in the designated complaints\ndetermination.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) However, the Minister must not grant the approval if doing so\nwould result in the number of designated complainants being\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nDesignated complainants  Division 3\n\nSection 154ZR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nabove the limit prescribed in the designated complaints\ndetermination.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb32bffbc83b6263c1c121df427ca1347c9231d343fe90f6ebc0ccca7aa59b36",
      "skos:note": "Minister cannot grant approval if it would exceed the limit of designated complainants."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zq-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZQ(5) Minister may grant approval",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 528,
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, the Minister must not grant the approval if doing so\nwould result in the number of designated complainants being\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nDesignated complaints  Part XIE\nDesignated complainants  Division 3\n\nSection 154ZR\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nabove the limit prescribed in the designated complaints\ndetermination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zq-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
