    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zz",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154ZZ Designated complaints determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zz"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.534",
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\n(the designated complaints determination) prescribing matters\nrequired or permitted by this Part to be prescribed by the\ndesignated complaints determination.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\n(the designated complaints determination) prescribing matters\nrequired or permitted by this Part to be prescribed by the\ndesignated complaints determination.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zz-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3cd2ace7aa268ca3419cb27de87c2982a55eca0378c49b8befa7f4d44987859b",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may make a determination prescribing matters required or permitted by this Part."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-154zz",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154ZZ Designated complaints determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 534,
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination\n(the designated complaints determination) prescribing matters\nrequired or permitted by this Part to be prescribed by the\ndesignated complaints determination.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zz-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zz"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155 Power to obtain information, documents and evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.535",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2A), if the Commission, the Chairperson or\na Deputy Chairperson has reason to believe that a person is capable\nof furnishing information, producing documents or giving evidence\nrelating to a matter referred to in subsection (2), a member of the\nCommission may, by notice in writing served on that person\n(whether in Australia or outside Australia), require that person:\n\n(a) to furnish to the Commission, by writing signed by that\nperson or, in the case of a body corporate, by a competent\nofficer of the body corporate, within the time and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such information;\n\n(b) to produce to the Commission, or to a person specified in the\nnotice acting on its behalf, in accordance with the notice, any\nsuch documents; or\n\n(c) to appear before the Commission, or before an associate\nmember of the Commission who is an AER member and who\nis specified in the notice, or before a member of the staff\nassisting the Commission who is an SES employee or an\nacting SES employee and who is specified in the notice, at a\ntime and place specified in the notice to give any such\nevidence, either orally or in writing, and produce any such\ndocuments.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the matter must be a matter\nthat:\n\n(a) constitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) Division 4B of Part 3.3 of the Radiocommunications Act\n1992; or\n\n(iii) any of the terms of an undertaking under section 87B of\nthis Act or under section 218 of the Australian\nConsumer Law; or\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2A), if the Commission, the Chairperson or\na Deputy Chairperson has reason to believe that a person is capable\nof furnishing information, producing documents or giving evidence\nrelating to a matter referred to in subsection (2), a member of the\nCommission may, by notice in writing served on that person\n(whether in Australia or outside Australia), require that person:\n\n(a) to furnish to the Commission, by writing signed by that\nperson or, in the case of a body corporate, by a competent\nofficer of the body corporate, within the time and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such information;\n\n(b) to produce to the Commission, or to a person specified in the\nnotice acting on its behalf, in accordance with the notice, any\nsuch documents; or\n\n(c) to appear before the Commission, or before an associate\nmember of the Commission who is an AER member and who\nis specified in the notice, or before a member of the staff\nassisting the Commission who is an SES employee or an\nacting SES employee and who is specified in the notice, at a\ntime and place specified in the notice to give any such\nevidence, either orally or in writing, and produce any such\ndocuments.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the matter must be a matter\nthat:\n\n(a) constitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) Division 4B of Part 3.3 of the Radiocommunications Act\n1992; or\n\n(iii) any of the terms of an undertaking under section 87B of\nthis Act or under section 218 of the Australian\nConsumer Law; or\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "24a9c282024d3719a3750f1be3382ee473451cfb54e99562c243b56e49afeb46"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155 Power to obtain information, documents and evidence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 535,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2A), if the Commission, the Chairperson or\na Deputy Chairperson has reason to believe that a person is capable\nof furnishing information, producing documents or giving evidence\nrelating to a matter referred to in subsection (2), a member of the\nCommission may, by notice in writing served on that person\n(whether in Australia or outside Australia), require that person:\n\n(a) to furnish to the Commission, by writing signed by that\nperson or, in the case of a body corporate, by a competent\nofficer of the body corporate, within the time and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such information;\n\n(b) to produce to the Commission, or to a person specified in the\nnotice acting on its behalf, in accordance with the notice, any\nsuch documents; or\n\n(c) to appear before the Commission, or before an associate\nmember of the Commission who is an AER member and who\nis specified in the notice, or before a member of the staff\nassisting the Commission who is an SES employee or an\nacting SES employee and who is specified in the notice, at a\ntime and place specified in the notice to give any such\nevidence, either orally or in writing, and produce any such\ndocuments.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the matter must be a matter\nthat:\n\n(a) constitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) Division 4B of Part 3.3 of the Radiocommunications Act\n1992; or\n\n(iii) any of the terms of an undertaking under section 87B of\nthis Act or under section 218 of the Australian\nConsumer Law; or\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
