    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155AA Protection of Part VB information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.548",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Commission official must not disclose any protected Part VB\ninformation to any person, except:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155A\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) when the Commission official is performing duties or\nfunctions as a Commission official; or\n\n(b) when the Commission official or the Commission is required\nor permitted by law to disclose the information.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not allow a Commission official to disclose\nprotected Part VB information when performing a function of the\nCommission described in section 28.\n\n(3) In this section:\nCommission official means:\n\n(a) a member, or associate member, of the Commission;\n\n(b) a person referred to in subsection 27(1);\n\n(c) a person engaged under section 27A.\ndisclose means divulge or communicate.\ninformation includes information in a document and information\ngiven in evidence.\nprotected Part VB information means:\n\n(a) information that:\n\n(i) was obtained by the Commission under Part XID or\nsection 155; and\n\n(ii) relates to a matter that arose under Part VB before its\nrepeal by item 32 of Schedule 1 to the Statute Stocktake\n(Regulatory and Other Laws) Act 2009; or\n\n(b) information that was obtained by the Commission under\nsection 75AY before its repeal by item 32 of Schedule 1 to\nthe Statute Stocktake (Regulatory and Other Laws) Act 2009.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A Commission official must not disclose any protected Part VB\ninformation to any person, except:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155A\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) when the Commission official is performing duties or\nfunctions as a Commission official; or\n\n(b) when the Commission official or the Commission is required\nor permitted by law to disclose the information.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not allow a Commission official to disclose\nprotected Part VB information when performing a function of the\nCommission described in section 28.\n\n(3) In this section:\nCommission official means:\n\n(a) a member, or associate member, of the Commission;\n\n(b) a person referred to in subsection 27(1);\n\n(c) a person engaged under section 27A.\ndisclose means divulge or communicate.\ninformation includes information in a document and information\ngiven in evidence.\nprotected Part VB information means:\n\n(a) information that:\n\n(i) was obtained by the Commission under Part XID or\nsection 155; and\n\n(ii) relates to a matter that arose under Part VB before its\nrepeal by item 32 of Schedule 1 to the Statute Stocktake\n(Regulatory and Other Laws) Act 2009; or\n\n(b) information that was obtained by the Commission under\nsection 75AY before its repeal by item 32 of Schedule 1 to\nthe Statute Stocktake (Regulatory and Other Laws) Act 2009.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155aa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155aa-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19dc6a3a0fe22d9838fc2f2bbf7d622a786412b2d2e4cbb955e31752ef9b3e9f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155AA Protection of Part VB information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 548,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Commission official must not disclose any protected Part VB\ninformation to any person, except:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155A\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) when the Commission official is performing duties or\nfunctions as a Commission official; or\n\n(b) when the Commission official or the Commission is required\nor permitted by law to disclose the information.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not allow a Commission official to disclose\nprotected Part VB information when performing a function of the\nCommission described in section 28.\n\n(3) In this section:\nCommission official means:\n\n(a) a member, or associate member, of the Commission;\n\n(b) a person referred to in subsection 27(1);\n\n(c) a person engaged under section 27A.\ndisclose means divulge or communicate.\ninformation includes information in a document and information\ngiven in evidence.\nprotected Part VB information means:\n\n(a) information that:\n\n(i) was obtained by the Commission under Part XID or\nsection 155; and\n\n(ii) relates to a matter that arose under Part VB before its\nrepeal by item 32 of Schedule 1 to the Statute Stocktake\n(Regulatory and Other Laws) Act 2009; or\n\n(b) information that was obtained by the Commission under\nsection 75AY before its repeal by item 32 of Schedule 1 to\nthe Statute Stocktake (Regulatory and Other Laws) Act 2009."
    },
