    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155B(3) Australian Competition and Consumer Commission may",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.550",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person must not:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) contravene a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act\n1986 of New Zealand; or\n\n(b) in purported compliance with such a notice, knowingly\nfurnish information that is false or misleading in a material\nparticular.\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\nNote 2:\nPart IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with\npenalties.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A person must not:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) contravene a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act\n1986 of New Zealand; or\n\n(b) in purported compliance with such a notice, knowingly\nfurnish information that is false or misleading in a material\nparticular.\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\nNote 2:\nPart IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with\npenalties.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43707f5e2efe641537b5053dff5a054393dd07a15c27da75787ddec47feccbd0",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on contravening a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act 1986 of New Zealand."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155B(3) Australian Competition and Consumer Commission may",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 550,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person must not:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 155B\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) contravene a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act\n1986 of New Zealand; or\n\n(b) in purported compliance with such a notice, knowingly\nfurnish information that is false or misleading in a material\nparticular.\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\nNote 2:\nPart IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with\npenalties."
    },
