      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.550",
      "values:originalText": "(3A) Paragraph (3)(a) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsection (3A), see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(3A) Paragraph (3)(a) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsection (3A), see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-3a-norm"
        },
