    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155B(4) Australian Competition and Consumer Commission may",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.550",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person is not excused from furnishing information or producing\na document under a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act\n1986 of New Zealand on the ground that the information, or the\nproduction of the document, may tend to incriminate the person,\nbut:\n\n(a) any information furnished or document produced under such\na notice; and\n\n(b) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of furnishing the information or\nproducing the document;\nis not admissible in evidence against the person in any criminal\nproceedings, other than proceedings for an offence against\nsubsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person is not excused from furnishing information or producing\na document under a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act\n1986 of New Zealand on the ground that the information, or the\nproduction of the document, may tend to incriminate the person,\nbut:\n\n(a) any information furnished or document produced under such\na notice; and\n\n(b) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of furnishing the information or\nproducing the document;\nis not admissible in evidence against the person in any criminal\nproceedings, other than proceedings for an offence against\nsubsection (3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a62d07b6b69aa2d7d5ffb0ff0be907ebc72ceab7c7ebefbedf4683732805f42b",
      "skos:note": "Must provide information or document under notice without claiming privilege against self-incrimination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-155b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155B(4) Australian Competition and Consumer Commission may",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 550,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person is not excused from furnishing information or producing\na document under a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act\n1986 of New Zealand on the ground that the information, or the\nproduction of the document, may tend to incriminate the person,\nbut:\n\n(a) any information furnished or document produced under such\na notice; and\n\n(b) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of furnishing the information or\nproducing the document;\nis not admissible in evidence against the person in any criminal\nproceedings, other than proceedings for an offence against\nsubsection (3)."
    },
