    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-156",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "156 Inspection of documents by Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-156"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.552",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A member of the Commission, or a person authorised by a member\nof the Commission, may inspect a document produced in\npursuance of a notice under section 155 or 155A and may make\ncopies of, or take extracts from, the document.\n\n(2) The Commission may, for the purposes of this Act, take, and retain\nfor as long as is necessary for those purposes, possession of a\ndocument produced in pursuance of a notice under section 155 or\n155A but the person otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument is entitled to be supplied, as soon as practicable, with a\ncopy certified by a member of the Commission under his or her\nhand to be a true copy and the certified copy shall be received in all\ncourts as evidence as if it were the original.\n\n(3) Until such a certified copy is supplied, the Commission shall, at\nsuch times and places as it thinks appropriate, permit the person\notherwise entitled to possession of the document, or a person\nauthorised by that person, to inspect and make copies of or take\nextracts from the document.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A member of the Commission, or a person authorised by a member\nof the Commission, may inspect a document produced in\npursuance of a notice under section 155 or 155A and may make\ncopies of, or take extracts from, the document.\n\n(2) The Commission may, for the purposes of this Act, take, and retain\nfor as long as is necessary for those purposes, possession of a\ndocument produced in pursuance of a notice under section 155 or\n155A but the person otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument is entitled to be supplied, as soon as practicable, with a\ncopy certified by a member of the Commission under his or her\nhand to be a true copy and the certified copy shall be received in all\ncourts as evidence as if it were the original.\n\n(3) Until such a certified copy is supplied, the Commission shall, at\nsuch times and places as it thinks appropriate, permit the person\notherwise entitled to possession of the document, or a person\nauthorised by that person, to inspect and make copies of or take\nextracts from the document.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-156-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-156-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-156-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "98e6e50a28ea6bbe439ba362d2136fd5ad8a1d11ed14b35e356d6a34233284e7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-156",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "156 Inspection of documents by Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 552,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A member of the Commission, or a person authorised by a member\nof the Commission, may inspect a document produced in\npursuance of a notice under section 155 or 155A and may make\ncopies of, or take extracts from, the document.\n\n(2) The Commission may, for the purposes of this Act, take, and retain\nfor as long as is necessary for those purposes, possession of a\ndocument produced in pursuance of a notice under section 155 or\n155A but the person otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument is entitled to be supplied, as soon as practicable, with a\ncopy certified by a member of the Commission under his or her\nhand to be a true copy and the certified copy shall be received in all\ncourts as evidence as if it were the original.\n\n(3) Until such a certified copy is supplied, the Commission shall, at\nsuch times and places as it thinks appropriate, permit the person\notherwise entitled to possession of the document, or a person\nauthorised by that person, to inspect and make copies of or take\nextracts from the document."
    },
