    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "157AA Disclosure of CDR-related information by Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-157aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.556",
      "values:originalText": "Disclosure to the Information Commissioner\n\n(1) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) the Information Commissioner; or\n\n(b) any staff or consultant assisting the Information\nCommissioner in performing that Commissioner’s functions,\nor exercising that Commissioner’s powers, relating to\nPart IVD or the consumer data rules;\nany information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the\nconsumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the\nfunctions or powers referred to in paragraph (b).\nNote:\nThe Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(2) The Information Commissioner or a person mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(b) must only use the information:\n\n(a) for a purpose connected with the performance of the\nfunctions, or the exercise of the powers, referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) in accordance with any conditions imposed under\nsubsection (4).\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 157AA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nDisclosure to the Secretary\n\n(2A) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n\n(b) any employee of the Department or consultant assisting the\nSecretary in performing the Secretary’s functions, or\nexercising the Secretary’s powers, relating to Part IVD;\nany information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the\nconsumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the\nfunctions or powers referred to in paragraph (b).\nNote:\nThe Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(2B) The Secretary or a person mentioned in paragraph (2A)(b) must\nonly use the information:\n\n(a) for a purpose connected with the performance of the\nfunctions, or the exercise of the powers, referred to in\nparagraph (2A)(b); and\n\n(b) in accordance with any conditions imposed under\nsubsection (4).\nDisclosure to a foreign agency\n\n(3) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) an agency having the function in a foreign country of\nsupervising or regulating the disclosure of similar\ninformation to that covered by an instrument designating a\nsector under subsection 56AC(2); or\n\n(aa) an agency having the function in a foreign country of\nsupervising or regulating types of actions similar to those\ndeclared under section 56ACA; or\n\n(b) an agency, that is prescribed by the regulations, of a foreign\ncountry;\nany information that the Commission obtains:\n\n(c) under this Act in relation to Part IVD or the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(d) under the consumer data rules.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "Disclosure to the Information Commissioner\n\n(1) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) the Information Commissioner; or\n\n(b) any staff or consultant assisting the Information\nCommissioner in performing that Commissioner’s functions,\nor exercising that Commissioner’s powers, relating to\nPart IVD or the consumer data rules;\nany information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the\nconsumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the\nfunctions or powers referred to in paragraph (b).\nNote:\nThe Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(2) The Information Commissioner or a person mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(b) must only use the information:\n\n(a) for a purpose connected with the performance of the\nfunctions, or the exercise of the powers, referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) in accordance with any conditions imposed under\nsubsection (4).\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 157AA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nDisclosure to the Secretary\n\n(2A) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n\n(b) any employee of the Department or consultant assisting the\nSecretary in performing the Secretary’s functions, or\nexercising the Secretary’s powers, relating to Part IVD;\nany information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the\nconsumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the\nfunctions or powers referred to in paragraph (b).\nNote:\nThe Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(2B) The Secretary or a person mentioned in paragraph (2A)(b) must\nonly use the information:\n\n(a) for a purpose connected with the performance of the\nfunctions, or the exercise of the powers, referred to in\nparagraph (2A)(b); and\n\n(b) in accordance with any conditions imposed under\nsubsection (4).\nDisclosure to a foreign",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa-ss-2b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43982b24035035a961b1681c5ef765994c6c3c181aef6bda4bcf2a6c456422fa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-157aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "157AA Disclosure of CDR-related information by Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 556,
      "values:originalText": "Disclosure to the Information Commissioner\n\n(1) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) the Information Commissioner; or\n\n(b) any staff or consultant assisting the Information\nCommissioner in performing that Commissioner’s functions,\nor exercising that Commissioner’s powers, relating to\nPart IVD or the consumer data rules;\nany information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the\nconsumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the\nfunctions or powers referred to in paragraph (b).\nNote:\nThe Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(2) The Information Commissioner or a person mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(b) must only use the information:\n\n(a) for a purpose connected with the performance of the\nfunctions, or the exercise of the powers, referred to in\nparagraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) in accordance with any conditions imposed under\nsubsection (4).\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 157AA\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\nDisclosure to the Secretary\n\n(2A) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n\n(b) any employee of the Department or consultant assisting the\nSecretary in performing the Secretary’s functions, or\nexercising the Secretary’s powers, relating to Part IVD;\nany information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the\nconsumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the\nfunctions or powers referred to in paragraph (b).\nNote:\nThe Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and\ndisclosure of information.\n\n(2B) The Secretary or a person mentioned in paragraph (2A)(b) must\nonly use the information:\n\n(a) for a purpose connected with the performance of the\nfunctions, or the exercise of the powers, referred to in\nparagraph (2A)(b); and\n\n(b) in accordance with any conditions imposed under\nsubsection (4).\nDisclosure to a foreign agency\n\n(3) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:\n\n(a) an agency having the function in a foreign country of\nsupervising or regulating the disclosure of similar\ninformation to that covered by an instrument designating a\nsector under subsection 56AC(2); or\n\n(aa) an agency having the function in a foreign country of\nsupervising or regulating types of actions similar to those\ndeclared under section 56ACA; or\n\n(b) an agency, that is prescribed by the regulations, of a foreign\ncountry;\nany information that the Commission obtains:\n\n(c) under this Act in relation to Part IVD or the consumer data\nrules; or\n\n(d) under the consumer data rules.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
