        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.564",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In deciding whether to order a stay of the civil proceeding, the\ncourt must consider:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 158\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the extent of any financial loss that a party would suffer as a\nresult of the proceeding being stayed; and\n\n(b) whether a party has reasonable prospects of obtaining a\nremedy in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) any other matter the court considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In deciding whether to order a stay of the civil proceeding, the\ncourt must consider:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 158\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the extent of any financial loss that a party would suffer as a\nresult of the proceeding being stayed; and\n\n(b) whether a party has reasonable prospects of obtaining a\nremedy in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) any other matter the court considers relevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157d-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157d-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f6c30792df0ad9dce70c55cbbe72f40b57a281d0575df33cedf18bb2dcd038a4",
      "skos:note": "Court must consider certain factors when deciding to order a stay of civil proceeding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-157d-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "157D(4) General powers of a court",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 564,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In deciding whether to order a stay of the civil proceeding, the\ncourt must consider:\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 158\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(a) the extent of any financial loss that a party would suffer as a\nresult of the proceeding being stayed; and\n\n(b) whether a party has reasonable prospects of obtaining a\nremedy in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) any other matter the court considers relevant."
    },
