      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.569",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 20 penalty units\nor imprisonment for 12 months.\nNote 1:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\nNote 2:\nPart IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with\npenalties.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 20 penalty units\nor imprisonment for 12 months.\nNote 1:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\nNote 2:\nPart IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with\npenalties.",
      "values:partOf": {
