      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-163",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "163 Prosecutions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-163"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.571",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Prosecutions for offences against this Act may be brought in any\ncourt having jurisdiction in the matter.\n\n(2) In so far as this section has effect as a law of the Commonwealth,\nthe Federal Court has jurisdiction in any matter in respect of which\na criminal proceeding is instituted for an offence to which\nsubsection (1) applies, and that jurisdiction is exclusive of the\njurisdiction of any other court other than:\n\n(a) the jurisdiction of a Supreme Court of a State or Territory\nunder section 68 of the Judiciary Act 1903 with respect to\nany matter in respect of which a criminal proceeding is\ninstituted for an offence against section 45AF or 45AG or\nsubsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1); and\n\n(b) the jurisdiction of a court under section 68 of the Judiciary\nAct 1903 with respect to the examination and commitment\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Prosecutions for offences against this Act may be brought in any\ncourt having jurisdiction in the matter.\n\n(2) In so far as this section has effect as a law of the Commonwealth,\nthe Federal Court has jurisdiction in any matter in respect of which\na criminal proceeding is instituted for an offence to which\nsubsection (1) applies, and that jurisdiction is exclusive of the\njurisdiction of any other court other than:\n\n(a) the jurisdiction of a Supreme Court of a State or Territory\nunder section 68 of the Judiciary Act 1903 with respect to\nany matter in respect of which a criminal proceeding is\ninstituted for an offence against section 45AF or 45AG or\nsubsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1); and\n\n(b) the jurisdiction of a court under section 68 of the Judiciary\nAct 1903 with respect to the examination and commitment\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-163-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-163-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "573da90ff790966db29e116ffd91a596bbe8e2fd79c1061efd5d562d78bd24af"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-163",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "163 Prosecutions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 571,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Prosecutions for offences against this Act may be brought in any\ncourt having jurisdiction in the matter.\n\n(2) In so far as this section has effect as a law of the Commonwealth,\nthe Federal Court has jurisdiction in any matter in respect of which\na criminal proceeding is instituted for an offence to which\nsubsection (1) applies, and that jurisdiction is exclusive of the\njurisdiction of any other court other than:\n\n(a) the jurisdiction of a Supreme Court of a State or Territory\nunder section 68 of the Judiciary Act 1903 with respect to\nany matter in respect of which a criminal proceeding is\ninstituted for an offence against section 45AF or 45AG or\nsubsection 56BN(1) or 56BZI(1); and\n\n(b) the jurisdiction of a court under section 68 of the Judiciary\nAct 1903 with respect to the examination and commitment\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
