    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-165-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "165(3) Inspection of, furnishing of copies of, and evidence of,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-165-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.576",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Unless the Tribunal in a particular case otherwise directs,\nsubsection (2) does not apply in relation to a document furnished to\nthe Tribunal if the person by whom the document was furnished\nclaims, as prescribed, that the document contains matter of a\nconfidential nature.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Unless the Tribunal in a particular case otherwise directs,\nsubsection (2) does not apply in relation to a document furnished to\nthe Tribunal if the person by whom the document was furnished\nclaims, as prescribed, that the document contains matter of a\nconfidential nature.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-165"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-165-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-165-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a75f2d027cc3e01cc7121fb99631debd37cfd56b92107fd08cdf254a408b146",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from subsection (2) for confidential documents"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-165-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "165(3) Inspection of, furnishing of copies of, and evidence of,",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 576,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Unless the Tribunal in a particular case otherwise directs,\nsubsection (2) does not apply in relation to a document furnished to\nthe Tribunal if the person by whom the document was furnished\nclaims, as prescribed, that the document contains matter of a\nconfidential nature."
    },
    {
