    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-171a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "171A Charges by the Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-171a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.582",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may make a charge of an amount, or at a rate,\ndetermined by the Commission for:\n\n(a) supplying a person with material published by the\nCommission in the course of carrying out its functions or\nexercising its powers; or\n\n(b) permitting a person to attend or take part in a prescribed\nactivity arranged by or on behalf of the Commission for the\npurpose of carrying out any of its functions.\n\n(2) Where:\n\n(a) the Commission provides a discretionary service for a\nperson; and\n\n(b) this Act does not otherwise provide for a charge for the\nservice;\nthe Commission may make a charge of such amount, or at such a\nrate, as is agreed between the Commission and the person.\n\n(3) In this section, a reference to the provision by the Commission of a\ndiscretionary service for a person is a reference to the doing of an\nact by the Commission, being a prescribed act that:\n\n(a) the Commission has power to do but is not required to do by\nor under any law; and\n\n(b) the Commission does at the person’s request.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may make a charge of an amount, or at a rate,\ndetermined by the Commission for:\n\n(a) supplying a person with material published by the\nCommission in the course of carrying out its functions or\nexercising its powers; or\n\n(b) permitting a person to attend or take part in a prescribed\nactivity arranged by or on behalf of the Commission for the\npurpose of carrying out any of its functions.\n\n(2) Where:\n\n(a) the Commission provides a discretionary service for a\nperson; and\n\n(b) this Act does not otherwise provide for a charge for the\nservice;\nthe Commission may make a charge of such amount, or at such a\nrate, as is agreed between the Commission and the person.\n\n(3) In this section, a reference to the provision by the Commission of a\ndiscretionary service for a person is a reference to the doing of an\nact by the Commission, being a prescribed act that:\n\n(a) the Commission has power to do but is not required to do by\nor under any law; and\n\n(b) the Commission does at the person’s request.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-171a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-171a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-171a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7c9f01fc4202d0e4b6f5321f44dedd86aa41af687e64659f51ffc07fb78ab7d6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-171a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "171A Charges by the Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 582,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may make a charge of an amount, or at a rate,\ndetermined by the Commission for:\n\n(a) supplying a person with material published by the\nCommission in the course of carrying out its functions or\nexercising its powers; or\n\n(b) permitting a person to attend or take part in a prescribed\nactivity arranged by or on behalf of the Commission for the\npurpose of carrying out any of its functions.\n\n(2) Where:\n\n(a) the Commission provides a discretionary service for a\nperson; and\n\n(b) this Act does not otherwise provide for a charge for the\nservice;\nthe Commission may make a charge of such amount, or at such a\nrate, as is agreed between the Commission and the person.\n\n(3) In this section, a reference to the provision by the Commission of a\ndiscretionary service for a person is a reference to the doing of an\nact by the Commission, being a prescribed act that:\n\n(a) the Commission has power to do but is not required to do by\nor under any law; and\n\n(b) the Commission does at the person’s request."
    },
