    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-173",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "173 Authorisation for the purposes of subsection 51(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-173"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.584",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether a person (including a corporation) has\ncontravened section 50 of this Act, the vesting of ownership of\nprimary products in the person by legislation is to be taken, for the\npurposes of subparagraph 51(1)(a)(i), to be specified in, and\nspecifically authorised by, this section.\n\n(2) In this section:\nprimary products means:\n\n(a) agricultural or horticultural produce, including produce that\nhas been subjected to a manufacturing process; or\n\n(b) crops, whether on or attached to the land or not; or\n\n(c) animals (whether dead or alive); or\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 173\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) the bodily produce (including natural increase) of animals.\nNote:\nAn example of agricultural produce that has been subjected to a\nmanufacturing process is sugar cane that has been transformed into\nraw sugar.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In deciding whether a person (including a corporation) has\ncontravened section 50 of this Act, the vesting of ownership of\nprimary products in the person by legislation is to be taken, for the\npurposes of subparagraph 51(1)(a)(i), to be specified in, and\nspecifically authorised by, this section.\n\n(2) In this section:\nprimary products means:\n\n(a) agricultural or horticultural produce, including produce that\nhas been subjected to a manufacturing process; or\n\n(b) crops, whether on or attached to the land or not; or\n\n(c) animals (whether dead or alive); or\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 173\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) the bodily produce (including natural increase) of animals.\nNote:\nAn example of agricultural produce that has been subjected to a\nmanufacturing process is sugar cane that has been transformed into\nraw sugar.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-173-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-173-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5eec4c092c01340050dfb4d4b6af299231fac788720caff12ba22aaab1cb1b8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-173",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "173 Authorisation for the purposes of subsection 51(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 584,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In deciding whether a person (including a corporation) has\ncontravened section 50 of this Act, the vesting of ownership of\nprimary products in the person by legislation is to be taken, for the\npurposes of subparagraph 51(1)(a)(i), to be specified in, and\nspecifically authorised by, this section.\n\n(2) In this section:\nprimary products means:\n\n(a) agricultural or horticultural produce, including produce that\nhas been subjected to a manufacturing process; or\n\n(b) crops, whether on or attached to the land or not; or\n\n(c) animals (whether dead or alive); or\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nMiscellaneous  Part XII\n\nSection 173\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\n(d) the bodily produce (including natural increase) of animals.\nNote:\nAn example of agricultural produce that has been subjected to a\nmanufacturing process is sugar cane that has been transformed into\nraw sugar.\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous"
    },
