    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-176",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "176 Proceedings relating to price-fixing contraventions taking place",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-176"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.586",
      "values:originalText": "before the commencement time\n\nDespite the repeal of section 76D by the Trade Practices\nAmendment (Cartel Conduct and Other Measures) Act 2009, that\nsection continues to apply, in relation to proceedings (whether\ninstituted before or after the commencement time) in relation to a\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nApplication and transitional provisions relating to the competition provisions  Part XIII\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 177\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\ncontravention that took place before the commencement time, as if\nthat repeal had not happened.",
      "skos:definition": "before the commencement time\n\nDespite the repeal of section 76D by the Trade Practices\nAmendment (Cartel Conduct and Other Measures) Act 2009, that\nsection continues to apply, in relation to proceedings (whether\ninstituted before or after the commencement time) in relation to a\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nApplication and transitional provisions relating to the competition provisions  Part XIII\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 177\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\ncontravention that took place before the commencement time, as if\nthat repeal had not happened.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-176-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-176-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-176-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-176-logic-argumentation-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e69170006ed3e0ef3c863e9cd0ba9736ab2f7fd67798a5b42f1c60409422b5f4",
      "skos:note": "Section continues to apply despite repeal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-176",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "176 Proceedings relating to price-fixing contraventions taking place",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 586,
      "values:originalText": "before the commencement time\n\nDespite the repeal of section 76D by the Trade Practices\nAmendment (Cartel Conduct and Other Measures) Act 2009, that\nsection continues to apply, in relation to proceedings (whether\ninstituted before or after the commencement time) in relation to a\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nApplication and transitional provisions relating to the competition provisions  Part XIII\nCartel conduct  Division 1\n\nSection 177\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026\n\ncontravention that took place before the commencement time, as if\nthat repeal had not happened."
    },
