    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-186",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186 Application of repeal of subsection 51(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-186"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.597",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The amendment made by item 1 of Schedule 4 to the Treasury\nLaws Amendment (2018 Measures No. 5) Act 2019 applies in\nrelation to a licence granted, an assignment made, or a contract,\narrangement or understanding entered into, on or after the\ncommencement of that Schedule.\n\n(2) The amendment also applies to a licence granted, an assignment\nmade, or a contract, arrangement or understanding entered into,\nbefore the commencement of that Schedule in relation to:\n\n(a) conditions imposed, or provisions included, on or after that\ncommencement; and\n\n(b) conditions imposed, or provisions included, before that\ncommencement.\n\n(3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the amendment does not apply to\nthe extent (if any) to which its operation would result in an\nacquisition of property (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi)\nof the Constitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms\n(within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The amendment made by item 1 of Schedule 4 to the Treasury\nLaws Amendment (2018 Measures No. 5) Act 2019 applies in\nrelation to a licence granted, an assignment made, or a contract,\narrangement or understanding entered into, on or after the\ncommencement of that Schedule.\n\n(2) The amendment also applies to a licence granted, an assignment\nmade, or a contract, arrangement or understanding entered into,\nbefore the commencement of that Schedule in relation to:\n\n(a) conditions imposed, or provisions included, on or after that\ncommencement; and\n\n(b) conditions imposed, or provisions included, before that\ncommencement.\n\n(3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the amendment does not apply to\nthe extent (if any) to which its operation would result in an\nacquisition of property (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi)\nof the Constitution) from a person otherwise than on just terms\n(within the meaning of that paragraph).\n\nChapter 8  Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-186-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-186-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-186-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d60f60ce2bf1f4d037ad63e5667581251851b2131e1ffa9ecb46e49d42acc1e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-186",
