    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-191",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "191 Amendments of section 50",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-191"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.600",
      "values:originalText": "The amendments made by Division 1 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Mergers and Acquisitions Reform) Act\n2024 apply in relation to an acquisition that is put into effect on or\nafter 1 January 2026, other than an acquisition to which\nsubsection 189(2) of this Act applies.",
      "skos:definition": "The amendments made by Division 1 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Mergers and Acquisitions Reform) Act\n2024 apply in relation to an acquisition that is put into effect on or\nafter 1 January 2026, other than an acquisition to which\nsubsection 189(2) of this Act applies.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-191-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04b55abadd066a53fc96464998dfdb36772e57947e1d26180664180174591fa4",
      "skos:note": "Amendments apply to acquisitions put into effect after 1 January 2026, with an exception for certain acquisitions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-191",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "191 Amendments of section 50",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 600,
      "values:originalText": "The amendments made by Division 1 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Mergers and Acquisitions Reform) Act\n2024 apply in relation to an acquisition that is put into effect on or\nafter 1 January 2026, other than an acquisition to which\nsubsection 189(2) of this Act applies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-191-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-191"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-192",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "192 Acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-192"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.600",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The amendments made by Schedule 1 to the Treasury Laws\nAmendment (Mergers and Acquisitions Reform) Act 2024 do not\napply in relation to an acquisition if:\n\n(a) apart from this section, the operation of the amendments in\nrelation to the acquisition would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms; and\n\n(b) the acquisition of property would be invalid because of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\n\n(2) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nApplication and transitional provisions relating to the competition provisions  Part XIII\nApplication of amendments made by the Treasury Laws Amendment (Doubling\nPenalties for ACCC Enforcement) Act 2026  Division 7\n\nSection 193\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The amendments made by Schedule 1 to the Treasury Laws\nAmendment (Mergers and Acquisitions Reform) Act 2024 do not\napply in relation to an acquisition if:\n\n(a) apart from this section, the operation of the amendments in\nrelation to the acquisition would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms; and\n\n(b) the acquisition of property would be invalid because of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\n\n(2) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nApplication and transitional provisions relating to the competition provisions  Part XIII\nApplication of amendments made by the Treasury Laws Amendment (Doubling\nPenalties for ACCC Enforcement) Act 2026  Division 7\n\nSection 193\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-192-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-192-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1e8934fb92ac6ef7547380e980933ec5c16283b5409bd443d5038809db05422c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-act-2010#sec-192",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "192 Acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 600,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The amendments made by Schedule 1 to the Treasury Laws\nAmendment (Mergers and Acquisitions Reform) Act 2024 do not\napply in relation to an acquisition if:\n\n(a) apart from this section, the operation of the amendments in\nrelation to the acquisition would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms; and\n\n(b) the acquisition of property would be invalid because of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\n\n(2) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 8\nApplication and transitional provisions relating to the competition provisions  Part XIII\nApplication of amendments made by the Treasury Laws Amendment (Doubling\nPenalties for ACCC Enforcement) Act 2026  Division 7\n\nSection 193\n\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010\n\nCompilation date: 27/05/2026"
    },
